      "postEditingDetails": "After Effects 후보정",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "S-1 1차 생성 — 괘불탱과 만다라의 결합 \n\n참조 갑사 삼신불괘불탱 실사 사진 + 티베트 만다라 도판 (3장) \n\nA modern reinterpretation of a Korean Buddhist triad artwork (inspired by Gapsa Samsinbul \nGwaebultaeng) fused with a mandala structure. Three clearly distinct seated Buddha figures \nat the center, each individually designed: the center Buddha has a plain smooth topknot and \nhands folded in a wisdom-fist mudra at the chest; the left Buddha wears a tall dark ritual \ncrown, hands in a calm meditation mudra, golden-yellow robe with a red sash; the right \nBuddha wears an ornate jeweled bodhisattva-style crown, one hand raised in a teaching \ngesture, richly patterned crimson robe — each figure has a unique crown, hand gesture, and \nrobe pattern so they clearly read as three different deities, never repeated copies of one \nfigure. \nThe triad sits at the center of a strongly geometric mandala structure with multiple clearly \nvisible concentric rings — nested squares within circles, sharp radial symmetry, precise \nsacred-geometry linework — inspired by Korean dancheong five-direction colors (obangsaek) \nbut reinterpreted in a bold contemporary palette: saturated modern jewel tones, clean color- \nblocked sections, subtle gradient lighting instead of literal aged pigment texture. Palace \nwalls use dancheong-inspired geometric lattice patterns rendered in a flat modern graphic- \ndesign style. Four cardinal gates are stylized as minimalist Korean temple gate silhouettes \nwith kkotsalmun flower-lattice motifs — east in blue, south in red, west in white, north in \nblack — simplified into clean contemporary linework. Retinue figures behind the triad are \narranged in radiating concentric rings in a simplified modern illustrative style. Guardian \nfigures anchor the four corners. \nOverall aesthetic: contemporary digital art reinterpretation of traditional Korean Buddhist \niconography, vibrant modern color grading, crisp clean linework, strong mandala symmetry, no aged or antique texture, gallery-quality contemporary illustration. \n\nS-2 배경 재편집 — 만다라 원 바깥만 교체 \n\nThe circular mandala design elements are retained as they are. Edit the background design \noutside the mandala. \n\nS-3 나전칠기 전환 — 채색에서 자개로 \n\nRecreate this exact Korean Buddhist mandala artwork composition — the heavenly palace scene with musicians and Buddhas at the top, the central triad of Buddhas within the mandala rings, the four guardian kings on lotus pedestals at the corners, the dragons and lotus pond at the bottom, and the monks approaching at the bottom right — but reimagine the entire rendering surface in the shimmering iridescent texture of Korean mother-of-pearl lacquerware (najeonchilgi): a deep black lacquer ground with abalone-shell iridescence in shifting blue- green-violet-pink hues replacing every area that was previously flat color. In addition, replace the mandala's hard geometric linework and background patterning with flowing, abstract ink-wash and silk-thread brushstrokes — hundreds of fine flowing lines swirling like liquid silk or sumi-e ink strokes forming the concentric rings, gates, and cloud motifs instead of flat color-blocked geometry. Keep the three central Buddha figures, the four guardian kings, the dragons, and the monk procession clearly recognizable and in their \noriginal poses and positions, rendered with nacre inlay detailing on black lacquer. The overall palette shifts to deep lacquer black as the dominant ground, with nacre's shifting \nrainbow iridescence and flowing ink-black brushwork replacing the previous flat color- \nblocked geometric mandala rings. \n. \n\nS-4 다색 자개 — 단색조 보정 \nUsing the same composition, layout, figures and abstract flowing ink/silk-thread linework as \nthis reference image, dramatically increase the color diversity of the mother-of-pearl \n(najeonchilgi) iridescence across the entire piece. Instead of a limited blue-purple \nmonotone, render the nacre shimmer with the full rainbow spectrum simultaneously visible \nacross the surface — vivid turquoise, emerald green, magenta, violet, golden yellow, and \nwarm orange all shifting together within the abalone-shell inlay, exactly like real \ntraditional Korean mother-of-pearl lacquerware (najeonchilgi), where every inlaid line and \nshape glows with multiple shifting colors at once rather than a single hue. Keep the deep \nblack lacquer as the ground color, but make every inlaid figure, cloud, ring and gate glow \nwith this rich multicolor iridescent shimmer. The three central Buddha figures, four \nguardian kings, dragons and monk procession remain unchanged in pose, position, and identity — only the color richness and vibrancy of the nacre inlay increases. \n\nS-5 흐르는 실 선 강화 \n\nUsing this reference image's rich multicolor nacre iridescence and figures as the starting \npoint, reintroduce and strengthen a flowing, thread-like abstract quality in the mandala's \nring and gate structures. Instead of solid flat inlaid shapes, render the concentric rings, \ngates and cloud patterns as hundreds of fine, flowing curved lines — like liquid silk \nthreads or sumi-e ink brush strokes swirling and weaving around each other — with the vivid \nrainbow abalone-shell iridescence (turquoise, emerald, magenta, violet, gold, orange) \nshimmering along these flowing thread-like lines rather than filling flat solid color \nblocks. The linework should feel loose, gestural and fluid, as if painted with a wet brush \nor woven from glowing silk, while still tracing the mandala's overall geometric structure. \nKeep the deep black lacquer ground, the three central Buddha figures, four guardian kings, \ndragons and monk procession unchanged in pose and position. \n\nS-6 중앙 삼신불 실물 고증 \n\nUsing the overall composition and layout from the mandala reference (heavenly palace scene at top, central triad within mandala rings, four guardian kings on lotus pedestals at the corners, dragons and lotus pond at the bottom, monks approaching at bottom right, flowing silk-thread linework and multicolor nacre iridescence in the outer mandala rings and gates), now render the central triad group and its immediate retinue with much higher fidelity to the detailed reference photographs of the real Gapsa Samsinbul Gwaebultaeng painting: each of the three central Buddhas seated in front of a tall pointed-arch flame-shaped nimbus witha deep red scalloped border and an intricate green background filled with red-and-white floral scrollwork; the center Buddha's hands held together at the chest in a prayer mudra, the flanking Buddhas each with a distinct hand gesture as shown in the references; \nsurrounding bodhisattva attendants wearing ornate crowns with flame-tipped diadems, standing in front of smaller green nimbus circles, dressed in red and green robes with gold jewelry; above them, individualized portrait-like arhat and immortal faces among swirling white, pink and orange clouds, one figure seated on clouds holding a vase with a long red halo; below the triad, standing guardian attendants flanking a red architectural throne-like structure with gold latticework. This entire central triad-and-retinue group keeps its authentic warm palette of vivid red, deep green, ivory and gold exactly as in the reference photographs — untouched by the dark lacquer treatment — while everything surrounding it (the outer mandala rings, gates, palace scene, guardian kings, dragons) keeps the black lacquer najeonchilginacre iridescence and flowing silk-thread abstract linework established in the mandala reference. The result should read as an authentic, richly detailed red-and-green Buddhist triad glowing at the center of a dark, iridescent nacre mandala. \n\n\nS-7 중앙부 자개 통합 \n\nUsing this reference image exactly as the base — keep every figure, pose, flame-shaped \nnimbus, mudra, crown, facial detail, and the overall composition of the central triad and \nits retinue completely unchanged — now convert the central triad group and its retinue from their warm red-green-gold coloring into the same black lacquer najeonchilgi mother-of-pearl treatment used in the surrounding mandala. Render the flame nimbus borders, robes, crowns, and floral background patterns of the central figures in the same shimmering multicolor abalone-shell iridescence (turquoise, emerald, magenta, violet, gold, orange) over a deep black lacquer ground, and let the fine flowing silk-thread linework style extend into this central area as well, so the entire piece — center and mandala alike — reads as one unified najeonchilgi artwork. Do not simplify, remove, or alter any of the detailed iconography — only replace the color and material treatment with the nacre lacquer style. \n\n\nS-8 사방문 구조 복원 + 오방색 적용 \n\nUsing this reference image as the base — keep the central triad and retinue's iconography, \nposes, and the najeonchilgi mother-of-pearl material quality on deep black lacquer \ncompletely unchanged — make two changes to the surrounding mandala structure. First, replace the loose flowing silk-thread ink-wash linework in the outer rings with a clearly \nstructured, defined mandala architecture: nested concentric squares within circles, with \nfour distinct cardinal gates (T-shaped gate structures at north, south, east and west) \nrendered as crisp geometric palace-wall architecture, precise sacred-geometry linework, \nsharp radial symmetry — restoring a defined architectural mandala rather than an abstract \npainterly one. Second, keep the shimmering nacre abalone-shell iridescence as the material \nfinish throughout, but organize its coloring according to the Korean five-direction color \nscheme (obangsaek): the eastern gate and its palace wall section glowing in iridescent blue- \ntuquoise, the southern section in iridescent red-magenta, the western section in iridescent \nwhite-silver, the northern section in iridescent black-violet, and the central palace area \nin iridescent gold-yellow. Each directional color zone should still shimmer with the full \nrainbow nacre iridescence, but with its zone's assigned hue dominant, so the five colors \nread harmoniously across the mandala structure rather than randomly mixed. \n\nS-9 정렬 + 오방색 전면 확장 \nUsing this reference image as the base — keep the central triad iconography, the four-gate \nmandala architecture, and the najeonchilgi nacre material treatment — make two corrections. \nFirst, fix the alignment: perfectly center the entire mandala structure on the vertical and \nhorizontal axis, straighten the four cardinal gates so they sit exactly at true north, \nsouth, east and west with no tilt or skew, and align the outer circular ring, the square palace walls, and the central triad all on the same true center axis, symmetrical and level. \nSecond, extend the obangsaek five-direction color scheme comprehensively across the ENTIRE piece, not just the inner palace walls: the guardian king standing at each corner should glow in the iridescent nacre color matching that corner's direction (east corner guardians in blue-turquoise, south corner in red-magenta, west corner in white-silver, north corner in black-violet), the heavenly palace scene at the very top should carry gold-yellow as its dominant nacre tone to represent the center/zenith, and the dragons and lotus pond at the bottom should blend blue and black nacre tones for the northern water element. Every part of the composition should visibly belong to one of the five direction-color zones in shimmering nacre iridescence, unified and symmetrical. \n\n\nS-10 중심 정렬 \nRecreate this exact artwork — same figures, same najeonchilgi nacre style, same obangsaek \ncoloring, same iconography — but fix the composition so it is perfectly centered and \nbilaterally symmetric. The large central circular mandala containing the three seated \nBuddhas must be positioned exactly in the horizontal center of the image, with equal empty \nmargin on the left and right sides. The vertical centerline of the image must pass precisely \nthrough: the peak of the palace roof at top, the center gate, the head and folded praying \nhands of the central Buddha, the small central figure below the triad, and the base pedestal \nat the bottom — all stacked on one true vertical axis. The left half and right half must \nmirror each other: the corner guardian kings, trees, pagodas and clouds on the left must be \nat the same height and same distance from center as their counterparts on the right. \nEliminate any leftward or rightward shift of the central circle. Keep the deep black lacquer \nbackground and iridescent multicolor nacre finish identical to the reference. \n\nS-11 대칭 재생성 — 최종본 \nRecreate this exact artwork — same three central Buddhas, same najeonchilgi mother-of-pearl iridescent style on deep black lacquer, same obangsaek five-direction coloring, same four-gate mandala architecture, same guardian kings, dragons, heavenly palace and monk procession — but rebuild the composition with STRICT perfect bilateral symmetry. One single true vertical center axis runs down the exact middle of the image. Every structural element is centered on and mirrored across this axis: the heavenly palace roof peak at top, the gate directly below it, the outer circular mandala ring, the square palace-wall frame, the \ncentral Buddha's head and folded praying hands, the small shrine niche below the triad, and \nthe base pedestal at the bottom must ALL sit precisely on this one centerline, stacked \nvertically. The left half and right half mirror each other exactly — the corner guardian \nkings, pagodas, trees and clouds on the left are at the same height, size and distance from \ncenter as their counterparts on the right. The circular mandala is perfectly centered \nhorizontally with equal margin on both sides. No tilt, no skew, no leftward or rightward \ndrift of any element. Keep every figure, ornament and color identical to the reference; only \nenforce flawless left-right symmetry and centering. \n\n\nS-12 정렬 보정과 16:9 변환 — 최종본 \n\n도구 ChatGPT (무료 버전) · 16:9 · 3840×2160 px \n\nS-11 결과물을 업로드하고 아래 세 문장을 순서대로 입력했습니다. \n\n-지금 이미지 보면 정렬이 안맞는 곳이 있어 이미지 일그러짐 훼손없이 수정해봐 \n-이 느낌 그대로 유지한채 16:9 그림도 그릴수 있어? \n-디자인 그대로 유지. 가운데 눌린 느낌이라 비율에 맞게 수정 \n\n\nS-13 업스케일 — 해상도 보강 \n\n도구 Magnific Upscale \n\nS-12의 4K 파일은 생성 결과를 확대한 것이라 명목 해상도(3840px)에 비해 실제 묘사 밀도가 낮았습니다. 공모 규격이 대형 출력 전시를 전제로 4K급 이상 고해상도 원본을 요구하므로, 업스케일러로 7680×4320까지 확대해 묘사를 보강한 뒤 3840×2160으로 정리했습니다. \n\n이 단계는 그림을 바꾸는 작업이 아니라 해상도를 채우는 작업입니다. 확대 전후 구도 상관계수 0.98로 도상과 배치는 그대로 유지됩니다. \n\nS-14 최종 보정 — 광배 상단과 색감 \n\n도구 After Effects \n\n만다라 원형 좌우에 있는 지붕이 센터와 어긋나 해당 부분만 수정했습니다. 생성 도구로 고치면 주변까지 함께 바뀌므로 편집 도구에서 직접 손봤습니다. 이어 전체 색감을 한 차례 보정했습니다. \n\n더 정확한 내용은 생성과정 캡쳐본_F ZIP 파일 안에 갑사 만다라 프롬프트 증빙자료 제출본 PDF 파일을 첨부하였습니다",
