      "fullPrompt": "Contemporary reinterpretation of Gongsanseong Fortress and Baekje heritage in Gongju, Korea, vertical 9:16 fine-art poster. Clearly recognizable Gongsanseong stands above the elegant S-shaped Geumgang River, simplified into flowing bands of deep navy, cobalt blue, coral, peach and warm orange.\n\nFrom Gongsanseong rises one monumental vertical stream of Baekje cultural memory. Inside the stream, clearly recognizable artifacts inspired by the Tomb of King Muryeong flow upward: delicate gold crown ornaments, gold earrings, bronze mirrors, silver cup, ancient brick patterns and refined Baekje decorative forms. Near the fortress, several artifacts are large and clearly identifiable; as they rise, they gradually fragment into smaller motifs, lines and particles, finally dissolving into abstract vertical bands of light.\n\nRender the artifacts in the SAME sophisticated graphic language as the landscape, not photorealistic objects: Korean printmaking, silkscreen, refined linework, subtle grain, flat layered shapes. Strong navy background, coral and peach glow, restrained antique gold accents, dramatic negative space, elegant symmetry, museum exhibition poster, iconic contemporary Korean design, culturally meaningful, visually unforgettable, no text, no collage, no fantasy palace, no clutter --ar 16:9",
