      "postEditingUsage": "사용함",
      "postEditingDetails": "없음",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "Create a single cinematic, museum-quality digital heritage artwork about King Muryeong’s Tomb and Ungjin Baekje in Gongju, Korea, expressing how archaeological remains reconnect the present with a civilization from 1,500 years ago.\n\nUse a seamless vertical cross-section composition within one 16:9 image.\n\nLOWER HALF — THE TOMB\n\nDepict the interior of the Tomb of King Muryeong, a 6th-century Baekje brick chamber tomb in Gongju.\nThe chamber has a historically inspired tunnel-shaped barrel-vaulted ceiling constructed from reddish-brown fired bricks. Use alternating horizontal and vertical brick arrangements and authentic-looking Baekje lotus-pattern bricks, but keep the lotus motifs subtle, irregularly distributed and archaeologically believable rather than repetitive decoration.\n\nThe tomb should feel solemn, archaeological and ancient, not like a fantasy treasure chamber. Include only a restrained number of burial objects in shadow.\n\nCENTER — KING MURYEONG'S GOLD DIADEM ORNAMENTS\n\nAt the exact visual center, prominently display the pair of gold diadem ornaments excavated from King Muryeong’s Tomb.\n\nMake them closely inspired by the actual Baekje artifacts:\ntwo thin openwork gold-sheet ornaments approximately 30 cm tall, each slightly different rather than perfect mirror copies; complex asymmetrical scrolling vegetal patterns; branching palmette and lotus motifs; long flame-like projections rising along the outer edges; delicate flower forms; and numerous tiny circular gold spangles attached with fine twisted gold wire across the surfaces.\n\nThe ornaments are flat, extremely delicate pieces of pierced gold sheet, not wearable solid crowns standing upright by themselves, not phoenix-shaped, not bird-headed, not a Chinese imperial headdress, and not fantasy jewelry.\n\nDisplay them discreetly on nearly invisible museum-style supports so that the gold ornaments themselves dominate the composition.\n\nA small amount of warm golden light rises from the artifacts. This light symbolizes historical memory and digital reconstruction, not supernatural magic. Avoid excessive sparkles or fantasy effects.\n\nUPPER HALF — UNGJIN BAEKJE\n\nThe light gradually reconstructs a plausible scene of 6th-century Ungjin Baekje, present-day Gongju, above the tomb.\n\nShow the Geumgang River winding naturally through a mountainous landscape, modest Baekje wooden buildings with tiled and thatched roofs, workshops, markets, craftspeople, residents, simple river boats and a historically restrained fortress landscape.\n\nThe settlement should feel like a sophisticated but realistically sized capital of 6th-century Baekje, not a monumental fantasy metropolis.\n\nDo not show modern bridges, paved roads, concrete, electrical infrastructure or modern boats within the ancient landscape.\n\nAvoid Joseon royal-palace architecture, Japanese castle forms, Chinese imperial palace architecture and generic fantasy East Asian architecture.\n\nPRESENT DAY\n\nAt the far upper edges of the image, subtly frame the reconstructed ancient landscape with a contemporary Korean museum interior and a small number of modern visitors observing Baekje artifacts and digital heritage displays.\n\nThe ancient reconstruction should visually emerge between the archaeological tomb below and the museum of the present above, connecting all three periods without using a split screen.\n\nThe central conceptual message is:\n“From artifacts buried for 1,500 years, the forgotten world of Ungjin Baekje becomes visible again.”\n\nSophisticated cultural-heritage visualization, cinematic realism, archaeological credibility, restrained digital aesthetic, museum exhibition quality, realistic aged gold, brick, wood and earth textures, natural warm sunset lighting, highly detailed, emotionally powerful but quiet and dignified.\n\nNo text. No letters. No logo. No watermark. No modern infrastructure inside ancient Baekje. No fantasy crown. No phoenix or bird heads. No cyberpunk neon. No magical fantasy atmosphere.\n\n16:9 horizontal composition, 4K master quality, extremely high detail.",
