      "fullPrompt": "작품: 왕의 금빛, 아이의 첫 선\n생성 도구: OpenAI image_gen(Codex 내장)\n참고사진: 국립중앙박물관 사진 / 국립공주박물관 소장 무령왕 금제관식. Wikimedia Commons, 공공누리 제1유형.\n출처: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:무령왕_금제관식.jpg\n\n[실제로 사용한 생성 프롬프트 전문]\nUse case: stylized-concept. Create a new museum-quality narrative fine-art image, horizontal 16:9, request native 3840x2160 if supported. Title, NOT printed: \"The King's Gold, A Child's First Line\" / \"왕의 금빛, 아이의 첫 선\".\n\nREFERENCE: Image 1 is the actual pair of gold cap ornaments of King Muryeong, Baekje, from Gongju. Reproduce ONE, the LEFT ornament in that photograph, as the identifiable heritage anchor: thin gold sheet, asymmetric pierced foliage, slender flame-shaped tips, small round hanging spangles, plain narrow mounting tab. It is a roughly 30cm cap ornament, not a whole crown. Keep the real outline and internal branching closely; do not redesign the artifact.\n\nSTORY: In a quiet contemporary museum, a Korean child about nine years old sees the ornament and begins drawing it in a sketchbook. The subject is the tiny moment of inspiration: something once worn by a king becomes the beginning of a child's own creation. The child's gaze and pencil hand must communicate real concentration, curiosity and a slight delighted realization.\n\nCOMPOSITION: An elegant, intimate, asymmetric triangle. The actual gold ornament is clearly visible in a very simple unobtrusive glass case at the left middle distance, occupying about one third of the frame height. On the right foreground, a large sensitively rendered three-quarter profile of the child in a plain contemporary muted teal cardigan, head and shoulders, warm natural skin, no costume or crown. The child glances toward the real ornament while the hand holding a graphite pencil rests over an open cream paper sketchbook in the lower center. The pencil point visibly touches the beginning of a child's imperfect, tentative drawing of the ornament. Natural credible hands and correct pencil grip. Emphasize the gaze, the pencil tip, and the small starting line.\n\nONE POETIC TRANSFORMATION: Beginning visibly at that graphite line on the page, a single graceful drawn stem extends outside the page, becoming luminous antique-gold ink and fine cut-paper-like foliage based on the real ornament's branching. It flows across the lower left foreground in one broad, exquisite sweep and rises softly along the left margin. It is clearly the child's imagined drawing expanding, not gold leaking from the real artifact. Keep the first graphite marks visible so the visual cause is unmistakable. The expanded painting is flat, delicate and artistically authored, with gold-leaf edges, muted vermilion mineral washes and deep peacock-teal ink. No generic floral explosion or unrelated motifs. Leave the child's face and the physical artifact unobstructed. This is the only surreal element; the museum object remains intact inside its case.\n\nSTYLE: Contemporary Korean fine-art painting seamlessly joined with beautifully natural cinematic portraiture and sharply observed museum-object detail. Rich yet restrained antique gold, ink indigo, luminous warm paper, deep vermilion and peacock teal. Sculptural warm light on the child's cheek and pencil hand, a precise soft spotlight on the actual thin gold. Subtle painterly negative space, layered tactile ink and paper, crisp object edges, human emotion. The space beyond the protagonists dissolves gently into ink, without visible museum signage, generic corridor, velvet backdrop or decorative palace. Use ample readable midtones; never a gloomy black frame. The large imagined gold brushwork supplies visual splendor, while the child's small physical action supplies the story. Exceptional anatomical realism and nuanced expression, no oversized sparkling eyes.\n\nAvoid: text, captions, logos, watermarks, crowns worn by the child, royal clothing, other people, ghosts, extra hands, giant enlarged physical artifacts, historical reconstruction, palace architecture, glass glare hiding the subject, exhibition-poster layout, posed grin, cartoon rendering, glitter confetti, fantasy lightning, photomontage seams, a fully finished adult-perfect drawing in the child's sketchbook. Produce one finished artwork.\n\n[생성 결과와 제출 규격 변환]\n실제 생성 원본: 1672×941 PNG. 제출용 1920×1080 및 3840×2160 파일은 Pillow Lanczos로 크기를 변환한 확대본이며, 새로운 그림 내용은 추가하지 않았습니다. 3840×2160 파일은 네이티브 4K 생성 원본이 아닙니다.\n\n[과정 캡처 설명]\n별도로 만든 이번 작업의 프롬프트 입력·실제 결과 기록 페이지를 브라우저에서 캡처했습니다. 생성 전 해당 입력값을 기록한 뒤 그대로 image_gen에 전달했고 실제 결과를 기록 페이지에 연결했습니다. OpenAI 서비스 자체의 대화 UI 캡처가 아니며, 서비스 UI를 모방하지 않았습니다. 실제 생성 원본 PNG와 프롬프트 텍스트도 증빙 압축파일에 함께 첨부합니다.",
