      "fullPrompt": "A small stone guardian beast statue (Jinmyosu) from King Muryeong's tomb, Baekje-era Korea: stout chubby body like a wild boar, short stubby legs, wing-like carvings on both sides, a broken horn stub on its forehead, blunt snub nose, bulging round eyes, sitting on a low weathered stone pedestal. Camera at extreme low angle looking upward; the statue occupies only the lower portion of the frame, appearing small. Beside its base, a broken rusted iron chisel and an extinguished torch lie abandoned in the dirt, hinting at a failed tomb robbery attempt long ago. A warm beam of light shines diagonally from lower left, casting the statue's shadow dramatically upward across a curved, vaulted brick wall carved with delicate lotus-flower relief patterns (Baekje tomb architecture). The shadow is the exact same stout boar-like creature as the statue — same wings, same snub nose, same proportions — not a dragon, not an elongated serpentine creature, just enlarged and looming. Its pose is fierce and protective: jaws open as if roaring, wings spread wide, one clawed foot raised as if warding off an intruder. Unlike the statue's broken horn, the shadow's horn is whole and unbroken, restored. Glowing dust particles drift through the light beam. Deep indigo and warm amber color palette, cinematic dramatic lighting, hyperrealistic statue and prop textures contrasted with a bold graphic dominating shadow, ultra-detailed, 8K, 16:9 aspect ratio, mood: solemn, protective, overwhelming scale, awe",
