      "id": "sub-1790860421651-105",
      "submissionNumber": "DH-IMG-106",
      "title": "황금 능선에서 만난 두 사슴",
      "category": "IMAGE",
      "submitterName": "장진석",
      "participantCategory": "일반인",
      "submitterAffiliation": "회사원",
      "nationalHeritageName": "백제 금동대향로(국보)",
      "baekjeRelated": "사용함",
      "description": "이 작품은 백제 금동대향로에 조형된 작은 산악 세계를 오늘의 살아 있는 풍경으로 확장한 국가유산 재해석 이미지다. 유물을 거대한 장식물로 제시하기보다, 금속에 새겨진 사슴과 살아 있는 사슴이 서로를 바라보는 한순간에 집중했다. 서로 다른 시간과 재료가 만나는 장면을 통해, 유산이 과거에 머무는 대상이 아니라 오늘의 감각으로 다시 관계 맺을 수 있는 존재임을 전하고자 했다.\n산형 뚜껑과 연꽃 테두리, 봉황과 악사의 모티프를 출발점으로 삼고, 금동의 능선이 회색 암석과 이끼, 소나무로 이어지는 공간을 구성했다. 왼쪽의 금속 사슴과 오른쪽의 살아 있는 사슴은 한 개체의 변신이 아니라, 유산에 담긴 상상과 현재의 생명이 마주하는 두 존재다. 금속의 반사광과 털의 부드러운 질감, 조각된 산세와 자연 암벽의 대비가 그 차이를 드러낸다. 오른쪽 아래의 현대적 의복을 입은 아이는 오늘의 관객이자 다음 세대를 상징하며, 두 사슴을 바라보는 시선을 통해 관객을 장면 안으로 이끈다.\n제작 과정에서는 생성형 AI로 미시적인 공예 세계와 거대한 산수의 규모를 결합하고, 반복적인 생성과 수정으로 전체 향로 중심의 구도에서 조우 장면 중심의 근접 구도로 발전시켰다. 이후 AI 업스케일과 독립 보정 레이어를 활용해 고해상도 출력, 중앙 명암과 주변 밝기, 금속·암석의 재질 대비를 정돈했다. 기술은 화려함을 더하기 위한 장치가 아니라 유산의 작은 세계를 관객이 경험할 수 있는 공간으로 확장하는 표현 수단으로 활용했다.\n작품 속 악기·복식·봉황의 세부 형태와 산수는 실물이나 특정 장소의 고증 복원도가 아닌 창작적 재해석이다. 유산을 보존한다는 것은 형상을 남기는 데서 나아가, 그 안에 담긴 상상력과 관계를 다음 세대가 다시 발견하도록 하는 일이라는 메시지를 담았다.",
      "aiTools": [
        "ChatGPT와 Higgifieid로 이미지 생성"
      ],
      "postEditingUsage": "사용함",
      "postEditingDetails": "없음",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "작품명: 황금 능선에서 만난 두 사슴\n\n아래는 최종 작품으로 이어진 이미지 생성·수정 및 업스케일 과정에서 실제로 요청한 프롬프트 원문이다. 단계 제목과 참조 이미지 설명은 제작 기록을 구분하기 위해 덧붙였다.\n\n제작 경로: 기본 이미지 생성(P04) → 근접 구도 재구성(P05) → 두 사슴의 조우와 현대의 아이 강조(P07) → 최종 생성 원본의 재질·시선 보완(P08) → AI 업스케일(U01)\n\n프롬프트의 고증·품질 관련 표현은 제작 목표이며, 실제 결과의 고증 정확성이나 공식 심사점수의 검증을 뜻하지 않는다.\n\n\n[1. 기본 이미지 생성 — ChatGPT 이미지 생성 / 기록 P04]\n참조 이미지 없이 텍스트로 생성.\n\nCreate a completely new replacement image from scratch for a Korean national-heritage reinterpretation artwork. Make one original, museum-grade fine-art image in a horizontal 16:9 composition, no text, no logo, no border. The subject is the Baekje Gilt-Bronze Incense Burner, reinterpreted with high cultural recognizability and clear narrative logic.\n\nPrimary goal: fix the specific weaknesses of the previous attempts. The image must not read as a generic fantasy landscape with a burner placed in front. Instead, it must clearly show that the world contained in the incense burner is awakening into a living Korean mountain landscape. The transformation must be unmistakable, structurally readable, and emotionally powerful.\n\nComposition: show the full incense burner large in the foreground, slightly left of center, fully visible from dragon base to phoenix. The child witness is small and quiet in the lower right foreground, but positioned so their gaze clearly leads toward the transformation zone, not just toward the sunrise. Keep the environment elegant and restrained rather than overly spectacular.\n\nHeritage fidelity: the burner must be recognizably based on the real Baekje Gilt-Bronze Incense Burner. Show these essential features clearly: a dragon pedestal with lifted head and open mouth supporting the lotus-bud-like bowl and lid; a rounded bowl with distinct lotus-petal structure; a mountain-shaped lid made of many peaks; an elegant East Asian phoenix on top. Just below the phoenix, clearly show five musicians in varied poses, each playing a different instrument. Also include a few other varied human figures and animals on the mountain lid, but do not make them all look like identical seated statues. Preserve openwork and negative-space feeling in the dragon base so it does not look like a solid fantasy trophy.\n\nTransformation logic: this is the most important part. On the right side of the lid, choose one dominant ridge and make it visually continuous as the exact same form transforms from gilded bronze into weathered stone, then moss, then pine-covered living mountain. The viewer must be able to trace the same ridge silhouette across the transition. One sculpted bronze deer on this ridge must seamlessly become one living deer in the same pose on the adjacent real mountain edge. Smoke rising from the burner must evolve into mountain mist and low clouds that wrap through the living landscape. The transformation should happen near the center of the composition, large and readable, not hidden deep in the background.\n\nEnvironment: create a refined Korean mountain landscape with granite peaks, pine trees, layered mist, and a quiet water edge or reflective inlet, but keep the scenery secondary to the burner and transformation ridge. Use only a few restrained distant waterfalls if needed. Avoid excessive spectacle, avoid too many birds, avoid random pagodas, avoid cityscapes, avoid giant moons, avoid western fantasy motifs.\n\nLighting and gaze control: use subtle dawn light with warm gold highlights and cool blue-gray mist, but do not let the far-right sunrise overpower the image. The brightest visual emphasis should stay on the burner and the transformation ridge. Use reflected light and composition so the eye moves from the dragon base and lotus bowl up to the lid, across the transforming ridge, and then toward the small child witness.\n\nMood: awe, reverence, continuity, quiet wonder, inheritance of heritage into the future.\n\nStyle: highly detailed fine-art realism with poetic atmosphere, visually refined and award-caliber, but not gaudy or overdecorated.\n\n\n[2. 근접 구도 재구성 — ChatGPT 이미지 생성 / 기록 P05]\nImage A: 1단계(P04)에서 생성한 이미지.\n\nCreate a completely new final artwork for a Korean cultural-heritage image competition. Image A is a prior concept reference for subject and overall poetic tone only; do NOT copy its composition. Replace the previous wide scenic layout with a new composition whose main subject is the transformation itself.\n\nSubject and concept:\nDepict the Baekje Gilt-Bronze Great Incense Burner in a culturally recognizable way, but as a fine-art reinterpretation rather than an archaeological illustration. The key idea is that the miniature sacred mountain world on the burner is visibly awakening into a real living mountain landscape. This must read as clear transformation, not simple side-by-side placement.\n\nComposition:\nUse a 16:9 horizontal composition, but crop much tighter than before. The viewer should feel close to the artifact. Place the burner large in the left half, with the right side of the mountain-shaped lid occupying the center of the image. Make the single most important focal area the transition ridge on the right side of the lid. Show only enough surrounding environment to support the story. Do not make the distant sunrise or far landscape the main attraction.\n\nHeritage fidelity:\nMake the incense burner clearly recognizable by its essential structure: a dragon pedestal with the lotus-bud vessel clearly supported at the dragon’s raised mouth, an elegant rounded lotus-petal bowl, a mountain-shaped lid, and a phoenix at the summit. The support contact between dragon mouth and vessel must be visually clear and structurally convincing. The phoenix should feel East Asian and elegant, not like a western eagle. Near the upper mountain zone, include several small but legible musicians in varied poses and with distinct instruments, inspired by the famous five musicians. Avoid repetitive identical seated figures.\n\nTransformation zone — highest priority:\nShow one specific bronze ridge on the right side of the lid continuing seamlessly into a real cliff. The same silhouette must remain traceable as it changes in material step by step: gilded bronze surface -> weathered bronze/stone transition -> raw rock -> moss -> rooted pine trees. Do not obscure this key transition with too much smoke. Let the change be visible and readable. Include one sculpted deer on the lid and, immediately beside it, a living deer emerging from the same contour logic so the relationship is unmistakable. Incense smoke should gently flow outward and become thin mountain mist, but it must support rather than hide the transition.\n\nNarrative and mood:\nInclude a small present-day child witness only as a subtle secondary element, placed low on the right or lower foreground, quietly observing the awakening world. The child should support the sense of inheritance, but must not dominate the frame. The emotional tone should be reverent, contemplative, and quietly awe-inspiring.\n\nEnvironment and lighting:\nUse refined early dawn light or soft morning light. Keep the lighting elegant and controlled. Reduce spectacle: fewer flashy waterfalls, fewer decorative extras, less emphasis on a huge glowing sun. The background should be a restrained Korean mountain atmosphere with mist, layered granite peaks, and pine trees, but the core emphasis remains on the burner and the transformation ridge.\n\nStyle:\nMuseum-quality fine-art realism, highly detailed, graceful, sophisticated, culturally respectful, cinematic but restrained. No text, no logo, no border, no caption.\n\n\n[3. 두 사슴의 조우·현대의 아이 강조 — ChatGPT 이미지 생성 / 기록 P07]\nImage A: 2단계(P05)에서 생성한 근접 구도 이미지.\n\nEdit Image A to implement the score-maximizing decision: do not show the full incense burner. Instead, make the final artwork focus on one decisive scene where the miniature world of the Baekje Gilt-Bronze Incense Burner awakens into a living landscape. Image A is the anchor for mood, close framing, and the overall concept. Preserve the poetic golden-dawn atmosphere, Korean granite peaks, pine trees, mist, and the elegant bronze mountain-lid world, but change the composition so the transformation itself becomes the unquestioned main subject.\n\nRequired composition changes:\n- Crop tighter and compose as a close, museum-quality fine-art scene. Show only the upper lotus-petal bowl rim and the mountain-shaped lid; do not show the dragon base at all.\n- Make the transformation ridge dominate the center of the image. The viewer must immediately read one continuous ridge line that begins as gilded bronze on the lid and then changes into real weathered granite with moss and rooted pine trees.\n- Do not let smoke obscure the crucial boundary. Reduce the smoke crossing the transformation zone so the material change is clearly visible.\n- Make the sequence visually readable: gilded bronze surface -> partly dulled metallic stone-like surface -> natural granite -> moss -> living pine-covered cliff.\n- Keep one bronze deer exactly on the lid-side of the transformation ridge and one living deer a few steps beyond on the natural side, clearly corresponding to each other. Their relationship should read as the artifact world awakening into life, not as random separate deer.\n- Keep several small musician figures on the bronze mountain lid, but make them clearly varied and readable: at least a flute player, a lute-like player, and a percussion player. Avoid repetitive identical seated figures.\n- Keep the phoenix at the summit elegant and East Asian in silhouette.\n- Keep the child witness small at lower right, but make the child read as a contemporary next-generation viewer in simple modern neutral clothing, quietly seated and looking directly toward the transformation ridge. The child should support the meaning, not dominate the image.\n- Reduce the dominance of the far-right sunrise. The brightest visual emphasis should stay on the transformation ridge, not on the distant sun.\n\nConcept and tone:\nThis is not a generic fantasy landscape and not a full-object product shot. It is a refined contemporary reinterpretation of Korean heritage. The image should communicate, without text, that the world imagined within the Baekje incense burner is coming alive for the next generation. The result should feel more conceptually focused, more readable, and more score-worthy for creativity, heritage value, and technical clarity.\n\nStyle:\nultra-detailed fine-art realism, elegant, restrained, cinematic but not overblown, museum-grade, no text, no border, no logo.\n\n\n[4. 최종 생성 원본의 재질·시선 보완 — ChatGPT 이미지 생성 / 기록 P08]\nImage A: 3단계(P07)에서 생성한 이미지.\n\nEdit Image A to create a more final, higher-scoring version while preserving its successful close-up composition and overall poetic mood. Image A is the direct edit target. Preserve the tight 16:9 close view of the upper Baekje gilt-bronze incense burner mountain world on the left, the living granite ridge on the right, the two deer meeting near the center-right, and the seated modern child witness in the lower-right. Do NOT zoom back out to show the full vessel or dragon base; keep the composition focused on the upper burner world and the encounter ridge.\n\nMain goals for the edit:\n1) Make the central theme unmistakable: the heritage world and the living world are meeting. The most important focal point must be the encounter between the bronze deer and the living deer, with the ridge itself clearly showing a material transition.\n2) Strengthen the continuous ridge transition from left to right: the same ridge silhouette should visibly change from polished gilded bronze and sculpted bronze texture, into weathered bronze, then into natural gray granite, then into moss and rooted pine. This material shift must be clear and readable, not hidden by mist.\n3) Keep the two-deer concept, but refine it: the left deer must read clearly as a bronze sculpted deer integrated into the burner’s mountain world, with metallic sheen and sculptural edges; the right deer must read clearly as a living deer with natural fur, soft anatomical realism, and warm sunlight. Their meeting should feel emotionally powerful and almost nose-to-nose.\n4) Preserve and refine heritage cues: keep the East Asian bronze phoenix at the summit, the sculpted musician figures, the bronze mountain world, and the visible lotus-petal rim of the burner. The musicians should look distinct and active, with varied postures and instruments, rather than repetitive statues.\n5) Reduce visual competition: slightly tone down the brightness and dominance of the phoenix and the leftmost gold highlights so they support the image instead of stealing focus from the deer encounter. Keep them elegant and detailed, but let the meeting of the two deer and the transforming ridge be the emotional and visual center.\n6) Keep the child as a next-generation witness: a small East Asian child in simple modern neutral clothing, seated quietly on the lower-right, gazing toward the deer encounter. The child should remain understated and contemplative.\n7) Keep the atmosphere refined and museum-grade: warm dawn light, misty Korean mountain peaks in the distance, crisp textures, poetic realism, calm emotional tone, no text, no logos.\n\nOverall intent: this should feel like a polished final artwork for a Korean heritage reinterpretation contest, with stronger clarity, stronger narrative focus, and clearer distinction between preserved heritage imagery and living-world reinterpretation.\n\n\n[5. 고해상도 확대 요청 — Higgsfield Bytedance Image Upscale / 기록 U01]\n입력 이미지: 4단계(P08)의 생성 결과.\n확인된 설정: resolution=4k, remove_bg=false.\n\n\nUpscale the provided finished artwork to 4K while preserving its exact composition, two deer and their anatomy, bronze musicians, phoenix, lotus rim, modern seated child, material transition, lighting and colors. Improve fine-detail rendering without adding or removing objects, changing silhouettes, inventing inscriptions, or removing