      "fullPrompt": "A sophisticated contemporary Korean luxury jewelry editorial portrait of an elegant Korean woman wearing an exquisite haute joaillerie hair ornament inspired by an ancient Baekje golden crown ornament.\n\nThe woman has sleek, smooth black hair with a precise center part, gathered into a refined low bun at the back of her head. She is photographed in a three-quarter back view, with her body turned slightly away from the camera and her face naturally turned back toward the viewer. Her expression is calm, composed, subtle and confident. Natural luminous skin, refined minimal makeup, clean brows, understated lips, elegant and sophisticated facial styling.\n\nShe wears a minimalist black sleeveless evening dress with a sculptural, clean silhouette and an elegant open back. The matte black fabric creates a strong but restrained contrast against the warm gold jewelry and luminous skin.\n\nThe main focal point is a contemporary haute joaillerie hair ornament positioned naturally around the side and upper area of the low bun.\n\nThe jewelry is a sophisticated modern reinterpretation of an ancient Baekje golden crown ornament. Preserve the distinctive visual language of the original artifact: vertical flame-like pointed forms, elegant branching structures, intricate openwork, delicate curling filigree, floral and leaf motifs, layered sculptural construction, refined symmetry and distinctive negative spaces.\n\nDo not reproduce the artifact literally. Transform its historical visual language into a modern collectible luxury jewelry piece with a refined architectural silhouette, sophisticated proportions and exceptional craftsmanship. The result should feel like an original contemporary jewelry design inspired by Baekje heritage.\n\nThe hair ornament is made of highly polished 18k yellow gold, combining extremely fine handcrafted filigree with precise sculptural metalwork. Subtle pavé diamonds and a limited number of small transparent gemstones are integrated naturally into the gold structure. Include a few elegant pear-shaped gemstone elements within the composition, used sparingly. The gold structure and intricate negative spaces remain the dominant visual feature rather than the gemstones.\n\nThe jewelry should appear physically integrated into the hairstyle, naturally resting against the low bun with realistic scale, depth, weight and contact with the hair. The entire ornament is visible and clearly readable, with no part of the jewelry cropped or hidden.\n\nThe overall aesthetic is contemporary Korean luxury, restrained haute joaillerie, sophisticated, architectural, elegant and timeless. It should resemble a prestigious luxury jewelry campaign rather than historical costume, traditional ceremonial styling or an archaeological reconstruction.\n\n### Atmosphere and mood\n\nQuiet, refined, luxurious and slightly mysterious atmosphere. Minimalist high-fashion editorial mood. Sophisticated Korean beauty aesthetic with an understated sense of heritage. The image should feel expensive and exclusive without being excessive or flashy.\n\nThe mood is calm and intimate rather than dramatic. The composition has generous negative space and a clean ivory background, allowing the silhouette of the woman and the gold jewelry to stand out clearly.\n\n### Lighting\n\nSoft diffused studio lighting with a large softbox positioned approximately 45 degrees to the front-left of the subject and slightly above eye level.\n\nA broad, feathered key light creates a soft gradient across the face, neck, shoulder and gold jewelry rather than hard shadows.\n\nUse a subtle warm directional rim light from the upper back-right side of the subject to gently separate the dark hair and black dress from the background and create delicate golden highlights along the edges of the jewelry.\n\nVery soft frontal fill light, approximately 1:3 contrast ratio, maintaining dimensionality without creating harsh facial shadows.\n\nThe gold jewelry catches narrow, controlled specular highlights from the large softbox, revealing the fine filigree and sculptural surface without producing excessive sparkle.\n\nSoft reflected light from the warm ivory environment creates delicate secondary highlights on the gold.\n\nNo harsh direct flash. No dramatic spotlight. No strong overhead light. No high-contrast cinematic lighting.\n\nThe background is a pale warm ivory / very light beige studio backdrop with a subtle tonal gradient, slightly brighter behind the subject and gently falling into a softer tone toward the edges.\n\nA very subtle soft shadow appears behind and below the subject, creating depth while maintaining an almost weightless luxury editorial feeling.\n\nNatural skin highlights, controlled exposure, soft highlight roll-off, realistic gold reflections, delicate gemstone refraction and physically accurate material response.\n\n### Photography\n\nHigh-end Korean luxury jewelry campaign photography.\n\nFull upper-body portrait with the complete head, hairstyle and entire jewelry piece visible.\n\nVertical editorial composition, approximately 4:5 portrait ratio.\n\nCamera positioned slightly below or approximately at shoulder-to-eye level, using an 85mm to 105mm portrait lens aesthetic.\n\nModerate shallow depth of field, keeping the woman's face and jewelry extremely sharp while allowing the distant background to fall into a very soft blur.\n\nExtremely realistic skin texture, individual hair strands, physically accurate gold reflections, realistic gemstone transparency and refraction.\n\nClean professional retouching while preserving natural skin texture.\n\nPremium fashion magazine photography, contemporary haute joaillerie campaign, museum-quality jewelry craftsmanship, photorealistic, elegant, restrained, sophisticated, timeless.",
