      "fullPrompt": "Monumental surreal media-art key visual, clean high-end Cinema 4D + Octane render, 16:9. Extreme low camera at ground level at the foot of a burial mound, 16mm ultra-wide lens looking sharply upward: the mound curve and a low cloud bank fill the bottom edge, two huge floating stone tablets loom above a tiny couple, ridges and statues rise in tall converging perspective. Strong foreshortening, dramatic near/middle/far scale contrast, dynamic and energetic.\n\nLIGHT AND COLOR: bright airy high-key dawn light, lifted shadows, nothing black. Palette about 60% warm cream/apricot/peach, 25% jade-teal and soft lilac, 15% accents of vermilion, saffron, gold, plum. Sky pale aqua at the top through lilac-pink to apricot-gold at the horizon. Three-point lighting on the tablets: strong warm key from upper-left front, soft cool aqua-lilac fill from right front, thin gold rim on the tablets' edges and the couple's shoulders. The backdrop behind the tablets is light apricot-peach at about 70% brightness, never white, never teal. Saturated accents stay off the tablet faces. Focal order: tablets, couple, main cloth, artifacts, statues, and last the tiny distant tomb entrance.\n\nRENDER: polished, smooth, crisp edges, no dirt, no noise or grain. Statues, ridges, mound and clouds are smooth satin surfaces with subtle detail. Fine detail is reserved for the tablets, artifacts, the couple's clothing and the animal heads.\n\nVFX PASSES in order: 1 Base render (PBR, soft global illumination, ambient occlusion). 2 Subsurface scattering on cloud edges and the translucent silk. 3 Volumetric light: faint champagne-gold light shafts from the horizon glow behind the far crest, never lighting a statue head or a tablet face. 4 Depth of field: tablets and all artifacts razor sharp, none blurred, far range softened by distance. 5 Emissive glow: only inside the tiny tomb entrance and on gold highlights, no halos, no red or orange emission. 6 Particles: about 40 tiny crisp gold light motes along the cloth path and rising with the artifacts, none on tablet faces. 7 Lens: chromatic aberration zero in the central 60% and rising toward the edges (thin red-cyan fringe, faint violet on corner highlights), mild barrel distortion, slight corner softness. 8 Grade: filmic S-curve, warm apricot highlights, teal-lilac shadows. 9 Finish: very light vignette, clean sharpening, zero noise.\n\nTABLETS (main subject, center): two separate thick stone slabs float apart with a clear vertical gap about one third of a slab's width; no hinge, frame or joint, never touching. Through the gap only a tiny, far-off glint of the tomb entrance shows. Left slab nearer, lower, larger; right slab farther, higher; both tilted about 25 degrees with top edges leaning to the upper right, three-quarter view from below, each about 65% of frame height, together about half the frame width, 1.15 times wider than tall, visible thickness. The faces reproduce the attached references exactly, as if each photo were mapped onto the slab. Left = Reference 1: blue-green verdigris, pitted surface, pale tan spots, six columns of bold incised characters with thin ruled lines, one tiny mark at the upper left, one small round hole above center. Right = Reference 2: warm gray-brown with a bluish tint, round tan blotches, a broad orange-rust stain down the left edge, only four tight columns of characters on the right edge, left two thirds blank with faint ruled lines, one small hole below center. Keep every character exactly as in the references: do not redraw, add, remove or invent characters. Omit photo watermarks and captions. No other text anywhere.\n\nMAIN CLOTH, the single leading line and the spatial backbone: exactly one long, wide, continuous piece of fine translucent silk, coral-vermilion with a saffron glow where the light passes through it, a thin gold-thread selvedge along both long edges, shaped by only a few large, clean, sculpted folds (each fold one smooth defined curve; no small wrinkles, no crumpling, no fraying). No other cloth, scroll, ribbon or banner anywhere, and no roll, rod, knot, tassel or bundle. Carried by an unseen wind, it builds depth by changing scale dramatically in strong perspective. It enters from the lower-left corner as a huge near-camera sweep about a quarter of the frame width, running off-frame; arcs up the left side outside the left slab; crosses just above the slabs' top edges in front of the statues' torsos, never higher than their shoulders, semi-translucent so the statues stay faintly visible through it; descends the right side outside the right slab; and ends in the right middle range with a clean straight hemmed end, fully visible, angled toward the center, no taper to a thread, width at least 4% of frame width. One unbroken piece, never torn, cut, split or knotted; it passes only in front of other objects or through open space, never behind, through or draped over any object, and is never overlapped by any object. Its silhouette stays bold and readable against the sky and ridges. It never covers the tablet faces, the gap, the tomb entrance, any statue head or the couple.\n\nCOUPLE: on the summit of a smooth round grass mound (short clean olive turf, no trees or stones) a king and a queen stand side by side seen from behind, faces hidden, holding hands, heads raised toward the tablets, tiny. King on the left: wide-sleeved layered deep-indigo robe with dark crimson trim, small black cap with a slender flame-shaped openwork gold ornament. Queen on the right: wide-sleeved muted-plum short jacket over a long pleated skirt, slender gold openwork floral hair ornament.\n\nARTIFACTS: excavated royal treasures levitate in one loose ascending spiral from the couple's joined hands, deliberately uneven and staggered (irregular spacing, big and small, near and far, high and low, alternating left and right, never in a row, never symmetrical). Exactly seven artifacts, each once, never merged or hybridized. Each is a faithful, undistorted copy of its reference photo: same shape, proportions, silhouette, material, color and pattern, with no redesign, simplification, smoothing or added ornament. Cut each from its photo and ignore backgrounds, pedestals, shadows, labels. All sharply focused, all levitating with empty space around, no contact shadow, none overlapping the tablets, cloth, gap, couple or statue heads. (1) Pair of gold diadem ornaments, upper-left zone, large, about 15% of frame height, tilted 20 degrees: tall flame-shaped openwork gold sheet with scrolling vines, small five-petal flowers, long pointed blades curving upward, folded base tab, two trailing flower-tipped stems. (2) Stone guardian beast, left edge at mid-height, about 13%: squat four-legged gray-green stone beast, faint pink-orange paint, round eye, wide flat muzzle, curled ear, ridged arched mane, swirling relief on the flank, thick short legs, one dark rust-iron horn. (3) Pair of gold earrings, low left above the mound slope, about 6%: gold ring, openwork cylinder, large heart-shaped plate with a pointed tip, chain of tiny gold leaf bells ending in a green jade comma bead. (4) Silver lidded cup on a dish, lower right below the cloth's descent, about 14%: domed silver lid, lotus-bud finial, ring of small gold petals, engraved cloud-and-wave bowl, short pedestal in a wide flat dish with green copper patina and reddish corrosion. (5) Wooden headrest, upper-right zone, about 14%, tilted 15 degrees: red-lacquer trapezoid block with a deep U-shaped raw-wood cutout, gold-line hexagonal turtle-shell pattern with small motifs, two dark carved bird-headed finials with gold accents. (6) Bronze mirror, right edge at mid-height, about 7%, face tilted 30 degrees toward the camera: dark-green bronze disc, central knob, square inner field with four raised beasts and small bosses, concentric bands with a serrated triangle band, plain rim. (7) Stack of relief bricks, low right above the mound slope, about 7%: gray-black bricks, five standing on edge with flower-rosette and X-frame reliefs, four flat bricks below with diagonal lattice between rosettes, the bottom one light tan, slightly warped and cracked. Also about five small plain bronze coins with square holes (no inscriptions), about 2% each, rise unevenly between the couple and the artifacts without touching anything.\n\nCLOUDS (afterlife layer): sculpted auspicious-cloud forms, smooth rounded volutes with spiral curls, never fog or realistic cumulus; peach-coral lit sides, lilac shadows, aqua undersides, thin gold rim; some volutes open like layered lotus petals. A low bank wraps the mound base at the couple's feet and fills the bottom edge (the threshold between worlds); a continuous bank runs under the twelve statues' feet; about five small-to-medium clouds drift in the middle range, sharp, never overlapping an artifact or the cloth. Keep the gap, tablet faces, couple and tomb entrance clear.\n\nFAR RANGE: about five broad, smooth, flowing dune-like ridge layers with rounded crests, never jagged. Colors by layer: the nearest two at the sides deep jade-teal, then warm olive-gold, terracotta-rose, lilac-mauve, farthest pale peach-cream; thin clean gold contour line on each ridge edge; thin mist bands only. Layers converge toward the center. A smooth pale-cream crescent crest curves toward the viewer; on it twelve colossal statues stand shoulder to shoulder in one wide arc with a narrow gap at the exact center, all feet at the same height, spanning about 85% of the frame width, seen from below, each about 42% of frame height with heads within 6% of the top edge. The tablets reach only chest level so all twelve heads and shoulders stay visible. Each has a human body and the full realistic head of one real animal (not a mask, no human eyes, nose or mouth), oversized (about one fifth of statue height), three-quarter view, heads turned slightly outward so silhouettes never overlap, natural muted species colors with fur, scale and feather detail. Left to right: rat (gray-brown, large round ears, pointed snout, whiskers, incisors); ox (brown, broad wet muzzle, two thick horns curving up); tiger (orange, bold black stripes, rounded ears, fangs); rabbit (white, two very tall ears, pink nose); dragon (jade scales, branching antlers, whiskers, beard, mane); snake (green-gold scales, no ears, wide cobra hood, forked tongue); horse (chestnut, very long face, flared nostrils, mane); goat (cream, long back-swept horns, beard, rectangular pupils); monkey (brown fur, bare pink face, brow ridge, flat nose); rooster (red comb, wattles, yellow beak, orange-gold neck feathers, no ears); dog (tan, long black-nosed muzzle, floppy ears hanging along the cheeks, never a disc snout); pig (pink-gray, flat disc snout with two nostrils, folded triangular ears, small tusks). Statues wear long belted wide-sleeved robes and trousers and hold staffs, spears or swords low so they never cross a head, in smooth pale gray-sepia satin stone like ancient carved reliefs, sashes alternating jade, vermilion, saffron, indigo; the end statues slightly larger.\n\nTOMB ENTRANCE: the smallest and farthest element of the whole image, placed far beyond the statues on the farthest pale ridge, in the center gap between statues six and seven at the vanishing point, visible through the gap between the tablets: a tiny semicircular arch of gray lotus-relief bricks only about 3% of frame height, softly hazed by distance, with a small soft champagne-gold light inside shaped like a single lotus bud, faint jade-aqua rim; not red, not orange, no fire, no embers, no smoke, not a furnace. It is a quiet distant point of light that never competes with the tablets and lights nothing around it. A few tiny birds in the sky.\n\nFINISH: wide but controlled palette; the tablets keep their own verdigris blue-green and warm gray-brown and stay the highest-contrast objects; artifacts keep their photo colors; the king's indigo and the queen's plum as secondary notes. Clean, polished, uncluttered CGI, 4K.\n네거티브\nextra or altered or invented characters, redrawn calligraphy, text on anything but the two tablets, watermark, logo, caption, hangul, latin letters, visible faces on the couple, human faces on statues, humanoid animal heads, animal masks, identical or duplicate or missing animal heads, pig-like dog, Joseon hanbok, gat hat, Western crown, Silla-style crown, palace building, pagoda roof, pointed Gothic arch, modern objects, pedestal, museum case, more than seven artifacts, merged or fused or hybrid or duplicated artifacts, redesigned, simplified, smoothed, warped, melted or blurred artifacts, bokeh on artifacts, artifacts resting on ground, artifacts in a straight row, evenly spaced or symmetrical artifact layout, hinge, hinged tablets, open book, tablets touching, more than two tablets, parchment scroll, paper strip, rolled fabric, fabric bolt, rod, knot, tassel, torn or cut or split cloth, frayed edges, tiny wrinkles, crumpled cloth, cloth hidden behind objects, cloth draped over objects, multiple cloths, narrow ribbon, banner, flag, oversized tomb entrance, large glowing tomb entrance, bright entrance dominating the center, ink wash painting, flat painting look, heavy color fringing across the center, overexposed, blown-out center, white glow behind subjects, bloom halo, lens flare, red glow, orange glow, fire, flames, embers, furnace, crematorium, smoke, heavy fog, uniform haze, realistic cumulus clouds, clouds covering tablets or gap, sea waves, ocean-like ripples, jagged rocky mountains, eye-level shot, high angle, aerial view, incense burner, censer, phoenix finial, dark, underexposed, muddy colors, garish neon, crushed blacks, heavy vignette, noise, grain, dust, dirt, grime, cluttered details",
      "processCaptureDriveUrl": "https://drive.google.com/open?id=1U7oJFQDOIrBWHTGxuKijLKUyQS0-Eg4p, https://drive.google.com/open?id=1rvNyZagB1GvsMWpDo5UFCz0CU9AnECkb, https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Y2v74BI_20CiYRZihJ_0HYUK8O5J6DJL",
      "driveLink": "https://drive.google.com/open?id=11pvj6ZqUOTV81Z2tNcTYCKucB_mwfceF, https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Q5TTjTQLBlaPtrTCmkGt8oM0Qmat0eMH",
