    {
      "id": "sub-1790860421651-118",
      "submissionNumber": "DH-IMG-119",
      "title": "돌아왔지만, 앉을 자리가 없다",
      "category": "IMAGE",
      "submitterName": "이웅기",
      "participantCategory": "일반인",
      "submitterAffiliation": "서울예술대학교 사진과",
      "nationalHeritageName": "두루미(천연기념물)",
      "baekjeRelated": "사용함",
      "description": "두루미 한 마리가 긴 비행 끝에 돌아와 작은 습지에 내려앉으려 한다. 땅은 넓게 펼쳐져 있지만, 정작 발을 디딜 곳은 얼마 남지 않았다. 멸종위기 야생생물 Ⅰ급이자 천연기념물인 두루미의 모습을 통해, 우리가 땅을 바꾸는 동안 그곳에 살아온 생명은 어디로 가야 하는지 묻고 싶었다.\n\n습지를 메워 농경지나 건설 부지로 바꾸면 두루미가 먹이를 찾고 쉬던 공간이 사라진다. 물을 빼거나 물길을 돌리면 남아 있는 습지도 제 역할을 하기 어렵다. 도로와 시설이 들어서고 사람과 차량의 왕래가 잦아지면 안심하고 머물 곳도 줄어든다. 두루미에게 필요한 것은 단순히 빈 땅이 아니라, 먹이를 구하고 방해받지 않고 쉴 수 있는 터전이다.\n\n이 차이를 인간이 만든 지도로 표현했다. 지도는 땅을 기록하면서 어디에 길을 내고 무엇을 세울지 정하는 계획의 바탕이 된다. 그러나 지도 위의 선으로 나뉘는 땅에도 이미 이어져 온 삶이 있다. 이를 드러내기 위해 생성형 AI로 주변의 풀과 둔덕을 지도 종이로 바꾸었다. 멀리서는 습지처럼 보이지만, 가까이에서는 잎과 땅 표면의 도로망과 필지 경계가 드러난다. 자연을 이루던 것들이 인간의 계획으로 대체된 풍경이다. 습지의 모습을 닮은 종이가 생명을 품을 수 없듯, 자연의 형태가 남아 있어도 살아갈 조건은 사라질 수 있음을 담았다.\n\n그 안에서 두루미와 바로 아래의 작은 습지는 사실적인 질감으로 남겼다. 젖은 흙과 갈색 갈대, 얕은 물은 회색과 아이보리의 종이 풍경 사이에서 아직 살아 있는 터전을 보여준다. 새의 펼쳐진 날개를 바라보던 시선이 그 몸을 받아줄 좁은 땅에도 머물기를 바랐다.\n\n제목 ‘돌아왔지만, 앉을 자리가 없다’에는 빠르고 무분별한 개발로 익숙한 터전을 잃어가는 생명의 처지를 담았다. 두루미를 지키는 일은 그 새가 의지하는 물과 먹이, 쉴 곳을 함께 남기는 일이다. 우리가 다음 개발의 선을 긋기 전에, 그 안에서 살아온 생명의 자리도 살펴보았으면 한다. 다음 계절에도 긴 비행 끝에 내려앉을 곳이 남아 있기를 바란다.",
      "aiTools": [
        "ChatGPT 이미지 생성 기능\nnanobanana 4k 업스케일링"
      ],
      "postEditingUsage": "사용함",
      "postEditingDetails": "없음",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "{\n\"task\": \"text_to_image\",\n\"requested_output\": {\n\"model\": \"GPT-Image-2\",\n\"resolution\": \"2K\",\n\"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\",\n},\n\"prompt\": {\n\"main_description\": \"Create a highly detailed fine-art environmental photograph combining a realistic red-crowned crane and one remaining natural wetland refuge with an expansive wetland constructed from ivory geographical map paper. The entire landscape resembles a marsh, but outside the crane's natural refuge, every exposed land surface and every reed-like leaf is made from printed map paper. Preserve a restrained, believable material contrast rather than creating a fantasy world.\",\n\"artistic_intent\": \"A red-crowned crane is descending toward the only remaining genuine wetland where it can land. The surrounding landscape still resembles its habitat in shape, but has been transformed into a human-planned cartographic environment. Express habitat loss through the contrast between a living muddy refuge and an extensive map-made wetland. Communicate this visually without text, symbols, buildings or explanatory graphics.\",\n\"camera_and_framing\": {\n\"format\": \"Wide horizontal landscape, approximately 16:9.\",\n\"viewpoint\": \"A low, moderately elevated viewpoint looking slightly downward across foreground marsh terrain toward a distant level horizon.\",\n\"perspective\": \"Natural perspective without wide-angle stretching or telephoto flattening.\",\n\"horizon_position\": \"Approximately 21 percent down from the top edge.\",\n\"sky_area\": \"Approximately the upper fifth of the frame.\",\n\"framing\": \"The crane is large and left of center. The natural refuge occupies the lower-left and lower-middle area. A winding pale water channel leads through the right half toward the horizon.\",\n\"focus\": \"Clearly resolved crane, foreground map textures and middle-ground paper reeds. Gradual atmospheric softness only in the far distance.\"\n},\n\"crane\": {\n\"species\": \"One anatomically accurate adult red-crowned crane.\",\n\"position\": \"The full crane spans approximately 17 to 49 percent of the image width and 5 to 58 percent of the image height.\",\n\"action\": \"Hovering just above the wetland in the final moment before landing, facing right, wings spread asymmetrically and legs extended downward.\",\n\"left_wing\": \"The wing on the viewer's left rises high toward the upper-left corner. Long white primary feathers fan upward and outward, with a clearly defined black lower feather section.\",\n\"right_wing\": \"The opposite wing extends diagonally upward toward the upper middle, appearing shorter because of its perspective.\",\n\"body\": \"White body positioned left of center, slightly tilted during descent, with individually articulated overlapping feathers.\",\n\"head_and_neck\": \"A graceful dark S-shaped neck bends forward and downward toward the right. A small red crown, dark face and long pointed gray-black beak remain clearly visible.\",\n\"legs_and_feet\": \"Exactly two slender dark legs hang below the body, slightly crossing in perspective. Distinct naturally jointed toes point downward and hover just above the muddy landing edge.\",\n\"surface_detail\": \"Fine feather structure, natural feather overlap, realistic beak and leg textures. No duplicated anatomy.\",\n\"shadow\": \"No visible bird-shaped cast shadow on the surrounding map terrain.\",\n\"reflection\": \"A restrained, partially fragmented reflection is visible in the dark natural pool beneath the bird.\"\n},\n\"natural_wetland_refuge\": {\n\"location\": \"An irregular oval refuge in the lower-left quadrant, extending approximately from 4 to 61 percent of the image width and from 49 to 87 percent of the image height.\",\n\"shape\": \"A shallow dark pool enclosed by uneven muddy banks and irregular clusters of dried brown reeds.\",\n\"landing_area\": \"A small damp muddy lip directly beneath the crane's feet.\",\n\"materials\": \"Photoreal wet dark-brown mud, granular soil, thin dried brown reed stems, small natural plant fragments and shallow dark reflective water.\",\n\"pool\": \"The darkest water in the scene, reflecting parts of the crane and nearby reeds with subtle distortion.\",\n\"boundary\": \"An organic, physically connected transition from the real muddy refuge into the surrounding pale map-made terrain. No cutout edge, decorative border or isolated floating platform.\",\n\"restriction\": \"This refuge is the only area containing genuine brown vegetation and exposed natural soil. Do not print map patterns on the crane, mud or natural reeds.\"\n},\n\"surrounding_map_wetland\": {\n\"extent\": \"The entire remaining foreground, middle ground and distant terrain is an ivory map-paper wetland extending to the horizon.\",\n\"topography\": \"Low irregular hummocks, shallow rounded ridges, gently raised islands and soft shoreline slopes. Subtle height differences create natural wetland relief.\",\n\"foreground\": \"Broad gently curved map-covered land surfaces occupy the bottom edge and lower-right corner, with paper reed clusters emerging from their surfaces.\",\n\"middle_ground\": \"Numerous irregular low islands and reed-covered banks separated by connected shallow water channels.\",\n\"background\": \"Increasingly small map-paper islands and reed clusters recede toward the horizon.\",\n\"material\": \"Warm off-white matte paper with restrained visible fibers, slight physical thickness and naturally curved surfaces.\",\n\"avoid\": \"No mountain landscape, cliffs, stacked contour-model terraces, snow, ice, stone formations or flat uninterrupted map sheet.\"\n},\n\"map_paper_reeds\": {\n\"appearance\": \"Ivory reed-like leaves made from individually folded narrow strips of geographical map paper.\",\n\"shape\": \"Slender elongated leaves with tapered pointed tips, shallow central folds and occasional gentle bends. Vary their heights and orientations naturally.\",\n\"distribution\": \"Irregular dense clusters on the foreground and middle-ground islands, with smaller clusters extending into the distance.\",\n\"physical_structure\": \"Every leaf has a coherent thin edge, distinct front and side surfaces and a believable rooted contact with the paper terrain.\",\n\"detail\": \"Visible separations between adjacent leaves. Resolve folded surfaces and printed lines without merging them into melted spikes or tangled ribbons.\",\n\"preservation_of_style\": \"These are paper-map interpretations of wetland grasses, not real plants and not architectural buildings.\"\n},\n\"cartographic_texture\": {\n\"coverage\": \"Printed geographical map texture covers all exposed paper terrain and the visible surfaces of the folded paper reeds.\",\n\"visual_language\": \"Clearly recognizable double-line roads, connected street networks, cadastral parcel boundaries, irregular city blocks and restrained fine contour lines.\",\n\"ink_color\": \"Muted slate gray and subdued blue-gray ink on ivory paper.\",\n\"line_quality\": \"Clean thin lines with consistent width, coherent intersections and legible separation between adjacent lines.\",\n\"surface_mapping\": \"The printed map bends continuously with the terrain and follows each paper leaf's folds and faces.\",\n\"scale\": \"Map patterns are clearly readable in the foreground and become proportionally finer with distance.\",\n\"restrictions\": \"No place names, letters, numbers, logos or random symbols. No marble veins, cracked-earth patterns, meaningless scribbles or printed lines floating above surfaces.\"\n},\n\"water_channels\": {\n\"main_channel\": \"A winding channel occupies the right half of the frame, entering from the right foreground and narrowing through the middle-right toward the distant center.\",\n\"secondary_channels\": \"Smaller connected channels curve between the low paper-map islands.\",\n\"relationship_to_map\": \"Shorelines follow the curved boundaries of mapped road corridors, creating an interaction between cartographic road geometry and wetland drainage.\",\n\"appearance\": \"Pale silver, creamy ivory and soft gray water, with delicate diffuse reflections and restrained fine ripples.\",\n\"physical_behavior\": \"Water occupies low areas and remains level. Shoreline contacts, reflection directions and small ripples are physically consistent.\",\n\"style\": \"A restrained, softly luminous water surface integrated into the paper-crafted landscape. Avoid a dark blue photographic lake or dramatic waves.\",\n\"critical_restriction\": \"Absolutely no printed map texture, road lines, parcel grids or text on the water surface or visibly beneath it.\"\n},\n\"lighting_and_color\": {\n\"time\": \"Quiet overcast dawn.\",\n\"sky\": \"Layered soft gray clouds with a small pale warm opening near the upper center-right.\",\n\"sun_position\": \"Approximately 58 percent across the image width and 13 percent down from the top.\",\n\"illumination\": \"Soft diffuse sky illumination with subtle directional highlights from the pale sun.\",\n\"palette\": \"Low-saturation ivory, neutral gray, muted blue-gray map ink, natural subdued brown reeds, white and black crane feathers, and a small red crown.\",\n\"reflections\": \"A restrained pale warm reflection runs through distant and middle-ground channels beneath the sun.\",\n\"contrast\": \"Moderate contrast with the natural muddy refuge distinctly darker than the surrounding ivory map terrain.\",\n\"avoid\": \"Strong orange sunset, saturated gold, vivid cyan, excessive HDR or dramatic artificial glow.\"\n},\n\"detail_reconstruction\": {\n\"priority\": \"Resolve individual paper leaves, map linework, feather layers, muddy shoreline textures and water boundaries at the selected high output resolution.\",\n\"requirements\": \"Separate adjacent objects, maintain clean silhouettes, preserve material-specific detail and use coherent geometry throughout.\",\n\"middle_ground\": \"Keep map reeds and shoreline structures readable instead of reducing them to lumpy crumpled paper or indistinct texture masses.\",\n\"sharpness\": \"Natural clarity without halos, oversharpened outlines, repeated noise or artificial microtexture.\",\n\"distance\": \"Retain atmospheric depth. Do not apply identical detail density or sharpness to every distance.\"\n},\n\"final_constraints\": [\n\"One crane only.\",\n\"One genuine muddy wetland refuge directly beneath the crane.\",\n\"All surrounding land and vegetation remain map-paper constructions.\",\n\"Water contains no map printing.\",\n\"No buildings, roads rendered as asphalt, vehicles, people or construction equipment.\",\n\"No added mountains.\",\n\"No visible crane cast shadow on the map ground.\",\n\"No text, labels, captions, borders or screen interface.\",\n\"No melted paper vegetation, fused leaves, floating ink or malformed anatomy.\",\n\"Produce one complete landscape image.\"\n]\n}\n}",
      "processCaptureDriveUrl": "https://drive.google.com/open?id=1whrFExzO9ddP5MoZjmEo1MBivgDuOyh8, https://drive.google.com/open?id=15-GtO86FIDtSt9ZWGJyPC-T684xnq0rX, https://drive.google.com/open?id=16A3pDbo2exxqDJkQPUBgx7hFIsLB26Ap",
