      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "Create a wide 16:9 Korean digital heritage artwork inspired by traditional Korean folding-screen paintings (Minhwa/landscape folding screens).\n\nMain Subject & Narrative: At the center, the authentic Seoksu (stone guardian statue) from the Tomb of King Muryeong of Baekje (depicted with its distinctive iron horn, snout, and ancient stone texture) swims gracefully forward in the sacred river, guiding exactly ONE single traditional wooden royal barge toward the afterlife. Inside this single boat, King Muryeong and his Queen sit quietly side-by-side. Their faces are softly obscured by traditional Korean mist and clouds, showing only their dignified silhouettes and ancient Baekje royal attire, keeping their presence symbolic, ceremonial, and mysterious.\n\nWater and Wave Effect: The vast surrounding river remains tranquil and natural in tone. Strictly along the wake/path directly behind the moving boat, the water transforms into a decorative trail of repeating arched fish-scale wave patterns (traditional Seigaiha / Korean wave motif). These waves flow in six distinct colors associated with the lost colors of the Seoksu, rendered not in neon, but in elegant, harmonious traditional mineral pigments (muted indigo, celadon jade, soft mustard gold, dusty coral, sage teal, and muted violet) that blend gracefully with the landscape.\n\nBackground & Environment: The landscape depicts Seocheon Flower Garden (Seocheonkkotbat), the mythical Korean flower garden of the afterlife realm. Mystical, sacred blooming lotus flowers and otherworldly afterlife blossoms line the waters and slopes. Surrounding the river are layered Korean indigo-violet mountains, waterfalls cascading into the river, stylized golden-edged clouds, and subtle celestial symbols.\n\nArt Style: A flat, decorative, symbolic painting style combining traditional Korean folding-screen spatial logic with contemporary digital heritage aesthetics. Clean bold contours, rhythmic curves, harmonious oriental mineral palette, and poetic atmospheric depth. Avoid photorealism, 3D rendering, duplication of boats or figures, and fluorescent over-saturation. High-resolution, ceremonial, sacred, and serene.",
