      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "[1] 최종 이미지 생성 프롬프트 — Nano Banana Pro (Higgsfield), 4K, 16:9, 참고 이미지 없음, 2026-09-27 14:01, 작업 ID cd789d10-ed58-4ef8-a5ff-d3a1c5bf5a25\n\nRender a cinematic, photorealistic night photograph: a small ancient Baekje stone guardian beast statue standing alone on top of an old fortress wall, keeping watch over a sleeping modern city across a river.\n\nSubject: the defining unreal detail is a warm gold light glowing from inside the carved flame-wing grooves on its flanks and legs, like thin gold inlay lit from within. The light stays inside the carved lines, which remain intact carved stone; the stone surface around them is unbroken. The glow is bright enough to read clearly against the cool blue night yet soft, like embers seen through a thin layer of ash, spilling only a faint golden sheen onto the nearby stone while the rest of the statue stays cool and moonlit. The statue is the Stone Guardian Beast (Jinmyosu) from the 6th-century tomb of King Muryeong in Gongju, Korea — a real national treasure about 30 cm tall and 49 cm long, carved from pale sage-green hornblende stone with ochre and rust-brown weathering settled in its crevices. Its body is long, low and heavy: the body is about 1.6 times longer than it is tall, a stout barrel-shaped torso resting on four very short, thick, stumpy legs, so short that its heavy belly hangs only a hand's width above the stone. A blunt square muzzle with a long, wide, closed mouth forming one straight horizontal slit, and thick lips that still carry faint traces of old red pigment; small oval ears and round bulging eyes; a single dark, corroded iron horn rising from the crown of its head as one single stem, splitting into just two small twigs only near its tip, like a small gnarled branch; exactly four raised scalloped mane ridges in a row along its back; flame-shaped wing motifs carved in low relief on both flanks and on the upper front and hind legs, curling like scrolling flames; a short tail pointing downward at the rear. The surface is hand-carved and worn smooth by 1,500 years, with tiny chips and pits.\n\nAction and location: it stands in three-quarter profile on a weathered granite capstone of the Gongsanseong fortress wall in Gongju, head held forward and slightly raised, gazing out over the Geumgang River toward the city. Beads of dew rest on the stone, and a few blades of grass grow from the joints of the wall.\n\nCamera: low viewpoint at the statue's own eye level, 100mm macro lens at f/2.8, the statue sharp from horn to tail.\n\nComposition: the guardian occupies the left third of the frame, facing right into open space; beyond the wall the dark river with drifting mist, the far bank lined with the warm lights of the city and a lit bridge, all rendered as soft round bokeh; a deep blue pre-dawn sky with a thin crescent moon high on the right.\n\nLighting: the key light is cool blue moonlight from the upper right, rim-lighting the horn and the back ridges; the front of the statue falls into soft blue shade, lit only by the ambient night sky and by the golden glow from its own carved grooves.\n\nStyle: fine-art cinematic still, natural fine film grain, true-to-life stone texture, restrained palette of slate blue, sage stone green and ember gold, quiet and reverent mood, a clean image with a plain untouched sky.\n\n[2] 수정용 AI 편집 프롬프트 — Nano Banana Pro 이미지 편집, 입력: [1]의 결과 이미지, 2026-09-27 14:07, 작업 ID 78204241-aa87-47bf-96d3-cc5985f99359\n\nEdit this image with one small local change only: on the front tip of the stone statue's blunt square muzzle, fill the two small nostril holes with solid carved stone, so the front of the snout becomes one smooth, plain, rounded stone surface with the same pale sage-green weathered texture, tiny pits and faint ochre stains as the surrounding muzzle. Keep everything else in the image exactly identical to the reference: the same composition and framing, the same statue shape, closed mouth with red-tinted lips, eyes, ears, iron horn with all its branches, back ridges, the thin golden glow inside the carved flame-wing grooves, the fortress wall, grass, river, city bokeh, crescent moon, colors, lighting and film grain.\n\n[3] 최종본 제작: [1] 결과 위에 [2] 결과의 주둥이 앞부분(전체 면적의 2.23%)만 합성하고, 16:9 크롭·축소·300dpi 지정만 했습니다(생성형 보정 없음).",
