      "fullPrompt": "평안을 잇는 춤 — 도시를 잇는 물결\n사용 도구: OpenAI Codex 내장 이미지 생성 도구(image_gen). 확인되지 않은 모델명을 별도로 기재하지 않음.\n아래는 최종 출품 이미지에 직접 이어지는 3단계 입력 프롬프트 전문이다. 다른 비교 시안의 입력은 최종 이미지 생성 경로에 포함되지 않아 구분한다.\n전 과정에서 외부 사진을 이미지 합성 재료로 업로드하지 않았으며, 앞 단계에서 생성한 자체 이미지를 다음 단계의 편집 입력으로 사용했다.\n\n[1단계 | 초기 군무 이미지 생성 | 2026-09-25]\n이미지 입력: 없음(텍스트로 생성).\n출력: exec-e4afc2bb-d3c1-40ff-813d-b04063e277b3.png\n출력 SHA256: 06918980a8fe5a145ab7a20da34dcb9ed6cfdedb300aaee033e5fb3160b82bfb\n입력 전문:\nUse case: stylized-concept. Asset type: one complete original image for the Korean AI Heritage art competition, not a film storyboard, no text, no border, no collage. Create a native 3840 x 2160 pixel 16:9 landscape image if supported, highest available fine detail. Korean cultural fantasy grounded in the lotus-pattern fired-clay bricks of King Muryeong's tomb in Gongju and the low hills and broad Geum River of Ungjin Baekje. This is a contemporary imaginative reinterpretation, NOT a historical reconstruction or a royal portrait. Refined epic fine-art realism with crafted painterly surfaces, believable human anatomy and weight, silk weave, porous terracotta relief, wet stone and water with differentiated textures. Palette from the approved project: deep cobalt, jade, ivory, restrained cinnabar, warm bronze and honey sunlight. Complex but intentional visual hierarchy and vast depth, dazzling material transformations, not generic palace fantasy or a stage show. Adult Korean dancers wear long ivory crossover tops with expansive cobalt-lined sleeves, jade pleated lower garments, narrow vermilion sashes and flat dark soft shoes, hair simply tied. Human bodies stay whole and anatomically plausible, fabric may undergo the surreal transformation only beyond the hands. Supporting soles touch the ground, knees soft, torso leads movement, clear separated hands. No queen, crowns, historical-costume claims, artist imitation, brushes, sketchbooks, artifact touching, floating humans, ballet pointe, duplicated limbs, faceless foreground people, generic Chinese palaces, neon circles, confetti, firework sparkles, watermarks or lettering. Core visual meaning: a wish for peace carried by heritage becomes shared living movement today. The oldest material, living dance and open landscape must be connected visibly in this single composition.\nCOMPOSITION B — THE LIVING LOTUS. A bold overhead-oblique fine-art composition, viewing at about 55 degrees, not vertically flat. An immense lotus shape emerges from seven grounded adult dancers arranged in an open spiral around a quiet oval mirror of warm sky. Six peripheral dancers and one subtly larger lead, each clearly separate and with two arms. Their ivory/cobalt sleeves unfurl as interwoven broad petal arcs; the outer ends transition gradually from woven silk into actual blue river channels and green sloping terraced land. These huge petal-shaped landscapes embrace a small completely still, unoccupied pool at the center: a space of peace created together. Half the lotus geometry at lower left remains ancient weathered terracotta lotus-relief brickwork; the other half at upper right is living silk and flowing landscape, a single continuous transformation across the diagonal. Dancers stay on firm wet terracotta walkways, not floating in water; slight natural ripples at shoreline. The near rim shows modest repeated rectangular lotus-pattern bricks. Open low Korean river hills far away at top right, with honey-colored morning mist. Strong readable graphic silhouette, texture rewards close viewing. Human bodies small but visible at 10 to 15 percent frame height. No literal giant botanical flower, no magical runes, no concentric decorative arena, no stage curtains, no identical synchronized copy-pasted people. Restrained luminous gold against deep indigo water, ivory silk and earthy vermilion. The whole image should feel like a single impossible yet coherent living cultural landscape.\n\n[2단계 | 구도 유지 보정 | 2026-09-25]\n이미지 입력: 1단계 생성 결과.\n출력: exec-a5be4248-7bb9-4f39-b20f-2c0a5b05c80f.png\n출력 SHA256: b113bf41eaea964390040ef78c60c62fffe0d7df6df9150bd78fc7b9bc71bd2e\n아래 프롬프트는 4K 생성을 요청했으나 실제 출력은 1672×941이었다. 요청과 실제 결과를 구분한다.\n입력 전문:\nUse case: precise-object-edit. Edit target: the supplied image B, selected final artwork titled \"평안을 잇는 춤\"; do NOT print this title. This is the final high-resolution export for a single-image competition. Return an actual 3840 x 2160 pixel PNG (4K landscape, 16:9), not a smaller preview labelled 4K. Preserve the entire composition and every subject's placement, the exact seven adult Korean dancers, anatomy and individual poses, all ivory/cobalt/jade/vermilion costumes, circular quiet reflecting pool, terracotta lotus relief foreground, silk-to-river landscape transformation, distant low Korean hills, and the dawn lighting. Only improve fine native-resolution detail and finish: clear natural faces with no waxiness, physically distinct wrists and sleeve edges, woven silk, finely porous brick relief, differentiated trees and clear water reflections. Keep the undisturbed center pool empty and calm. Do not add or remove humans or buildings or alter terrain. Do not change crop or camera, do not introduce duplicate limbs, do not add text, title, signature, marks, frame, sharpening halos or artificial glitter. Preserve the poetic painted realism. Essential: output pixel dimensions 3840 by 2160, the file itself must be 4K.\n\n[3단계 | 현대 도시와 물길 연결 | 2026-09-26]\n이미지 입력: 2단계 생성 결과. 사용자가 다시 첨부한 동일 구도의 화면 캡처 대신 도구 모음이 없는 깨끗한 원본을 사용.\n출력: exec-9539c597-75ef-4d81-9b85-73c677f7cf1a.png\n출력 SHA256: 16f05648a0006bd966e8f5201a5637c28ce6a3f17faacb1869d607392b8f9978\n입력 전문:\nUse case: compositing.\nAsset type: a refined landscape artwork for an AI Heritage image competition, candidate B.\nInput image 1 is the EDIT TARGET: the clean original corresponding exactly to the user's attached screenshot. Preserve the compelling elevated oblique camera, seven ivory/cobalt/jade traditional dancers circling a calm mirror pool, warm terracotta lotus-relief terraces at left/front, broad low Korean hills, a sweeping river valley, warm low sunlight from upper right, and the extraordinary blue sleeve-to-landscape idea. This is a creative imagined landscape inspired by Baekje heritage; not a historical reconstruction or geographically exact city.\n\nPRIMARY EDIT: develop the existing sleeve/landscape metamorphosis so it visibly links cultural heritage with TODAY'S city and a living river landscape. The clear visual thesis is: \"An old shared gesture flows through today's city, reconnecting people and nature.\" It should feel imaginative, moving and culturally grounded, with a clear continuous visual cause: lotus terracotta → living dance → blue silk → river and green public space within a contemporary town.\n\nKeep the seven dancers as the main human focus in the left/center 60 percent, in distinct confident grounded dance poses, anatomically coherent bodies with two arms each, leg/foot support where visible, connected shoulders and natural hands. Maintain the open reflective circular pool as a quiet visual anchor. Do not replace the ensemble with modern protagonists. Keep the large clay lotus reliefs legible and materially tactile, with coherent brick construction, fewer random tiny rubble-like fragments, believable weathering rather than a collapse.\n\nRefine the RIGHT-HAND flowing blue forms into TWO or THREE broad graceful continuous ribbons rather than a busy mesh of tiny streams. At the dancers the material is clearly woven silk; moving away it continuously becomes translucent flowing river water; farther through the valley it becomes a real winding river corridor with wooded banks, planted promenades and small pocket parks. A silk fold can carry a believable miniature landscape briefly as it unfurls, an intentional elegant impossible metamorphosis. Let the curves guide the eye from the dancers into modern civic life. Show lucid transitions of weave → ripples → tree-lined banks, not multiple disconnected pasted worlds. This fantasy is the single dominant visual invention. Retain generous clean river surfaces and depth. No destructive wave, flood, tsunami, broken streets, waterfall spilling over houses or water swallowing a city.\n\nReplace the old palace-like settlement in the upper-right and some right-middle-distance fields with a recognizably PRESENT-DAY KOREAN RIVERSIDE TOWN: restrained pale masonry mid-rise residential blocks with clear contemporary window grids, a few low civic buildings with clean flat roofs, streets and an accessible green waterfront promenade. Place the town in the right-hand third at a scale visibly readable as modern architecture at normal viewing size. It must belong to the same perspective and warm atmosphere as the original valley. No skyscraper megacity, futuristic towers or neon. Keep substantial natural hills, trees and river; do not replace all the landscape with buildings.\n\nBring the nearer right-side ribbon down gently into a tree-lined public riverbank next to these contemporary blocks. Include one slender contemporary pedestrian bridge across the narrow river corridor and a few naturally scaled tiny walkers and one cyclist on a dry path, as subtle evidence of today's everyday use. Modern people stay far smaller than the traditional dancers and do not compete with them. Calm natural water flow, protected green bank, ordinary usable public space; no spectacle fountains and no ornamental palace resort.\n\nMake the composition asymmetrical and panoramic like the input, not frontal or symmetrical, not a circular concert plaza and not a generic luxury landscape rendering. Preserve energy and the unified terracotta / cobalt / jade / gold palette, but use atmospheric perspective and distinct material textures so it reads as one physically lit world. Dancers, brick relief and sleeve transformations remain dominant; contemporary buildings support the story without becoming the focal subject.\nElegant cinematic fine-art realism, detailed silk, fired clay, trees, light and reflections, rich but controlled color. Landscape 16:9 at the highest available native detail. No text, logo, watermark, border, interface toolbar, magic particles, floating glyphs, queen/crown, generic pagodas, modern giant foreground visitors, or picture-in-picture.\n\n[생성 후 출력 처리]\n최종 생성 원본: 1672×941 RGB PNG. 생성 도구의 실제 출력 그대로 보관.\n제출본: Pillow LANCZOS로 1920×1080 및 3840×2160 로컬 확대, sRGB 및 300dpi 메타데이터 적용.\n이미지 내용의 추가 합성·생성형 디테일 복원은 하지 않음. 3840×2160 파일은 로컬 확대본이며 네이티브 4K 생성 원본이 아님.",
