      "fullPrompt": "[영상 생성 프롬프트] · [CUT 01–07]\n\n================================================================\n\n[Cut_01_Prompt]\n\nAn 8-second single continuous shot beginning from the supplied image. The camera tracks very slowly to the right at a low height. Nearby leaves on the left slide toward the left edge of the frame through natural parallax, gradually revealing slightly more of the existing pond and valley, while the distant mountains remain nearly stationary. Maintain a constant camera height and field of view.\n\nThe single stag on the right bank takes two short, careful steps toward the water, placing its hooves naturally on the ground. It then stops and slowly begins to lower its head a little. Preserve its body size, antler branching, four legs, warm brown coat, cream-colored underside, and delicate golden markings. Its body moves naturally with its steps, and its hooves maintain firm contact with the ground without sliding.\n\nThin mist drifts slowly through the valleys, and slender waterfalls flow continuously. Pink lotus flowers and green lotus leaves sway almost imperceptibly with the gentle ripples. Preserve the reference image’s deep midnight navy sky, green mountains and trees, muted green-teal water with warm golden reflections, and pale pink lotus petals. A tranquil, mystical holographic media-art aesthetic with soft silver and gold contour light. Show one coherent space with continuous, natural movement, without camera rotation, zooming, or cuts.\n\n================================================================\n\n[Cut_02_Prompt]\n\nA 7-second single continuous shot beginning from the supplied image. A single stag is already leaning down with its muzzle touching the water, drinking quietly. All four hooves remain firmly planted in their original positions on the bank. Only its mouth and jaw make very small, natural drinking movements. One ear flicks gently once, and subtle breathing is visible in its body. Its head and neck remain lowered.\n\nSmall, gentle concentric ripples form continuously at the point where its muzzle touches the water and spread slowly toward the pink lotus flowers and green lotus leaves on the left. The stag's reflection wavers naturally with those same ripples, while the flowers and leaves sway softly. The camera makes a very short, slow lateral move to the left at water level. Keep both the stag and the lotus flowers on the left in frame, gradually guiding attention toward the ripples and flowers. Maintain a constant camera height and field of view.\n\nPreserve the stag's brown coat, cream-colored underside, antler branching, four legs, and delicate golden markings. Maintain the deep midnight navy sky, green mountains and trees, muted green-teal water with warm golden reflections, pale pink lotuses, and fine silver contours. Background waterfalls and mist flow quietly. Tranquil, mystical holographic media art with soft, steady lighting. The stag remains in place with its head lowered throughout. No camera rotation, zooming, or cuts; show one coherent, continuous scene.\n\n================================================================\n\n[Cut_03_Prompt]\n\nA 6-second single continuous shot beginning from the supplied image. From near water level, frame the already fully open lotus and the broad green lotus leaf on the left. One droplet hanging from the leaf tip falls into the pond, sending small, gentle concentric ripples slowly beneath the lotus. The droplet falls only once and merges naturally with the water.\n\nThe pale pink and pearl-white petals retain their fully open form, swaying almost imperceptibly with the ripples. Preserve the number and arrangement of the petals, the yellow stamens and seedpod, and the delicate silver and gold veins. The green leaf moves slightly with the water, while the pink and golden reflections shimmer naturally with those same ripples.\n\nThe camera makes a very short, slow forward move toward the lotus. Keep the entire flower and the point where the droplet falls from the leaf tip within the frame. Focus stays on the lotus and the nearby water. The single small bird already visible in the background flies gently from left to right close to the water, beginning a slight upward glide toward the end. Keep the bird small and distant.\n\nPreserve the deep midnight navy sky, green mountains and trees, muted green-teal water with warm golden reflections, and pale pink lotus petals. Distant waterfalls and thin mist flow quietly in a mystical holographic media-art atmosphere. The flower remains open throughout, without blooming again or changing shape. No camera rotation or cuts; show one coherent, continuous scene.\n\n================================================================\n\n[Cut_04_Prompt]\n\nA 7-second continuous shot. In the wide landscape composition of the starting image, exactly two birds fly away from the camera into the valley, following the open central waterway. Both are seen from behind. The nearer bird stays slightly left of center, and the farther bird remains ahead and to the right, with clear separation. Each bird alternates gentle, naturally timed wingbeats with short glides. Their backs and short fan-shaped tails remain visible, with their heads pointing forward into the valley. Preserve each bird's two wings, compact body and coherent feather structure.\n\nThe camera glides smoothly forward over the water, following behind at the starting camera height with a constant wide field of view. Foreground lotuses and the nearby banks gradually pass outward beyond the frame edges. Mid-distance mountains shift more slowly, while distant peaks remain nearly stable, creating natural depth and parallax. Maintain roughly the same distance from the nearer bird. Both birds remain clearly recognizable and inside the frame throughout. By the end, the camera has moved slightly closer to the valley entrance.\n\nThin waterfalls flow continuously. Delicate mist drifts slowly through the valleys. Pink lotuses and green leaves sway subtly, with soft golden reflections rippling on the water. Preserve the deep midnight navy sky, naturally green mountains and trees, silver feathers and fine warm gold outlines. Peaceful, mysterious holographic media art. Exactly two birds; no new animals appear. One smooth forward tracking movement with no zoom, camera rotation, sudden acceleration or cuts.\n\n\n================================================================\n\n[Cut_05_Prompt]\n\nAn 5-second continuous shot. Preserve the starting image's composition and holographic media art palette. Clouds, waterfalls and mist remain visibly alive together from the first moment to the last.\n\nCloud motion is the highest priority. Translucent cloud masses with delicate gold outlines drift slowly from left to right in a light mountain breeze. Their gradual displacement relative to the mountain ridges is clearly visible. Rounded edges softly billow, curl and unfurl as they travel, with the gold outlines flexing naturally with the cloud forms. Nearby clouds move more noticeably while distant clouds drift more slowly. Keep the motion perceptible throughout all eight seconds at a calm, unhurried pace.\n\nWater continuously falls down the central tall waterfall and the smaller surrounding waterfalls at a natural gravity-driven speed. Flowing texture travels downward within the water streams. Fine spray rises at their bases, gentle ripples spread where the water lands, and golden reflections shimmer softly across the water.\n\nThinner, more transparent mist remains layered around the mountain slopes and valleys, drifting slowly. Its edges blend naturally with the clouds, gently revealing and veiling small areas of green mountain. Maintain this mist layer throughout, with clear openings around the central waterfall and the dragons' faces.\n\nExactly three silver dragons rise slowly a short distance from their starting positions, gently bending their bodies as whiskers and manes trail softly. Keep them separate and preserve their existing heads, horns, limbs and continuous body structure. The camera glides forward very slowly with a slight upward tilt, retaining a wide view of the central waterfall and all three dragons. Keep all three heads inside the frame throughout.\n\nDeep midnight navy sky, natural green mountains and trees, pearl-silver dragons, fine warm gold outlines and subtle blue-violet iridescence. Peaceful, beautiful holographic media art. Steady natural flow without fast clouds, time-lapse, vortices, flashes, orbiting, camera roll, zoom or cuts.\n\n================================================================\n\n[Cut_06_Prompt]\n\nOne continuous 4-second shot using the supplied image as the starting frame. Keep the camera stationary throughout.\n\n0–2 seconds: Immediately, the human-faced bird makes one powerful downward wing stroke and flies swiftly upward toward the upper-right corner. Its body radiates pearl-silver and warm golden light. Its long tail and feather tips stream fluidly behind it. Following a fast, smooth ascending trajectory, its body and wings exit through the upper-right frame boundary, followed by the entire tail and the pink lotus held in its feet. The bird completely leaves the frame by approximately 2 seconds. Preserve its beautiful facial profile and coherent avian anatomy.\n\nDuring the ascent, abundant fine silver and gold particles stream from the tail tips, leaving a graceful curved wake behind the bird. Vary the particles subtly in size and brightness for delicate depth. The luminous trail follows the tail’s movement and spreads naturally behind it.\n\n2–4 seconds: Only the lingering particles remain in the sky after the bird has departed. They swirl gently, spread apart and gradually dim. Clouds continue drifting slowly with softly billowing edges, while thin mist flows between the mountain peaks.\n\nPreserve the deep navy night sky, green mountains and beautiful silver-gold holographic media art. The intact bird physically flies out of frame; its body does not dissolve into particles or become transparent. No slow motion, hovering, camera tracking, rotation, flashes, particle explosions, additional creatures, cuts or text.\n\n================================================================\n\n[Cut_07_Prompt]\n\nOne continuous 7-second shot. Begin with the engraved silver surface close-up in the start image and finish on the complete Dongtak-eunjan cup and saucer composition in the end image.\n\n0–5 seconds: The camera moves smoothly backward along the same viewing axis at a gentle, steady pace. Preserve the engraved grooves, fine scratches and aged silver texture as the field of view gradually expands. Reveal that the curved engraved surface is part of the lid. The lotus-shaped knob, gold petal ornament, cup body, short pedestal and wide bronze saucer with green patina progressively enter the frame. The original engraving remains attached to the same metal surface and naturally becomes smaller with increasing distance. Focus adjusts smoothly so the complete vessel and its material details become clear.\n\nThe light illuminating the engraving slowly subsides, leaving a delicate silver-gold afterglow along the existing lines, matching the end image. The cup, closed lid and saucer remain stationary, preserving their shapes and proportions. As the view widens, reveal dark green mountains, layered mist and calm reflective water. Clouds and mist drift slowly in a light breeze, with subtle ripples in the reflections.\n\nEase the camera to a stop upon reaching the full end-image composition at 5 seconds. From 5–7 seconds, hold the camera still on the complete vessel. Clouds, mist and water reflections continue their gentle movement during this hold.\n\nPreserve aged silver and bronze, gold ornament, green patina and the existing engraved motifs. A peaceful, mysterious holographic media art afterglow. Reveal the complete vessel through backward camera movement alone, without morphing the object or rearranging its engravings. No cuts, abrupt zoom, camera rotation, additional creatures or generated text.",
