      "fullPrompt": "〈빛으로 이어진 시간, 웅진〉 사용 프롬프트 전문 (Midjourney 동영상, 시작·끝 프레임 지정 방식 / 각 프롬프트 끝의 hard cut, jump cut 등은 네거티브 문구)\n\n[전환 1 · 진묘수 → 왕실 치장]\nSeamless continuous shot, one unbroken camera movement from the first frame to the last frame. Start: inside an ancient Baekje brick-vaulted royal tomb with carved lotus patterns on the arched ceiling, a weathered stone guardian beast (jinmyosu) sits in the dark, its eyes glowing amber. A small oil lamp flickers at the lower left, fine dust particles drift in the blue darkness on the right. Transition: the camera pushes forward slowly and steadily toward the guardian beast's glowing right eye. The amber light in the eye gently intensifies and blooms outward, soft volumetric golden glow spreading until it fills the entire frame. Floating dust particles turn into drifting golden light specks. As the glow slowly settles, the golden light condenses and resolves into the intricate openwork gold filigree of a flame-shaped Baekje crown ornament, positioned in the same spot where the eye was. End: the camera eases back slightly to reveal a noblewoman seen from behind over her shoulder, glossy black hair with a black silk headpiece, a long ornate gold earring, a black collar with gold embroidery on a deep red velvet robe. An attendant's two hands carefully insert the gold crown ornament into her hair. Behind her, a painted wall with a bird mural and warm candlelight glowing at the lower right. Warm amber-gold color palette maintained throughout, no sudden color or brightness jump. Slow, constant camera speed. Cinematic, 35mm film look, shallow depth of field, soft film grain, photorealistic. hard cut, jump cut, white flash, fade to black, morphing face, warping, camera shake, speed ramp, distorted hands, extra fingers, face visible, text, watermark\n\n[전환 2 · 왕실 치장 → 왕의 모습]\nSeamless continuous shot, one unbroken camera movement from the first frame to the last frame. Start: close-up from behind a Baekje noblewoman, an attendant's hands pressing a flame-shaped openwork gold crown ornament into her black silk headpiece, long gold earring, black collar with gold embroidery on a deep red velvet robe, painted bird mural and warm candlelight in the background. Transition: as the attendant's hands release the ornament and gently withdraw out of frame, the camera slowly tilts down and drifts along the black-and-gold embroidered collar, following it downward until the rich deep red fabric fills the entire frame. The camera keeps gliding smoothly through the soft folds of red silk without any cut. The folds of fabric shift and flow, becoming the wide red brocade sleeve of a king's robe with a black band of gold floral medallions. The warm candlelight gradually turns into low golden sunset light streaming in from the side. End: the camera eases back to reveal the torso of a Baekje king seen from the side, face not visible, deep red brocade robe with gold phoenix patterns, wide sleeves with black-and-gold trim, an ornate gold plaque belt, gold pendant ornaments with white jade beads and long red tassels hanging at his waist, hands resting calmly at his sides. Behind him, a grand wooden palace hall with lattice windows, royal guards standing in silhouette at a bright open doorway, long golden sunbeams stretching across the stone floor, backlit haze. Warm red-gold color palette throughout, no sudden change in brightness or color. Slow, constant, fluid camera speed. Cinematic, 35mm film look, shallow depth of field, soft film grain, photorealistic. hard cut, jump cut, flash, fade to black, morphing body, warping, woman turning into man, face visible, camera shake, speed ramp, distorted hands, extra fingers, text, watermark\n\n[전환 3 · 왕의 모습 → 강가의 교류]\nSeamless continuous shot, one unbroken camera movement from the first frame to the last frame. Start: inside a grand Baekje palace hall at sunset, close on the side of a king's torso, deep red brocade robe, black-and-gold belt, gold pendant ornaments with red and gold tassels. Two royal guards stand in silhouette on either side of a bright open doorway, long golden sunbeams stretch across the stone floor. Transition: the camera glides forward past the king's sleeve and moves steadily toward the gap between the two silhouetted guards at the doorway. As the camera passes between them, the guards naturally slide out of frame to the left and right through parallax and are never seen again. The dark wooden door pillar sweeps across the frame for a brief moment. Beyond the doorway, the warm backlight completely fills the frame with soft golden haze. The haze slowly clears to reveal an empty open landscape with no people at all: a wide calm river below, and a fortress on a distant hill across the water. The camera flies forward low over the empty river toward the fortress. During the flight, the sun sinks behind the far hills, and the color shifts step by step: warm gold, to soft orange, to dusky pink and violet, and finally into cool misty blue twilight. River mist rises over the water. Warm lights begin to glow on the fortress walls, keeping a touch of gold in the cool scene. End: the camera lowers smoothly onto an old wooden boat deck at the river's edge. Two arms in dark sleeves enter from the left and right edges of the frame. One hand passes a round green bronze mirror with dragon relief to the other open palm. Behind them, the misty blue river and the fortress with warm glowing lights on the hill. Only hands and arms visible, no full bodies, no faces. The guards remain inside the palace hall. No person appears outside the doorway, on the river, or on the boat except the two arms at the end. Gradual, smooth color temperature transition from warm golden sunset to cool blue twilight, no sudden jump in color or brightness. Slow, constant, fluid camera speed. Cinematic, 35mm film look, soft film grain, photorealistic. person suddenly disappearing, person vanishing, figure fading out, guard standing outside, guard on the boat, standing figure on the deck, extra people, crowd, full body person, face visible, hard cut, jump cut, white flash, fade to black, sudden color change, morphing, warping, camera shake, speed ramp, distorted hands, extra fingers, text, watermark\n\n[전환 4 · 강가의 교류 → 연화문 기와]\nSeamless continuous shot, one unbroken camera movement from the first frame to the last frame. Start: blue dawn on a misty river, on an old wooden boat deck, two hands in dark sleeves exchange a round green bronze mirror with dragon relief. Across the water, a fortress on a hill with warm glowing lights. Transition: the receiving hand gently takes the mirror and both hands withdraw out of frame. The camera rises slowly from the boat deck and glides forward over the calm water toward the fortress on the hill. River mist thickens and softly envelops the frame in cool blue-grey haze. Within the drifting mist, time quietly passes: the fortress lights fade out, the wooden buildings disappear, and only the weathered stone walls remain, covered with moss and grass. The camera continues forward and slowly descends along the old stone wall toward the ground at its base. Soil, dry leaves and small stones gradually settle and accumulate. Meanwhile the sun rises, and the mist warms and thins, the color shifting step by step from cool blue, to pale blue-grey, to soft peach dawn, to warm golden sunlight. End: extreme low-angle close-up at ground level at the foot of the weathered stone fortress wall. A broken ancient Baekje roof tile with a carved lotus flower pattern lies half-buried in dark brown soil, surrounded by pebbles, dry fallen leaves and thin grass blades. Warm low golden sunlight rakes across the textured surface from the right, soft bokeh background. The camera settles into a slow lateral drift to the left. Gradual, smooth color temperature shift from cool blue dawn to warm golden light, no sudden jump in color or brightness. Slow, constant, fluid camera speed. Cinematic, macro detail, 35mm film look, shallow depth of field, soft film grain, photorealistic. hard cut, jump cut, white flash, fade to black, sudden color change, abrupt lighting change, mirror morphing into tile, object morphing, warping, camera shake, speed ramp, face visible, distorted hands, extra fingers, people, modern objects, text, watermark\n\n[전환 5 · 연화문 기와 → 발굴 현장]\nSeamless continuous shot, one unbroken camera movement from the first frame to the last frame. Start: extreme low-angle close-up at ground level at the foot of a weathered stone fortress wall. A broken ancient Baekje roof tile with a carved lotus flower pattern lies half-buried in dark brown soil among pebbles, dry leaves and thin grass. Soft warm golden sunlight rakes across it from the right. The camera drifts slowly to the left. Transition: an archaeologist's hand holding a soft-bristled brush enters from the right side of the frame and gently sweeps the soil off the lotus pattern, fine dust drifting in the golden light. The hand lifts away and sets the brush down on the ground to the lower right. Then the camera begins to pull back and rise, very slowly at first, keeping the old stone wall on the left side of the frame. The camera smoothly accelerates as it cranes up and back, revealing more and more of the site: the lotus tile becomes one of many excavated roof tiles stacked in the lower left foreground, next to a dark ceramic jar, a celadon bowl, trowels and brushes. The low stones at the start grow into the tall stone fortress wall on the left, lit by torches. Soldiers holding torches on top of the wall and archaeologists working in the trenches are gradually revealed as the camera rises, already in place, never appearing suddenly. Meanwhile the sun sinks lower, the golden light deepens step by step into rich orange sunset, and a soft purple tone spreads across the upper sky. As dusk falls, the white work lights at the site switch on one by one, gently. The camera smoothly decelerates as it reaches the final framing. End: high-angle wide view of an archaeological excavation site beside a torch-lit stone fortress wall with a traditional Korean gate pavilion and red banners on the left. Grid lines and strings mark the trenches, archaeologists work under white lights, a wide river winds to the right reflecting the sunset, the sun setting between mountains under an orange and purple sky, distant city lights along the river. Warm golden-orange palette maintained throughout, color deepening gradually with no sudden jump in color or brightness. One continuous camera move with smooth ease-in acceleration and ease-out deceleration, no jerky speed change. Cinematic, 35mm film look, soft film grain, photorealistic. hard cut, jump cut, white flash, fade to black, sudden color change, abrupt lighting change, people suddenly appearing, figures popping in, lights turning on all at once, tile morphing, object morphing, warping, jerky speed change, camera shake, distorted hands, extra fingers, face close-up, text, watermark\n\n[전환 6 · 발굴 현장 → 공산성 야경 (마지막 장면)]\nSeamless continuous shot, one unbroken camera movement from the first frame to the last frame. This is the final shot of the film, calm and majestic. Start: high-angle wide view at sunset of an archaeological excavation site beside a stone fortress wall lit by torches, a traditional Korean gate pavilion with red banners on the upper left. Excavated roof tiles, a dark ceramic jar, a celadon bowl, trowels and brushes in the foreground, archaeologists working under white lights in the trenches, a wide river winding on the right reflecting the orange sunset, the sun setting between the mountains on the upper right under an orange and purple sky. Phase 1: the camera begins to rise very slowly, then gradually accelerates as it cranes up and forward. The foreground artifacts, the trenches, the archaeologists with their white work lights, and the torch-bearing soldiers on the wall all naturally slide out of the bottom of the frame as the camera climbs, never disappearing on screen. The river stays on the right side of the frame. Phase 2: the camera pushes smoothly toward the setting sun, the fastest but still fluid part of the move. The warm glow of the sun grows larger and blooms softly until warm golden light fills the entire frame. Phase 3: the camera almost hovers inside the golden glow for a quiet moment, like a slow breath. Within the glow, the torch flames along the fortress wall become warm modern lamp lights in the same places. Phase 4: the glow slowly recedes as the sun sets behind the mountains. The sky deepens step by step from orange, to violet, to deep navy night. The camera smoothly decelerates while making a wide, graceful arc to the left and descending, until it looks down from high above on the same gate pavilion, now lit by warm golden lights. The fortress wall winds diagonally through the dark pine forest, lined with glowing lamps and red banners. The modern city lights and illuminated bridges shimmer along the river on the right, their reflections dancing on the water. End: high aerial night view of the illuminated Gongsanseong fortress: the stone wall glowing warm gold runs diagonally from the left toward the lower right, the gate pavilion with its arched gate in the center right, small pavilions on the grassy hilltop at the upper left, red banners along the wall, the wide river on the right reflecting the lights of the modern city and a long lit bridge, dark navy sky over layered mountains. The camera settles into a very slow, steady forward glide, lingering peacefully. Warm golden light is carried through the whole shot: from the setting sun, to the golden glow, to the fortress lights, with no sudden jump in color or brightness. One continuous camera move with smooth ease-in at the start, gentle acceleration toward the sun, a soft pause in the glow, and a long ease-out deceleration at the end, no jerky speed change. No people visible at the end. Cinematic aerial drone cinematography, 35mm film look, soft film grain, photorealistic. person suddenly disappearing, person vanishing, figures fading out, people in the final frame, hard cut, jump cut, white flash, burnt-out white glow, fade to black, sudden color change, abrupt lighting change, lights turning on all at once, river switching sides, gate pavilion morphing, warping, jerky speed change, sudden stop, camera shake, text, watermark.",
