    {
      "id": "sub-1790860421651-11",
      "submissionNumber": "DH-VID-012",
      "title": "찬란의 시대",
      "category": "VIDEO",
      "submitterName": "이원택",
      "participantCategory": "일반인",
      "submitterAffiliation": "모션그래픽 디자이너",
      "nationalHeritageName": "금동대향로",
      "baekjeRelated": "사용함",
      "description": "〈찬란의 시대〉는 백제 시대의 찬란한 황금 유물인 금동대향로가 단순한 공예품이 아니라, 사슴·용·봉황과 같은 영험한 신수들과 이상적인 세계관을 정교하게 담아낸 위대한 문화유산임을 표현한 영상입니다. 향로에 새겨진 신수의 세계가 실제로 살아 움직이는 듯한 장면을 통해, 백제인의 뛰어난 예술성과 상상력, 그리고 금동대향로에 담긴 신성하고 찬란한 가치를 보여주고자 했습니다.",
      "aiTools": [
        "Seedance 2.5"
      ],
      "postEditingUsage": "사용함",
      "postEditingDetails": "After effect",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "Create a cinematic photorealistic fantasy film inspired by the Baekje Gilt-bronze Incense Burner, visualizing the mythical sacred world carved into the artifact as if it truly existed.\n\nThe film should express the brilliance, spirituality, artistic imagination, and cultural sophistication of Baekje through a continuous journey connecting sacred mythical creatures, a celestial realm, an ancient Baekje city, and the Gilt-bronze Incense Burner.\n\nUse a realistic cinematic visual style rather than stylized fantasy illustration.\nMaintain consistent lighting, geography, scale, atmosphere, and visual continuity throughout the sequence.\n\nSCENE 1 — SACRED DEER\n\nBegin in a quiet ancient mountain forest at dawn.\n\nA sacred deer discovers a small piece of glowing golden ore hidden beneath grass and vegetation.\nThe deer approaches naturally and touches the golden object with its nose.\n\nAt the moment of contact, subtle sacred golden energy begins to flow through the deer’s antlers.\n\nThe light should feel ancient, mysterious, sacred, and restrained rather than magical or explosive.\n\nThe deer should move naturally like a real living animal, with subtle breathing, weight shifts, ear movement, blinking, and realistic interaction with the environment.\n\nThe forest, mountains, waterfalls, clouds, vegetation, and terrain must remain stable and physically believable.\n\n\nSCENE 2 — ASCENDING DRAGON\n\nThe camera gradually reveals a massive wingless Eastern dragon ascending from the mountain landscape toward the sky.\n\nThe dragon must look upward toward the direction of its ascent.\n\nIts head leads the movement while its long body continuously performs large, flowing S-shaped waves.\n\nThe dragon must never appear static, rigid, frozen, or simply translated upward as one solid object.\n\nThe full-body wave is the primary locomotion:\n\nhead leads upward\n→ neck follows\n→ wave travels through the chest\n→ continues through the torso\n→ reaches the rear body\n→ finally passes through the long tail.\n\nDifferent parts of the body should move with delayed inertia, giving the dragon believable mass and momentum.\n\nThe mane, beard, and whiskers respond naturally to airflow with delayed secondary motion.\n\nThe camera orbits around the ascending dragon, but the dragon does not turn to follow the camera.\nIt continues looking upward toward the open sky.\n\nSubtle golden energy travels through selected seams between the dragon’s scales, visually connecting it to the sacred energy previously seen in the deer’s antlers.\n\nAvoid excessive neon glow, electrical effects, or artificial magical energy.\n\n\nSCENE 3 — CLOUD TRANSITION AND PHOENIX\n\nThe camera continues its movement and enters a dense natural cloud layer.\n\nThe cloud progressively surrounds the camera until the frame becomes fully obscured.\n\nThis must feel like real physical travel through volumetric clouds, never a cut, dissolve, wipe, or morph.\n\nWhile the view is fully obscured, the dragon exits the visible scene.\n\nThe camera continues upward and emerges above the main cloud layer.\n\nReveal a high-altitude celestial realm above a vast sea of clouds.\n\nThe phoenix appears on the highest rocky summit.\n\nThe phoenix is an elegant ivory-white sacred bird with long flowing tail feathers.\n\nIt lands naturally on the rocky peak with realistic wingbeats, clear foot contact, weight transfer, folding wings, and subtle residual movement in the long tail feathers.\n\nThe phoenix must feel like a living creature rather than a rigid CG model.\n\nThe celestial terrain contains rocky mountain peaks, waterfalls, clouds, pink flowering trees and vegetation.\n\nThe environment should feel sacred, beautiful, vast, and natural.\n\nThere are no buildings in the celestial realm.\n\nThe dragon, phoenix, and deer are all part of the same sacred world represented by the imagery of the Baekje Gilt-bronze Incense Burner.\n\n\nSCENE 4 — DESCENT TO BAEKJE\n\nThe camera continues backward and downward through clouds, physically traveling from the celestial world into the earthly Baekje city.\n\nMaintain one continuous spatial world.\n\nDo not teleport or reset the environment.\n\nThe camera emerges into a vast and prosperous ancient Baekje city.\n\n\nSCENE 5 — LIVING BAEKJE CITY\n\nTravel continuously backward through a large, deep, inhabited Baekje city.\n\nShow successive streets, courtyards, bridges, waterways, markets, palace districts, ceremonial areas, craft districts, gates, and layered urban spaces.\n\nThe city must feel genuinely alive.\n\nPopulate the city with naturally moving inhabitants.\n\nPeople should walk in different directions, carry baskets and pottery, transport materials, cross bridges, enter and leave buildings, work, interact, talk, and continue their daily lives.\n\nDo not make people stand motionless like mannequins or wooden dolls.\n\nAvoid synchronized crowd movement and repetitive walking loops.\n\nThe city should feel peaceful, prosperous, active, and culturally rich.\n\nInclude clearly visible Baekje-inspired golden and gilt-bronze objects throughout the city:\n\ngolden lotus ornaments,\ngilt-bronze ceremonial objects,\ncrown-inspired decorative motifs,\ngolden fittings,\nceremonial vessels,\nmetal craft objects,\nornamental details,\nand precious objects.\n\nDo not turn the entire city into gold.\n\nArchitecture should remain realistic timber, stone, plaster, and gray tiled roofs, while refined golden cultural elements appear throughout the journey and catch the warm sunlight.\n\nThe visual impression should communicate the brilliance and prosperity of Baekje.\n\n\nSCENE 6 — GILT-BRONZE INCENSE BURNER\n\nContinue moving backward and rise toward a sacred terrace.\n\nReveal the Baekje Gilt-bronze Incense Burner as the dominant foreground object.\n\nPreserve its recognizable form:\n\nlotus-shaped bowl,\nmountain-shaped lid,\nphoenix finial,\ndragon support,\nand intricate gilt-bronze craftsmanship.\n\nThe incense burner is stationary and monumental.\n\n\nSMOKE CONNECTION\n\nFine translucent incense smoke continuously emerges from the vents of the incense burner.\n\nThe smoke forms one continuous visual connection:\n\nincense burner\n→ thin rising smoke\n→ flowing translucent ribbons\n→ broader atmospheric vapor\n→ cloud layer\n→ celestial realm.\n\nThe smoke must never appear as disconnected patches.\n\nThe viewer should clearly understand that the celestial realm of the sacred creatures and the Gilt-bronze Incense Burner are connected through this continuous incense smoke.\n\nThe smoke should move organically with subtle turbulence and changing thickness.\n\nAvoid making it look like a cable, tube, laser, solid ribbon, or artificial energy beam.\n\n\nFINAL HERO SHOT\n\nMove the camera toward the Gilt-bronze Incense Burner while maintaining the established camera movement and perspective.\n\nThe floating celestial terrain in the background must behave as a real three-dimensional environment with proper parallax.\n\nIt must not behave like a flat background image, billboard, or projected matte.\n\nNear cliffs should shift more than distant peaks.\nMountain layers should naturally occlude one another.\nThe silhouette of the celestial terrain should change according to camera perspective.\n\nAt the final moment, visually isolate the Gilt-bronze Incense Burner as the hero object.\n\nThe surrounding city, terrace, sky, clouds, mountains, celestial realm, and foreground distractions gradually recede into darkness.\n\nThe Gilt-bronze Incense Burner remains visible the longest, illuminated with restrained warm golden light.\n\nEnd with the Baekje Gilt-bronze Incense Burner isolated as the final symbol of the entire journey.\n\n\nOVERALL VISUAL DIRECTION\n\nPhotorealistic cinematic fantasy.\nHigh-end historical cultural film.\nNatural camera movement.\nRealistic materials.\nSoft champagne-gold dawn light.\nBlue-gray and lavender atmospheric depth.\nSubtle warm gold highlights.\nPink flowering vegetation in the celestial realm.\nIvory sacred creatures.\nNatural volumetric clouds.\nRealistic atmospheric perspective.\n\nAvoid excessive saturation, artificial HDR, plastic surfaces, repeated AI-generated patterns, identical vegetation clusters, cotton-like clouds, excessive bloom, exaggerated fantasy colors, and overly decorative imagery.\n\nThe final film should express that the Baekje Gilt-bronze Incense Burner is not merely an ancient object, but an extraordinary cultural heritage containing a rich sacred world of mythical creatures, nature, spirituality, and the brilliant imagination of Baekje.",
