      "fullPrompt": "S1 시작 프레임 (K1b) | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 참조: 스토리보드 S1\nCinematic 16:9 keyframe, the opening frame of a film. Use the reference image for the world, wardrobe, lighting and mood, but this is the moment BEFORE the discovery. Korea, July 1971, heavy summer monsoon rain at night on a grassy royal burial mound hillside in Gongju. Low handheld medium-wide shot from inside the edge of a muddy drainage trench looking along it: two Korean labourers in their 40s in worn olive-drab rubber rain ponchos and frayed straw hats, faces mostly hidden under the hat brims, one driving a steel shovel into the wet clay, the other crouched holding a battered tungsten flashlight aimed at the trench wall. The trench wall is still ALL mud and clay, only a tiny corner of an old dark brick barely visible in the flashlight spot. Grass-covered mound rising behind them against a dark rainy sky, a kerosene hurricane lantern on a wooden stake. Only light: warm tungsten flashlight and kerosene lantern, rain streaks backlit, puddles reflecting light. Shot on 16mm Kodak 7247, Arriflex 16SR, visible grain, slight halation, muted desaturated colors, realistic weathered hands, documentary realism, no HDR, not oversaturated, no text.\nS1 시작 프레임 보정 | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 편집\nEdit the reference image. Keep EVERYTHING identical: composition, camera angle, both labourers and their poses, straw hats, shovel, flashlight, trench, the small brick corner in the flashlight spot, lantern, mound, rain, lighting and color grade. Change ONLY the surface of the rain ponchos and the droplets: the ponchos are matte, thick, worn olive rubber with a wet oily sheen and water running down in streaks and a few natural drips at the edges, NOT covered in hundreds of glittering beads or sequin-like sparkles. Reduce the sparkly droplets on the straw hats and grass too, so the wetness looks like real 16mm film footage in rain: soft specular sheen, not glitter. Keep the 16mm grain and muted colors.\nS1 끝 프레임 | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 참조: S1 시작 프레임, 무령왕릉 내부 벽돌 사진\nThe final frame of a slow handheld push-in that started on the first reference image: the camera has moved into a tight close-up of the trench wall exactly where the flashlight was pointing. Same night, same rain, same warm tungsten flashlight coming from the LEFT side of frame, same muddy clay, same 16mm Kodak grain and muted color grade. Now the wet mud has just been wiped away by hand, revealing a rectangular patch about 60 cm wide of ancient Baekje tomb brickwork, built exactly like the second reference photo: small dark grey-brown bricks laid in four horizontal courses then one course of upright bricks, their faces stamped with lotus flower and lozenge relief patterns, still partly smeared with wet clay and streaked with rainwater. At the left edge of frame, the labourer's weathered muddy hand in a wet olive rubber poncho sleeve rests on the bricks; the flashlight in his other hand is just visible at frame left edge, its beam raking across the brick patterns so the reliefs cast tiny shadows. Mud crumbs falling, rain drops hitting the bricks. Shallow depth of field, realistic, not glittery, no text.\nS2 끝 프레임 | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 편집 (S1 영상 마지막 프레임)\nEdit this exact image. Keep the camera framing IDENTICAL (same position, same zoom, same crop - no push-in, no reframing), and keep every brick, pattern, clay smear, mud, rain streak, color and grain exactly where it is. Make only these changes: 1. In the FIRST flat horizontal course (directly beneath the top row of upright bricks, where the labourer's fingertips currently touch), remove the TWO LEFTMOST bricks only; where they were, there is now one dark rectangular hole with crumbled wet clay on its lower lip. Every other brick stays exactly in place. 2. Remove the labourer's bare muddy hand; the wet olive poncho sleeve pulls back toward the left edge so the hole is fully visible. 3. The flashlight stays at the same spot at the left edge, and its warm beam now points into the hole: a thin visible shaft of light with fine dust particles drifting out. No text.\nS3 무덤 내부 (스토리보드 → 고증 수정) | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 참조: 진묘수·무덤 내부 복원 모형 사진\nRecreate the first reference image (a dark tunnel-vaulted brick tomb passage lit by a single flashlight beam from the left, dust in the air) keeping its composition, but correct it for historical accuracy of the Tomb of King Muryeong (Baekje, 525 AD): replace the statue with the real stone guardian beast (jinmyosu) exactly as in the second reference photo: a squat, low, horizontally long body, short thick legs, a blunt protruding snout, flame/wing-shaped relief swirls on its flanks, and a small branching iron horn like a twig of antler on top of its head, facing toward the camera. The walls and barrel vault built like the reference photos: small dark bricks laid in four horizontal courses then one course of upright bricks, stamped with lotus and lozenge relief patterns; small pointed peach-shaped wall niches. On the floor in front of the beast, two flat, nearly square granite slabs lying flat (the epitaph stones), with a small pile of ancient bronze coins on one slab. 16mm film grain, muted desaturated tones, volumetric dusty beam, photorealistic, no text.\nS3 끝 프레임 | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 편집\nEdit this exact image. Keep the camera framing IDENTICAL, and keep the tunnel-vaulted brick passage, every brick and its relief pattern, the stone guardian beast, the two flat stone slabs with the pile of coins, and the floor exactly where they are. Change only: 1. The light beam: a warm 3200K tungsten flashlight beam entering from the same upper-left point, angled downward so it lands on the beast's face and chest, with soft spill across the two slabs; fine dust floating in the beam. 2. Only surfaces touched by the beam are lit; the rest falls into deep darkness; bricks are plain stone-brown with NO golden glow. 3. Each small pointed wall niche holds one small, empty, unlit white porcelain oil-lamp cup. Photoreal, 16mm film grain, muted tones. No text.\nS3 시작 프레임 | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 편집 (S3 끝 프레임)\nEdit this exact image. Keep the camera framing IDENTICAL and keep every object exactly in place and unchanged in shape. Change ONLY the lighting, to the moment a few seconds earlier: the warm flashlight beam enters from the same upper-left point but lights only a small oval patch of bricks in the upper-left corner, not reaching the beast, the slabs, or the floor. Everything else is in near-total darkness; the beast, the slabs and the niches remain barely perceptible as very dim silhouettes at about 5 percent brightness. No golden glow on any brick. Photoreal, 16mm film grain. No text.\nS4 지석 (글자 없는 판석) | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 참조: S3 끝 프레임, 무령왕 지석 사진\nCinematic 16:9 close-up inside a dark 6th-century Baekje brick tomb passage in 1971. Subject: a single flat epitaph stone slab lying flat on the dusty earthen floor, seen from about 60 degrees above, filling roughly 85 percent of the frame. The slab is modeled on the second reference photo: a slightly wider-than-tall slab of grey-green granite with fine speckled grain, chipped rounded edges, faint reddish rust stains along its right edge, one small round drilled hole near the center. Its face has a thin incised border line and six thin vertical ruling lines. The face is COMPLETELY BLANK between the lines: no characters, no letters, no symbols. A thin layer of pale 1400-year-old dust. A single warm 3200K flashlight beam enters low from the upper-left corner, raking across the surface. Photoreal, 16mm film grain, muted desaturated tones. No text anywhere.\n※ 명문 52자(寧東大將軍百濟斯麻王年六十二歲癸卯年五月丙戌朔七日壬辰崩到乙巳年八月癸酉朔十二日甲申安厝登冠大墓立志如左)는 AI로 생성하지 않고 후반 작업에서 서체로 음각 합성함.\nS5-1 끝 프레임 (525년) | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 편집 (S3 끝 프레임)\nEdit this exact image. Keep the camera framing IDENTICAL and keep every object in exactly the same place, size and shape. Change the moment to the year 525, the night of the funeral, when the tomb was new: 1. Remove the flashlight beam completely. 2. Each small white porcelain cup in the four wall niches now holds a small burning oil-lamp flame; these flames are the ONLY light, warm 1800K amber. 3. Everything is brand new and clean: crisp bricks and reliefs, no dust, smooth swept floor, freshly carved pale granite beast, clean slabs, bright bronze coins. Photoreal, natural film grain, restrained warm color, deep shadows. No text.\nS5-2 끝 프레임 (관이 닫힌 상태) | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 참조: 무령왕 목관 사진\nCinematic 16:9 film still in a Baekje brick burial chamber lit by oil lamps, three-quarter side view: a long black-lacquered wooden coffin on a low brick platform runs horizontally across the frame; its steep gabled roof-shaped lid with rows of small gilt nail heads and a clear ridge line is fully CLOSED, flush with both ends of the box; gilt-bronze ring handles. Behind the coffin stand two mourners in plain undyed hemp robes with topknots, heads deeply bowed so their faces are hidden, backlit silhouettes, both hands resting flat on the lid. Only small 1800K oil-lamp flames in peach-shaped niches; glossy highlights on the lacquer, deep shadows. Photoreal, natural film grain. No text.\nS5-2 시작 프레임 (뚜껑이 열린 상태) | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 편집\n(끝 프레임의 뚜껑을 후반 작업에서 왼쪽으로 평행 이동해 합성한 이미지를 바탕으로) Edit this exact image. Keep the camera framing IDENTICAL and keep the chamber, lamps, platform, the coffin box, the shifted gabled lid, the open right section with the gold flame-shaped crown ornaments inside, and the mourners' standing positions exactly as they are. Change ONLY the two mourners' upper bodies, arms and heads, to the moment they start pushing the lid closed: both lean to screen left and stretch both arms out, gripping the far top edge of the lid, shoulders braced; faces stay in dark shadow. No text.\nS6 현재의 왕릉원 | GPT Image 2.5 (Higgsfield), high / 2K / 16:9 / 참조: 커먼즈 현장 사진 2장\nCinematic 16:9 photograph of the real Royal Tombs of King Muryeong in Gongju, Korea, today, modeled closely on the first reference photo: a group of adjoining, smooth, grass-covered round burial mounds on a gentle hillside, a low curb of grey dressed stones along their base, a paved walking path curving in front, and Korean red pines behind. At the lower right, the small stone doorway of the King Muryeong tomb entrance. Remove all modern signs. Late September, just after sunrise: thin low morning mist in the hollows, the sun rising behind the pines at upper left with soft golden shafts; dew on the grass. In the far distance one small person walks away on the path. Low camera about 50 cm above the grass, 35mm-equivalent lens. Photoreal, natural color, not oversaturated, no HDR look. No text.\n2. 영상\nS1 발견 (8초) | Seedance 2.5 (Higgsfield), omni_reference / 720p / 16:9 / 시작·끝 프레임 고정\nSCENE CONTEXT: Korea, July 1971, night, heavy monsoon rain on a grassy royal burial-mound hillside. Two labourers dig a narrow drainage trench cut into the mound and uncover ancient brickwork hidden in the clay.\nFORMAT: One continuous shot. OPTICS: medium-wide 63° to close-up 29° through a continuous push-in.\nCAMERA: Handheld, low at trench height, slow steady push-in toward the flashlight spot at about 1 km/h, gentle breathing sway.\nACTION: 0.0–2.5s Labourer A drives the shovel into the clay near the wall; the blade stops dead with a hard jolt. 2.5–5.0s Labourer B leans in and sweeps wet mud away from the brick corner with his bare palm in three firm strokes. 5.0–8.0s The camera arrives on the wall as more brick faces appear; stamped lotus reliefs catch the raking flashlight beam. Settles exactly on the end frame.\nLIGHTING: warm 3200K tungsten flashlight from frame left and a kerosene lantern backlighting the rain.\nSTYLE: Photoreal 1970s documentary footage on 16mm film, visible grain, slight halation, muted earth tones.\nS2 틈 (7초) | Seedance 2.5 (Higgsfield), omni_reference / 720p / 16:9 / 시작 = S1 마지막 프레임\nSCENE CONTEXT: Korea, July 1971, rainy night, inside a muddy drainage trench. A labourer pulls one old brick out of an ancient brick wall, the wet clay beside it collapses, and a dark hole opens into a sealed chamber.\nFORMAT: One continuous shot. OPTICS: Fixed close-up at 47° FOV. CAMERA: Locked off, completely static.\nACTION: 0.0–3.0s The right hand digs its fingertips around the leftmost brick of the first flat course, rocks it twice, and draws it straight out toward frame left; the soft wet clay beside it slumps down. 3.0–4.0s The hand carries the brick out of frame. 4.0–7.0s The flashlight tilts to aim into the hole; a thin shaft of warm light enters the darkness and a slow wisp of fine dust drifts out.\nPHYSICS: The brick is one heavy solid block; all other bricks remain perfectly fixed.\nSTYLE: Photoreal 1970s documentary footage on 16mm film.\nS3 진묘수 (10초) | Seedance 2.5 (Higgsfield), omni_reference / 720p / 16:9 / 시작·끝 프레임 고정\nSCENE CONTEXT: Inside a sealed 6th-century Baekje royal tomb passage, discovered in 1971. A flashlight beam shines in through a small hole high on the upper left and slowly searches the darkness until it finds a stone guardian beast.\nFORMAT: One continuous shot. OPTICS: Fixed wide shot at 63° FOV. CAMERA: Locked off on a tripod.\nACTION: Only the light moves. 0.0–4.0s The beam slides along the upper-left wall and vault, raking across the relief bricks. 4.0–7.0s It tilts down onto the two stone slabs; the coins catch small glints. 7.0–10.0s It rises up the beast's front legs to its face and stops; the carved face emerges from the dark.\nAUDIO/STYLE: sealed chamber room tone; photoreal 16mm, muted stone-brown tones.\n※ 연꽃무늬 벽돌의 금빛은 후반 작업에서 합성.\nS5-1 시간의 역행 (7초) | Seedance 2.5 (Higgsfield), omni_reference / 720p / 16:9 / 시작·끝 프레임 고정\nSCENE CONTEXT: Inside a Baekje royal tomb passage. Time flows backward from 1971 to the night of the funeral in 525: the flashlight goes out, small oil lamps in the wall niches light up one by one, and the dust of centuries clears to reveal the tomb as it was when new.\nFORMAT: One continuous shot. OPTICS: Fixed wide shot 63°. CAMERA: Locked off.\nACTION: Every object stays still; only light and surface state change. 0.0–1.5s The flashlight beam flickers once and goes out. 1.5–4.5s The four niche lamps ignite one at a time. 4.5–7.0s Under the steady lamplight the dust fades away like mist clearing; the tomb becomes clean and new.\nLIGHTING: flashlight, then only four small 1800K oil-lamp flames.\nS5-2 봉인 (7초) | Seedance 2.5 (Higgsfield), omni_reference / 720p / 16:9 / 시작·끝 프레임 고정\nSCENE CONTEXT: The night of a Baekje royal funeral in 525, inside a brick burial chamber lit by small oil lamps. Two mourners push the heavy gabled lid of the king's coffin closed with their own hands, then bow.\nFORMAT: One continuous shot. OPTICS: Fixed medium-wide 47°. CAMERA: Locked off.\nACTION: 0.0–5.0s The two mourners push the lid toward screen-right with visible effort, shifting their weight; their hands stay gripping the lid's top edge and travel with it. The lid, one rigid solid piece, slides steadily right at about 0.3 km/h and covers the gold ornaments; the last glint of gold disappears. 5.0–7.0s They straighten, rest their palms flat on the lid, and slowly bow their heads.\nPHYSICS: The lid moves only because the mourners push it, as a single rigid body.\nSTYLE: Photoreal, natural film grain, restrained warm color.\nS6 오늘 (8초) | Seedance 2.5 (Higgsfield), omni_reference / 720p / 16:9 / 시작 프레임\nSCENE CONTEXT: Present day, just after sunrise in late September, at the Royal Tombs of King Muryeong in Gongju, Korea. Quiet morning mist over grass-covered burial mounds; one distant walker on the path.\nFORMAT: One continuous shot. OPTICS: 63° FOV, deep focus.\nCAMERA: A slow, smooth crane move over the full 8 seconds while the mounds stay centered.\nACTION: Mist drifts slowly through the hollows between the mounds; the small walker continues along the path away from the camera; sun shafts through the pines shimmer faintly in the mist.\nLIGHTING: Low warm sunrise from upper left behind the pines.\nSTYLE: Photoreal present-day cinematic footage, natural color, restrained saturation.\n3. 효과음·환경음\n비 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 22s\nHeavy steady summer monsoon rain at night on a grassy hillside, dense rainfall on grass and wet mud, water trickling in a muddy ditch, raindrops tapping on thick rubber rain ponchos, close and immersive, field recording, no thunder, no music, no voices\n삽 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 3s\nA steel shovel digging into wet heavy clay twice, then striking a buried brick with a hard dull stony thud, close foley, no music\n진흙 쓸기 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 3s\nA bare hand wiping thick wet mud off a brick wall in three slow firm strokes, squelching clay, clumps of mud dropping into a puddle, close foley, no music\n벽돌 빼기 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 3s\nAn old brick being wiggled loose and dragged out of a wall, gritty stone scraping friction, sandy mortar crumbling and trickling down, close foley, no music\n공기 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 5s\nA sealed ancient chamber opening: a slow hollow rush of stale air breathing out through a small hole, deep low resonance, fine dust hissing, eerie and quiet, no music\n무덤 룸톤 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 22s\nRoom tone inside a sealed underground brick tomb: very low deep hollow drone, subtle reverberant air, faint settling dust, extremely distant muffled rain far above, dark and still, no music, no melody\n저음 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 4s\nA single deep soft cinematic sub boom with a long dark reverberant tail, like a stone resonance in a vault, no melody, no music\n돌 긁힘 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 4s\nVery soft fine grit and dust brushing over an engraved stone slab, delicate scratchy texture, quiet, close, no music\n손전등 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 1s\nAn old metal 1970s flashlight switch clicking off, a single mechanical click, close, dry, no music\n등잔 점화 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 1.5s\nA small oil lamp wick igniting: a soft breathy whoosh and a gentle flame catching, quiet, close, no music\n등잔 불꽃 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 16s\nSeveral small oil lamp flames burning quietly in a stone chamber, soft gentle flicker and faint crackle, calm warm stillness, no music, no voices\n관 뚜껑 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 5s\nA heavy lacquered wooden coffin lid being pushed and sliding slowly along wooden rails for three seconds, low continuous wooden scrape with rustle of hemp cloth, then a solid soft wooden knock as it seats closed, close foley, no music\n전환 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 3s\nA soft airy rising wind swell brightening into open air, gentle whoosh, ethereal but natural, no music, no melody\n새벽 | ElevenLabs Sound Effects (Comfy Cloud) / 16s\nEarly morning in a quiet Korean pine forest park at sunrise: gentle birdsong from a few small birds, soft breeze through pine needles, very faint distant footsteps on a paved path, peaceful, field recording, no music, no voices",
