      "fullPrompt": "스타일 접미어와 네거티브\n스타일 접미어 (모든 이미지 프롬프트에 부착)\ncinematic still, Korean traditional Buddhist temple aesthetic, natural volumetric light,\nshallow depth of field, rich but muted color grading, 16:9 horizontal composition,\nultra detailed, 4K\n\n영상 네거티브\n네거티브를 별도로 기술한 것은 A-6 신중도 한 컷뿐입니다. 벽화가 입체로 변형되거나 화면에\n글자가 생성되는 것을 막기 위해 붙였고, 나머지 컷은 프롬프트 본문에서 카메라 움직임을 직접\n제한했습니다.\nNo camera shake. No image blurring. No text generation for images, original image retained\n\n컷별 이미지 생성 프롬프트\n\nA-1 태화산 새벽 부감\nAerial view at dawn of a Korean Buddhist mountain temple complex nestled in a forested\nvalley, a winding stream curving in a taegeuk S-shape around the temple grounds, thick\nlow-lying morning mist drifting between dark pine ridges, silhouette of a five-story stone\npagoda and a tiled hipped-and-gabled temple hall emerging from the fog, cold blue-grey dawn\nlight with a faint warm glow on the eastern ridge, autumn forest colors\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n참고 자료 마곡사 항공 사진 1 장을 참조 이미지로 투입해, 마곡천이 태극 모양으로 절을\n휘감아 도는 고유 지형과 전각 배치를 반영했습니다.\n이 컷의 결과물을 이후 전 컷의 스타일 참조 이미지로 투입해 톤을 통일했습니다.\n\nA-2 극락교와 범종루\nA three-arched stone bridge (Geungnakgyo) at a Korean Buddhist temple, low carved stone\nbalustrade with round finial posts along the deck, the bridge crossing a still reflective\npond, beyond the bridge stands an ornately detailed two-story Korean bell pavilion\n(beomjongnu) with a distinctive cross-shaped roof formed by two intersecting hip-and-gable\nridgelines meeting at a central peak, four gracefully upturned eave corners, richly layered\nteal-green dancheong with red accents and intricate gold floral and cloud filigree covering\nevery beam, bracket and rafter end, deep red lacquered columns, a wooden sign reading\n'梵鐘樓' mounted beneath the corner eave, a white stone balustrade with round finial posts\naround its elevated platform.\nInside, each ritual instrument occupies its own bay: in one front corner bay, a large\nbarrel-shaped drum (beopgo) rests horizontally on a low wooden stand, its round end facing\nthe viewer painted with a vivid taegeuk-inspired multicolor radial pattern of blue, red,\nyellow and white, its wooden barrel painted with a blue dragon winding through clouds; in\nthe center-rear bay, a large dark bronze temple bell (beomjong) hangs vertically from a\nthick crossbeam via an ornate carved wooden dragon-shaped hanger gripping the bell's top\nloop; in an adjacent side bay, a round flat bronze gong plate (cheongdong banja) with a\ngently domed center boss hangs flat and vertical from its own wooden frame, its surface\nplain and unpatterned.\nBare wintry tree branches frame the scene from above, the entire bridge and pavilion\nmirrored perfectly in the calm glassy water below, thin morning mist drifting low over the\nwater, cold blue-grey dawn light with a faint warm glow, muted desaturated color grading,\ntranquil and meditative atmosphere\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n참고 자료 극락교와 범종루는 공공 자료에 실린 사진만으로는 형태를 파악하기 어려워,\n인터넷 검색으로 정면·측면·내부 등 각 각도별 장면을 캡처해 함께 참조했습니다.\n이렇게 확보한 자료와 국가유산포털·한국민족문화대백과사전의 마곡사 범종루 사진을\n5 회 대조하며 수정했습니다. 현판 표기를 梵鐘閣 → 梵鍾樓 → 梵鐘樓로 정정, 십자형\n이중 지붕 반영, 법고·범종·청동반자를 각각 다른 칸에 배치, 법고 북면을 태극 문양으로\n수정, 청동반자를 무늬 없는 민무늬 원판으로 정정.\n\nA-3 대광보전 외부와 편액\n두 가지 화각을 모두 생성해 편집본에 함께 사용했습니다.\n① 클로즈업 — 공포와 용두 세부\nClose-up of the ornate wooden bracket system (gongpo) and painted eaves of an old Korean\nBuddhist temple hall, faded dancheong polychrome patterns in green, red, blue and gold on\naged timber, a dark lacquered signboard with bold white calligraphy reading '大光寶殿'\nhanging beneath the eave, two carved wooden dragon heads protruding from the corner brackets\non either side of the signboard, each dragon biting a small orb, low warm sunlight raking\nacross the weathered wood grain, deep shadows between the brackets\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n② 와이드 — 전각 정면\nA slightly wider view of a Korean Buddhist temple hall's front facade, ornate multi-tiered\nwooden bracket system (dapo gongpo) beneath a black tiled eave, weathered dancheong\npolychrome patterns in faded green, red and gold, a dark lacquered signboard with a\nred-and-gold border and bold white calligraphy reading '大光寶殿' hanging just below the\neave, two fierce carved wooden dragon-head brackets (yongdu) with pale curved horns,\nbulging eyes and bared teeth flanking the signboard on the corner pillars, patterned wooden\ndiamond-lattice doors below the eave line, warm low-angle sunlight raking across the\nweathered wood grain, clear blue sky visible above the roofline, deep shadows between the\nbrackets, aged and weathered wood texture\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n참고 자료 국가유산포털과 한국민족문화대백과사전의 마곡사 대광보전 사진을 참조해\n편액 서체, 다포식 공포 구조, 용두 장식을 고증했습니다.\nA-4 대광보전 법당 내부\nInterior of an old Korean Buddhist temple hall (Daegwangbojeon), a large golden seated\nBuddha statue on an ornate multi-tiered altar, hands folded together at the chest in a\nprayer mudra, an elaborately painted red-and-green mural filled with rows of small haloed\nbuddhas and bodhisattvas hanging on the wall directly behind the statue, above stretches a\nheavily painted wooden beam carved and painted like a great sinuous dragon winding across\nthe ceiling, richly patterned dancheong ceiling coffers in green, red and gold, rows of\nsmall orange prayer-tag racks in glass-fronted cabinets flanking the altar, a tall tower of\nstacked pink and white paper lotus lanterns standing beside the altar, woven straw floor\nmats, brass candlesticks and offering bowls arranged in front of the statue, dim warm\ninterior lit by soft daylight filtering in from latticed wooden doors on the left, faint\nincense haze in the air\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n참고 자료 국가유산포털과 한국민족문화대백과사전의 대광보전 내부 사진을 참조해 용\n그림 대들보·연등탑·축원함·삿자리 바닥 등 실제 내부 요소를 반영했습니다.\nA-5 사천왕도 — 대광보전 외벽\n방식 대광보전 외벽 사천왕도 실사 사진 2 장을 참조 이미지로 투입한 상태에서, 네 존상의 지물·\n자세·복색과 배경·상하 구조를 하나씩 문장으로 옮긴 장문 묘사 프롬프트를 적용\nAn authentic traditional Korean Buddhist temple mural in a flat, naive folk-painting style\n(minhwa-influenced Buddhist wall painting), painted directly onto four separate vertical\nwooden wall panels divided by exposed wooden posts, on the exterior wall of a temple hall.\nPale flat mint-green background with almost no shading or gradient, thick bold black outline\nlinework throughout, minimal modeling on the pale pink-toned skin. Four Heavenly King\nguardian figures (Sacheonwang), each confined to his own panel: leftmost figure stands with\nboth arms crossed over a bare muscular chest, hands tucked in, wearing a red-and-green\npatterned lower skirt with a white underskirt showing beneath; second figure holds a\nstraight sword pointing down at his side with one hand, wears a reddish-brown skirt with a\nwhite sash draped over one shoulder; third figure raises a curved glaive-like sword\ndiagonally overhead with one hand while the other hand grips a small coiled black serpent,\nwears a green apron-skirt; fourth (rightmost) figure holds one palm raised open near his\nchest while his other hand rests near a sword hilt at his hip, wears a blue patterned skirt\nwith a red sash. Every figure shares the same distinctive iconographic feature: a wide\nribbon of solid blue fabric that loops into a large circular spiral above and beside the\nhead like a giant flat ribbon knot, then trails down along the body in flowing curved bands.\nFierce grimacing faces with thick eyebrows, bulging round eyes, and small flame-like tufts\nof orange-red hair. Above the panels, a densely painted wooden architrave beam with\ngeometric brocade lattice medallions and a small painted bird or dragon roundel at the\ncenter. Below the panels, an exposed unpainted wooden crossbeam. Weathered, slightly faded\npigment with fine age cracking, flat frontal composition, no dramatic lighting, even soft\ndaylight, documentary photograph of an existing temple mural, ultra detailed, 4K\n참고 자료 및 프롬프트 설계 근거 짧은 텍스트 묘사로는 지물·자세·채색이 실물과 계속\n어긋나, 공공 자료의 실사 사진을 참조 이미지로 투입하고 네 존상을 한 명씩 개별\n기술하는 방식으로 다시 썼습니다. 왼쪽부터 팔짱·직도·언월도와 뱀·손바닥으로 지물을\n각각 지정하고, 청색 리본 고리의 형태, 민화풍 평면 채색, 민트빛 배경, 상부 창방의 금문\n단청과 하부 노출 가로보까지 문장으로 고정했습니다. 앞선 두 차례의 짧은 프롬프트와\n달리 이 프롬프트에서 실물과 일치하는 결과가 나왔습니다.\n\nA-6 신중도 — 대광보전 내부벽\n방식 국가유산포털·한국민족문화대백과사전의 대광보전 신중도 사진을 참조 이미지로 병행 투입\nA large traditional Korean Buddhist guardian deity painting (Shinjungdo) on the temple's\ninterior wall, featuring a serene central figure in pale colors wearing a splendid red and\ngold crown beneath a blue-green and gold fan-shaped halo; dozens of bearded Deva generals\nand heavenly kings stand on either side, clad in teal and brown armor with red and gold\nornamentation, holding spears, halberds, and weapons, while some wear feathered helmets. A\ndeep navy blue night sky background with a faint golden cloud pattern, showing wear and fine\ncracks due to aged mineral pigments, a red panel along the lower edge, and intense side\nlighting from a single candle below\n<p>\nThe caution illustration must be implemented identically to the reference image\n<p>\nCinematic still images, aesthetics of traditional Korean Buddhist temples, natural\nvolumetric lighting, shallow depth of field, rich yet restrained color grading, 16:9\nhorizontal aspect ratio, ultra-high resolution, 4K\n부분 수정 (Talk 기능)\n프롬프트만으로는 실제 신중도와 무관한 불화가 계속 임의로 생성되어, 국가유산포털과\n한국민족문화대백과사전의 대광보전 신중도 실제 사진을 다시 첨부한 뒤 해당 영역만 교체하는\n방식으로 수정했습니다.\n가운데 신중도 그림 이걸로 대체하기\n좌우에 있는 불화 디자인을 레퍼런스 이미지에 있는 불화로 바꿔줘\n\nA-7 괘불과 연꽃 — 클라이맥스\nAn enormous Korean Buddhist hanging scroll painting (gwaebul) unfurled outdoors in a temple\ncourtyard, towering vertical banner showing a standing Shakyamuni Buddha with an elaborate\njeweled crown holding a single lotus flower raised in one hand, surrounded by densely packed\nbodhisattvas, arhats and guardian kings in red and green robes, gold halo rings, the scroll\nsuspended from a tall wooden pole, monks and lay people gathered small at its base, bright\nclear daylight, dramatic scale\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n참고 자료 보물 제 1260 호 마곡사 석가모니불 괘불탱의 실제 사진을 참조 이미지로\n투입해 제작했습니다. 연꽃을 든 석가모니 도상, 보관 형태, 권속 배치를 실물대로\n반영했습니다.\n\nA-8 연꽃에서 만다라로\nA single luminous lotus flower at the center of frame dissolving into countless drifting\nparticles of golden light, the particles arranging themselves into a vast concentric mandala\nstructure — nested circles and squares, four cardinal gates rendered as Korean temple gate\nsilhouettes, dancheong obangsaek five-direction colors of blue, red, yellow, white and\nblack, radial sacred geometry, deep dark background, glowing linework, contemporary digital\nart reinterpretation of Korean Buddhist iconography\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n참고 자료 및 생성 방식 만다라를 새로 그린 것이 아니라, 보물 제 1260 호 마곡사\n석가모니불 괘불탱의 실제 사진을 참조 이미지로 투입한 상태에서 위 프롬프트를\n적용했습니다. 그 결과 괘불의 본존과 권속이 그대로 남은 채 배경과 후광만 동심원\n만다라로 재구성되어, 앞 컷의 괘불이 만다라로 변해가는 연결이 성립합니다.\n단청의 오방색(동청·서백·남적·북흑·중황)과 밀교 만다라의 오방불 색채 체계가 '\n방위에 색을 대응시킨다'는 동일한 우주관에서 비롯되었다는 점을 시각적 연결 고리로\n삼았습니다.\n\nA-9 대웅보전 내부\nWide interior shot of a quiet Korean temple hall from behind, a single seated figure in\nplain grey robes seen from the back kneeling before the golden Buddha altar, warm afternoon\nlight streaming through latticed paper doors casting long geometric shadows across the woven\nfloor mats, dust suspended in the light, deeply peaceful and still, muted warm tones\n＋ 스타일 접미어\n참고 자료 마곡사 대웅보전 내부 사진을 검색해 참조 이미지로 투입, 삼세불 배치와 연등\n·창살 빛이 드는 실제 내부 구조를 반영했습니다.\n\n\n씬별 영상 프롬프트\n\n컷 이미지 한 장에서 그 컷 안의 카메라 이동과 화면 내 움직임만 생성한 프롬프트입니다. A-8 은\n별도의 씬 영상 없이 앞뒤 두 트랜지션으로만 구성했습니다.\n\nA-1 태화산 부감 — 안개 속 하강\nLeaping slowly through the air toward the employee, the camera moves smoothly forward and\ndownward through the layer of mist. The mist slowly flows across the screen. The surface of\nthe city sparkles faintly. It's a very slow and meditative pace. No cuts, no zoom snaps.\nApply as-is without changing the elements shown in the reference image\n\nA-2 극락교와 범종루 — 수면 접근\nCamera glides slowly forward at near water-level toward the bridge, low angle, the\nreflection of the bridge and richly detailed bell pavilion staying perfectly still and\nsymmetric, the silhouette of the taegeuk drum, the bronze bell with its carved dragon\nhanger, and the flat banja plate each clearly visible in their own bay in the reflection. A\nsingle gentle ripple crosses the water once, briefly distorting the mirrored image, then the\nsurface settles back to glass-like stillness. Bare branches overhead sway almost\nimperceptibly. Slow, meditative pace, no cuts.\n\n연출 의도 반영이 흔들리지 않아야 다음 컷에서 수면이 실제 처마로 솟아오르는\n매치컷이 성립하므로, 물결을 단 한 번만 지나가게 하고 다시 거울처럼 가라앉게\n지시했습니다.\n\nA-3 대광보전 편액 — 틸트업\nCamera tilts upward slowly from the pillar to the signboard and eaves. As it rises, the\nfaded dancheong pigments gradually saturate and restore to vivid original color, as if time\nreverses. Dust motes float in the light beam. Smooth continuous tilt, no cut.\n\n연출 의도 기둥에서 편액으로 올라가는 동안 바랜 단청이 원래 색으로 되살아나게 해,\n시간이 거꾸로 흐르는 인상을 만들었습니다.\n\nA-4 법당 내부 — 돌리인\nCamera pushes slowly forward down the center of the hall toward the Buddha statue, very\nslight upward tilt as it approaches. Candle flames flicker gently. A thin wisp of incense\nsmoke rises and curls. Dust floats in the door light. Extremely slow dolly-in.\n\nA-5 사천왕도 — 좌우 트래킹\nThe camera slowly pans from left to right beside the four guardian figures, without shaking.\nConstruct the frame as a flat front-facing documentary shot, parallel to the wall, without\nany dramatic angles. The figures on the wall seem to be alive and moving, but they are\nrendered in a completely flat, painterly manner, giving no sense of three-dimensionality.\n\n연출 의도 벽화를 입체로 만들지 않는 것이 핵심이라, 평면 정면 구도를 고정하고 존상만\n미세하게 살아 움직이게 했습니다.\n\nA-6 신중도 — 존상 애니메이션\nWith slow close-ups, all the figures in the painting maintain a flat, painterly feel while\nappearing alive and moving.\n<p>\nNo camera shake. No image blurring. No text generation for images, original image retained\n\nA-7 괘불 — 크레인 업\nCamera starts wide at the base and slowly cranes upward along the scroll to the Buddha's\nface, then pushes in on the hand holding the lotus. All surrounding figures freeze\ncompletely still. Only the lotus flower begins to glow with a soft inner light and its\npetals slowly open. The fabric of the scroll sways very gently in the breeze.\n\n연출 의도 권속을 전부 정지시키고 연꽃만 빛나게 해, 시선이 자연스럽게 연꽃 한 송이로\n모이도록 했습니다. 작품 전체의 정점입니다.\n\nA-9 대웅보전 내부 — 정지\nA fully submerged fixed camera. A calm and peaceful atmosphere; a gentle breeze flows\ninside, and soft light filters in. Other than that, there is no movement at all.The key is\nthe contrast with the movement in the previous shot.\n\n연출 의도 앞 컷(만다라 수렴)의 움직임과 대비를 만드는 것이 핵심이라, 카메라를\n완전히 고정하고 바람과 빛 외에는 어떤 움직임도 넣지 않았습니다.\n\n더 디테일한 내용은 생성과정 캡쳐 ZIP 파일에 생성과정 이미지와 함께 문서 PDF로 함께 첨부해서 전달드립니다.",
