      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "[ChatGPT / 레퍼런스 분석 및 프롬프트 설계]\n첨부 1은 미드저니로 생성한 초안 이미지이고, 첨부 2는 실제 국가유산 레퍼런스 이미지입니다.\n첨부 2의 시각적 정보와 문화유산의 구조적 특징을 분석하여, 첨부 1의 분위기와 표현 방식을 유지하면서도 실제 유산의 형태적 특성이 반영된 미드저니 프롬프트를 설계해 주세요.\n*핵심 구조를 분석할 것\n-중앙에 위치한 석탑의 비례와 층단 구조\n-뒤편 불전(법당)의 지붕 곡선, 기와, 공포와 단청 요소\n-앞마당의 배치감, 석재 난간, 연등 배열\n-배경의 소나무와 하늘, 사찰 경내의 전반적 구도\n\n[Midjourney / 마곡사·갑사 레퍼런스 기반 사찰 장면]\nMasterpiece Korean heritage media art illustration, cinematic frontal portrait of a traditional Korean Buddhist temple courtyard. Centered ancient tall stone pagoda, pale beige weathered stacked tiers with square base, rising before a traditional temple hall with dark gray curved tiled roof, dancheong bracket details, warm wood tones. Foreground: pale gravel courtyard, low stone railings, rows of soft pink, yellow, green, orange, and pale red lotus lanterns. Sipjangsaengdo motifs: ancient red pines with twisting trunks, jade green sculptural rocks, pale curling decorative clouds, one or two distant white cranes, layered jade hills beyond. Bright blue sky, stylized cloud motifs, tall pines behind temple. Refined minhwa and Sipjangsaengdo style: hand painted gouache, watercolor, ink wash, mineral pigments, hanji grain texture. Palette: stone beige, warm brown, dark gray, jade green, sky blue, ivory, soft pastels. Sacred, serene, auspicious, contemplative, museum quality. No people, no text, no modern elements, no fantasy excess.\n[Kling 3.0 / 장면 전환]\nUse Image 1 as the exact start frame and Image 2 as the exact end frame.\nCreate a seamless 8–10 second cinematic transition.\nBegin exactly on Image 1. The camera slowly pulls back and gently tilts down, revealing that the starting temple eaves corner is part of a larger, already-existing architectural space.\nImportant: keep the temple eaves, dancheong ornament, and roof edge visually continuous and stable during the transition. Do not let the dancheong disappear, morph, or drift. The starting roof corner should remain the visual anchor in the early part of the shot.\nAs the camera moves back, more of the connected roof structure is gradually revealed. The wider courtyard composition opens naturally. The central axis of the scene becomes clear, and the pagoda is gradually revealed in alignment with that axis. The pagoda should feel discovered by the camera, not transformed from the pillar.\nThe surrounding trees, clouds, rocks, lotus-lined path, and architectural elements appear progressively as part of the same unified space, settling into the balanced final composition of Image 2.\nKeep all motion smooth, elegant, and spatially coherent.\nNo abrupt cuts, no flashy VFX, no distortion, no object morphing, no disappearing ornament, no redesign of the architecture.\nThe transition should feel like a single continuous camera reveal from a close architectural detail into a full scenic composition.",
