      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "작품명: 시간을 유영하다\n\n사용 도구: Google Flow(Veo), Grok, 이미지 생성 도구, SUNO / 최종 편집 CapCut\n\n[S1 붓의 첫 선]\nCinematic 16:9 extreme macro close-up of a traditional Korean brush touching the matte, unglazed gray-white surface of an unfired buncheong bottle. Dark iron pigment absorbs naturally into the clay as the brush slowly draws one elegant curved line. Preserve handmade clay texture, warm side lighting, shallow depth of field, and a quiet museum-documentary mood. No completed fish, no glossy surface, no distortion, no magical effects.\n\n[S2 물고기 머리 외곽선]\nPreserve the same buncheong vessel, lighting, clay texture, and camera angle. A bamboo brush extends one dark brown-black iron-painted curved stroke toward the lower-right, forming only part of the fish-head outline. Keep the motif flat on the ceramic surface. No completed fish, no 3D transformation, no duplicate brush, no camera shake.\n\n[S3 물고기 눈과 아가미]\nPreserve the vessel and authentic fish motif from the reference images. The brush makes one controlled vertical press to create a small imperfect pupil inside the fish eye, then slowly lifts away. The vessel remains dry, porous, chalky, matte, and completely unglazed. No blinking, fish movement, extra lines, glaze, gloss, deformation, or zoom.\n\n[S4 완성된 철화 문양]\nCreate a full 16:9 Hero Frame of the long-necked pear-shaped buncheong bottle with the authentic iron-painted fish motif. Preserve the exact silhouette, proportions, fish direction, eye, fins, body dots, and brush lines from the reference. The surface remains completely matte and unglazed. The camera slowly pushes in from the full vessel toward the fish eye. No motif movement, vessel rotation, gloss, glaze, smoke, or fire.\n\n[S5 담금 시유]\nPreserve the exact vessel and fish motif. A traditional Korean potter lifts the bottle from a wide earthenware glaze vat using both hands, one gripping the neck and the other supporting the foot. Pale gray-green glaze drains naturally from the lower body. The coating remains thin, cloudy, wet, and unfired, while the fish motif stays visible and unchanged. No floating vessel, ladle, spray gun, modern equipment, crackle glaze, or glass-like gloss.\n\n[S6 굽 닦기]\nPreserve the traditional recessed foot ring with a narrow circular contact rim. One hand supports the vessel while the other wipes only 3–4 cm of the contact rim with a natural-fiber cloth, removing wet glaze and revealing dry matte clay. The bottle remains stable and suspended above the workbench. No repeated scrubbing, vessel rotation, flat base, glossy glaze, extra fingers, or hand deformation.\n\n[S7 공주 학봉리 가마]\nCreate a historically informed reconstruction of a 15–16th century ceramic kiln on the wooded slope of Gyeryongsan Mountain in Gongju. Show a long, narrow, semi-subterranean earthen kiln built into the hillside. The camera slowly dollies toward the small firebox opening while a restrained amber glow remains deep inside the kiln. No giant flames, modern chimney, metal door, modern building, explosion, or fantasy effects.\n\n[S8 실제 유물 엔딩]\nUse the supplied museum photograph as the authoritative reference. Preserve the exact Buncheong ware bottle with iron-painted lotus and fish design, including its silhouette, proportions, glaze character, age marks, firing traces, asymmetry, and original painted lines. Present it against a dark museum background with restrained warm side lighting. Do not restore, beautify, redraw, symmetrize, or alter the artifact.\n\n[S8 편집]\nThe real artifact close-up and full-view photographs were edited in CapCut using slow scale-down keyframes and cross-dissolve transitions. No generated fish movement or motif animation was used.\n\n[SUNO 배경음악]\nInstrumental cinematic heritage score, about 58 seconds, ancient yet refined and mysterious. Low warm cello drones, airy room tone, faint ceramic textures, delicate bowed strings and sparse felt-piano. Build gently through glazing and kiln scenes, then resolve into an emotional final chord at the museum artifact reveal. No vocals, choir, lyrics, pentatonic melody, Chinese-style music, EDM, trailer hits, or aggressive drums. 72 BPM.\n\n※ 장면별 상세 프롬프트 및 수정 프롬프트 전문은 별도 첨부 PDF로 제출함.",
