    {
      "id": "sub-1790860421651-35",
      "submissionNumber": "DH-VID-036",
      "title": "거울 뒤에서 1500년",
      "category": "VIDEO",
      "submitterName": "최수안",
      "participantCategory": "일반인",
      "submitterAffiliation": "직장인 프리랜서",
      "nationalHeritageName": "무령왕릉 청동거울",
      "baekjeRelated": "사용함",
      "description": "〈거울 뒤에서 1500년〉은 공주 무령왕릉에서 출토된 청동거울 일괄을 소재로, 유물 뒷면에 새겨진 세계가 깨어나는 순간을 상상한 56.8초 분량의 생성형 AI 영상이다.\n\n거울의 앞면이 사람의 얼굴을 비춘다면, 뒷면에는 어떤 시간과 이야기가 남아 있을까? 작품은 이 질문에서 출발한다. 흙 속에 묻힌 청동거울에 빛이 스며들고, 테두리의 열두 간지가 움직이며 잠들었던 시간이 흐르기 시작한다. 이어 사냥꾼과 신수의 부조가 일어나 거울 표면을 달리고, 다른 거울의 세계로 건너간다. 마지막에는 사냥꾼이 거울 너머 왕의 형상과 마주한 뒤, 모든 움직임이 다시 청동 속으로 가라앉는다.\n\n시각적 중심은 청동의 물성과 문양이다. 움직이는 형상도 금속 부조의 질감을 유지하며, 녹청과 금빛을 중심으로 유물의 깊은 시간을 표현했다. 왕과 마주하는 순간에만 색채를 더해 과거와 현재가 만나는 찰나를 강조하고, 음악을 통해 깨어남과 귀환의 흐름을 연결했다.\n\nNano Banana로 컷별 이미지를 생성하고 Seedance로 영상화한 뒤, 편집과 음악 삽입, 업스케일을 거쳐 완성했다. 웅진백제의 유물을 상상력의 출발점으로 삼아, 관람자가 작은 문양 속 이야기를 새롭게 바라보도록 기획했다.",
      "aiTools": [
        "Higgsfield 플랫폼의 Nano Banana(이미지 생성)",
        "ByteDance Seedance(영상 생성)",
        "Topaz Video(4K 업스케일)"
      ],
      "postEditingUsage": "사용함",
      "postEditingDetails": "FFmpeg(컷 연결, 크로스디졸브, 페이드인·아웃, 음악 삽입), Topaz Video(4K 업스케일)",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "작품명: 거울 뒤에서 1500년\n\n프롬프트는 두 단계로 사용했습니다.\nA. 컷별 키프레임 이미지 생성\nB. 해당 키프레임을 시작 이미지로 지정한 영상 생성\n\nA. 키프레임 이미지 생성 프롬프트\n사용 도구: Higgsfield / Nano Banana\n설정: 16:9, 2K\n\n컷 1 — 흙 속의 거울\nExtreme macro close-up of an ancient bronze mirror lying half-buried in dark tomb earth. Thick verdigris patina in jade-green and oxidized copper, faint traces of engraved relief just visible under the corrosion. Fine soil particles drifting through a single low shaft of cold light. Deep black background, cinematic museum lighting, hyperreal metal texture, shallow depth of field. Monochrome bronze palette, no color other than green-gold patina.\n\n컷 2 — 거울 뒷면 전체\nFull frame view of the complete reverse face of an ancient Korean Baekje bronze mirror, seen straight on and centered, the whole disc visible against pure black. A raised square panel at the center around the pierced knob, four mythical beasts in shallow bas-relief in the quadrants around it, and a continuous ring of twelve engraved zodiac characters running around the outer rim. Verdigris patina, casting marks, hyperreal cast-metal texture, strictly monochrome bronze palette, cool rim light, cinematic, pure black background.\n\n컷 3 — 12간지가 도는 림\nClose macro view of the outer rim of an ancient bronze mirror. The ring of twelve engraved zodiac characters catches a travelling band of warm gold light that sweeps around the circle like a clock hand, the engraved strokes glowing from within the metal. Everything else stays dark oxidized bronze. Motion-blurred light trail along the rim, strictly monochrome bronze palette, hyperreal cast-metal texture, pure black background, cinematic.\n\n컷 4 — 부조가 일어선다\nThe reverse side of an ancient Korean Baekje bronze mirror filling the frame. A square central panel at the center, surrounded by low-relief mythical beasts and a bare-chested hunter figure in a short loincloth raising a spear mid-stride, with a ring of twelve engraved zodiac characters around the outer rim. The relief figures are just beginning to lift and detach from the metal surface, edges catching warm gold rim-light against deep oxidized bronze-green. Strictly monochrome bronze palette, dramatic chiaroscuro, pure black background, cinematic, hyperreal cast-metal texture.\n\n컷 5 — 추격\nLow sweeping camera view skimming across the surface of a vast ancient bronze mirror as if the metal were a landscape. A bare-chested bas-relief hunter in a short loincloth runs in pursuit of four bas-relief beasts across the raised terrain — all of them still solid cast bronze with no realistic skin and no human facial features, only raised carved outlines. A deep engraved square boundary line cuts across the ground ahead of them and the surface begins to fold at that line. Strictly monochrome bronze, verdigris patina, dramatic raking light, pure black background, cinematic wide angle, sense of motion.\n\n컷 6 — 건너뜀\nA bas-relief bronze beast leaping across a dark gap between two ancient bronze mirror surfaces. On the far side lies a different world: four bas-relief immortal figures seated among three auspicious animals, arranged around nine small raised bosses, all in shallow carved bronze with fine engraved line work. The far mirror is slightly lighter and more silvery than the near one. Strictly monochrome metal, no realistic skin, hyperreal cast texture, pure black background, cinematic.\n\n컷 7 — 마주침\nA bare-chested hunter rendered entirely as shallow bronze bas-relief — no realistic skin or facial features, only the raised carved outline of a figure — standing at the edge of an engraved square boundary line on a vast ancient bronze mirror surface. He has turned his head toward a huge circular opening of light ahead. On the far side of that opening, also rendered as shallow bas-relief carving rather than a photographic face, the calm profile of an ancient Korean king with closed eyes. Everything stays cast metal: verdigris patina, casting marks, fine scratches, hyperreal metal texture. Strictly monochrome bronze world, with a single narrow bloom of soft pastel pink and mint light appearing exactly along the boundary line. Cinematic wide shot, pure black background, dramatic rim light.\n\n컷 8 — 다시 굳는다\nAn ancient bronze mirror lying flat, its bas-relief figures frozen mid-motion and hardening back down into the flat metal surface, raised edges sinking level with the disc. Dark tomb soil drifts in from the edges of the frame and begins to cover the metal. The light is draining away. Verdigris patina, hyperreal cast-metal texture, strictly monochrome bronze palette, deep black background, cinematic, slow and final.\n\nB. 영상 생성 프롬프트\n사용 도구: Higgsfield / ByteDance Seedance\n설정: 16:9, 1080p, 무음\n각 컷의 A단계 이미지를 시작 이미지로 지정했습니다.\n\n컷 1 — 7초\nExtremely slow, patient camera push-in toward the half-buried bronze mirror. Fine soil particles drift and settle through the shaft of cold light. The light creeps slowly across the corroded metal, gradually revealing more of the engraved relief hidden under the verdigris. The mirror itself does not move. Static, meditative, single continuous shot, no cuts, no people.\n\n컷 2 — 7초\nSlow steady camera pull-back revealing the complete disc of the bronze mirror against black. The metal stays perfectly still; only the camera moves and the raking light shifts slowly across the relief, picking out the four beasts and the ring of engraved characters in turn. Single continuous shot, no cuts, no people, strictly monochrome bronze.\n\n컷 3 — 7초\nA band of warm gold light sweeps around the rim of the bronze mirror like a clock hand, lighting each engraved zodiac character in turn as it passes. The rotation starts slowly and accelerates through the shot, leaving a motion-blurred light trail. The mirror itself does not move. Single continuous shot, no cuts, strictly monochrome bronze, pure black background.\n\n컷 4 — 9초\nThe carved bas-relief figures slowly begin to lift and detach from the flat bronze mirror surface: the hunter's spear arm rises, the four beasts push their legs free of the metal and start to move. Everything stays solid cast bronze with verdigris patina — no realistic skin, no human faces, only raised carved outlines catching gold rim-light. The ring of engraved zodiac characters rotates slowly around the rim. Very slow cinematic push-in, single continuous shot, no cuts, pure black background.\n\n컷 5 — 8초\nFast low tracking shot skimming across the bronze surface as the bas-relief hunter chases the four bas-relief beasts across the metal terrain. They all remain solid cast bronze with no realistic skin and no human faces, only raised carved outlines catching raking light. As they reach the engraved square boundary line the metal surface folds upward like a page. Single continuous shot, no cuts, strictly monochrome bronze, pure black background.\n\n컷 6 — 7초\nThe bas-relief bronze beast leaps across the dark gap and lands on the far mirror, where four seated bas-relief immortals and three auspicious animals rest around nine raised bosses. The far surface is lighter and more silvery. Everything stays shallow carved bronze with no realistic skin. Slow arcing camera follow, single continuous shot, no cuts, pure black background.\n\n컷 7 — 8초\nThe bas-relief hunter comes to a stop and slowly turns his head to face the great circular opening of light. Beyond it the carved profile of the king holds still, eyes closed. A single narrow bloom of soft pastel pink and mint light spreads slowly along the engraved boundary line between them. Everything remains cast bronze relief with no realistic skin, no photographic faces. Very slow push-in, single continuous shot, no cuts, pure black background.\n\n컷 8 — 7초\nThe bas-relief figures sink back down and harden flat into the bronze disc until the surface is smooth relief again. Dark tomb soil drifts in from the frame edges and slowly covers the metal. The light drains away to black. Static camera, slow and final, single continuous shot, no cuts, strictly monochrome bronze.\n\nC. 후반 작업 참고 사항 — 생성 프롬프트 아님\nFFmpeg로 8개 컷을 순차 연결하고, 컷 사이에 0.5초 크로스디졸브, 시작과 끝에 1초 페이드를 적용했습니다. 음악 트랙을 삽입하고 라우드니스 −16 LUFS, 트루피크 −1.5dB로 음량을 정규화했습니다. Topaz Video로 4K 업스케일을 진행했습니다.\n최종 영상: 56.8초 / 3840×2160 / 24fps",
