      "fullPrompt": "웅진 빛의탄생 | 실제 사용 AI 프롬프트 전문\n이미지 9건(선행 생성·수정 포함), 영상 8건, 새 음악 1건: 총 18건. 제작자의 기획·수정 지시를 바탕으로 Codex가 상세 프롬프트 작성을 보조했다.\n\n[PRE_K01_v01] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nUse case: lighting-weather. Create one landscape 16:9 cinematic reference still of the REAL Gongsanseong Fortress viewed across the Geum River, using the attached location photo. Preserve the recognizable stepped wall climbing from lower left to the wooded high point on the right, the pavilion near that high point, actual wooded slope, shoreline and relative placement. Change night to a CLEAR QUIET DAWN with pale blue-grey sky and extremely subtle peach light, thin low river mist and readable soft grey stonework. Remove the temporary illuminated festival boats, their reflections and artificial decorative floodlighting. Show empty calm river in the lower 40 percent, shoreline near 58 percent of image height, trees and the existing wall above it, and airy dawn sky. Do not place a new wall at the water's edge. Keep the wall on its wooded slope with its documented rise and fall. Water has an ordinary coherent reflection of that same slope and wall, vertically aligned and softly rippled. Reframe gently wider only as needed to allow the water and reflection to read; do not invent buildings or new gates. Photographic restrained art-film lighting, luminous clean dawn rather than dark night. No people, boats, temporary festival structures, neon, text or logos. This is the normal reflection before any effect.\n\n[PRE_K01_v02] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nUse case: precise-object-edit.\nAsset: revised K01 landscape 16:9 art-film reference still, Gongsanseong Fortress across the Geum River.\nImage 1 is the existing scene to improve and the dawn color/mood reference. Image 2 is the real location photograph: use its existing fortress wall course, masonry mass and pavilion architecture as the structural reference.\nUser correction: the old image is pleasant but looks like a wooded hill with a pavilion, not recognizably a mountain fortress. Make the REAL STONE FORTIFICATION unmistakable at first glance while preserving that calm dawn.\nReframe substantially closer with a moderately long lens from the same opposite riverbank: the continuous existing wall snakes prominently from the left middle/lower hillside up to the pavilion on the upper right, occupying most of the frame width. Less empty sky (about upper 12-18%) and less irrelevant forest at the sides. Keep the river and an ordinary vertically aligned reflection across the lower 28-33%. Pavilion is clearly legible and visibly associated with the wall; do not isolate it as a temple.\nCrucial improvement: preserve the actual existing stone wall dimensions and alignment from Image 2, but reveal its outward-facing masonry with delicate warm low-angle dawn illumination. The wall's grey-beige stone face, top edge and changes of slope must read distinctly against cooler, slightly darker green trees. Increase local clarity and soft directional light on stone, not overall saturation or fantasy height. Stone blocks have natural size variation, aged joints, credible rough texture and clearly resolved edges. The middle climbing section must be visually substantial, not a hair-thin line lost in trees. Keep hillside below the wall and true shoreline; never move the wall directly to the river.\nRetain pale blue-grey and faint peach dawn, tranquil water and only a very thin horizontal band of mist at the shore, not hiding the wall. Photorealistic, dignified, spacious art-film still. The viewer should instantly read stone fortifications built along a hill.\nDo not invent a new gate, castle towers, extra pavilions, crenellation pattern, giant wall or new fortification route. Do not transplant an unrelated gate into this riverside view. No modern boats, festival lights, lanterns, people, text, signs, logos, neon or theatrical light beams. This is the normal-reflection image; no reflection anomaly yet.\n\n[PRE_K01_v03] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nUse case: precise-object-edit. Revise this improved Gongsanseong dawn still ONLY for composition. Its clear, softly warm stone fortress wall climbing the real wooded slope and pavilion at upper right are the approved visual direction. Preserve the existing architecture, individual wall path, material appearance, stone wall visibility, faint blue-peach dawn and green forest as closely as possible.\nOne targeted change: provide a little more river for the later reflection effect. Keep landscape 16:9. Recompose the same view so the shoreline sits at roughly 72% of image height instead of about 82%, and calm normally reflecting river occupies the lower 28%. Shift the hill and architecture upward while gently widening the framing just enough (about 10% smaller scene scale, not a return to the distant original). Keep the entire pavilion roof within frame with some sky above. Retain the clearly readable long climbing stone wall as the primary subject. The wall must remain substantial, luminous natural stone against cooler trees, not a tiny faint line. Do not add or elongate structures. Do not enlarge the physical stone wall. \nContinue the ordinary vertically aligned water reflection realistically into the enlarged lower area. There is one subtle low mist band at the shoreline. No reflected distortion yet. No people, boats, festival installations, extra gates, text, glow or added buildings. Only one clean cinematic still, no labels or split panels.\n\n[PRE_K02_v01] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nUse case: historical-scene. Create one landscape 16:9 photorealistic art-film still of King Muryeong's actual small brick tomb chamber, using the attached interior photo as the geometry and material reference. View from the entrance along the chamber centre toward the intact rear wall. Preserve the modest real scale, rectangular floor, both side walls, continuous curved barrel-vault ceiling, alternating rows of bricks laid flat and edge-on, worn joints and the small flame-shaped lamp niches. The rear wall has one small central niche; each side wall has two in the documented chamber, show only those visible from the entrance. Pull back just enough to show the entire rounded ceiling profile, a readable floor and both sides without a fisheye lens. Keep the rear wall closed and at normal chamber depth. Illuminate from the left with soft warm amber light, rich tactile brown-grey aged brick, gentle blue-grey shadows and a calm dark entrance edge. Give a sense of intimate ancient craftsmanship, not a grand palace. Empty room with the floor-wall junction clear; no people, coffin, bones, objects, fires, murals, columns, writing, museum fixtures or overlay labels. Do not extend the room into a tunnel. This is the REAL-STRUCTURE starting still; imaginary expansion happens in a different image.\n\n[K02_vault] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nCreate one polished 16:9 cinematic art-film production keyframe, edge-to-edge, no text or panels, no people. Museum heritage reimagined as immense surreal architecture, sophisticated spectacular installation art, extreme dimensional depth and legible foreground/midground/background, tactile photoreal materials, precise fine detail, strong controlled luminous contrast, no washed-out highlights. This is an explicitly imaginative world, not a historical reconstruction. Use the reference for the distinctive small King Muryeong tomb chamber's GREY thin rectangular brick courses, barrel vault and single flame-shaped central wall niche. From low center of an actual small dark chamber in foreground, its vault opens into a breathtaking impossible cosmos of hundreds of nested suspended semicircular BRICK RIBS, sweeping diagonally up and right in a broad spiral. Large loose architectural ribs in extreme foreground frame the view, progressively tinier ribs disappear into deep lapis blue space. Fine amber light threads trace mortar joints and describe wave fronts. A clear floor path leads into the ribbed blue and amber distance. Brick is weathered gray-brown, not a fantasy palace or generic cathedral. Dramatic close-to-vast scale, black shadows, lapis/teal recesses, warm gilded rim-light. Tangible and monumental. No debris explosion; carefully organized coherent construction.\n\n[K03_guardian] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nCreate one polished 16:9 cinematic art-film production keyframe, edge-to-edge, no text or panels, no people. Museum heritage reimagined as immense surreal architecture, sophisticated spectacular installation art, extreme dimensional depth and legible foreground/midground/background, tactile photoreal materials, precise fine detail, strong controlled luminous contrast, no washed-out highlights. This is an explicitly imaginative world, not a historical reconstruction. Accurately retain the reference's SINGLE distinctive chunky pale weathered stone guardian from King Muryeong tomb: low broad muzzle, squat bulky body, short four legs, carved wing-like side ridges and ONE small dark metal horn. The guardian is a recognizable complete sculpture in center foreground, about 35 percent of frame height, on a broad obsidian stone island. Surrounding it, gigantic horizontal contour rings of thousands of levitating stone tablets trace the guardian's protective force across a vast dark turquoise void, with three broad sweeping waves moving outward, not a mechanical sci-fi machine. Near-camera floating rough stone blocks beautifully frame left and right edges; fine amber seams and emerald/gold dust rivers, immense scale and rich spatial parallax. A monumental sweeping aurora of stone and golden light fills upper background. Guarding the space, ancient and powerful, solid sculpture intact and motionless. Controlled turquoise, aged bone-white stone, amber. NOT a living animal, lion, dragon or humanoid.\n\n[K04_silver] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nCreate one polished 16:9 cinematic art-film production keyframe, edge-to-edge, no text or panels, no people. Museum heritage reimagined as immense surreal architecture, sophisticated spectacular installation art, extreme dimensional depth and legible foreground/midground/background, tactile photoreal materials, precise fine detail, strong controlled luminous contrast, no washed-out highlights. This is an explicitly imaginative world, not a historical reconstruction. Use the two actual antique SILVER bracelets with shallow entwined dragon carvings from the reference; retain their dark silver patina, compact solid rounded band and relief pattern, no gems, no gold. Reinterpret the pair at gigantic scale as TWO upright inclined ring portals rising from an immense liquid silver ocean. One ring close in foreground on left partly beyond frame, its dragon-carved skin macro crisp, second complete ring in midground right. The central opening offers a long luminous vanishing point through smaller echo rings far away. Strong diagonal camera view at water level, deeply layered silver ridges and mercury waves, reflective black and cold aquamarine shadows, a thin amber light river cutting across water toward the portal. Sky almost black with luminous teal horizontal curtains, spectacular immense scale, sculptural tangibility and avant-garde luxury art film. Keep continuous open centers and antique carved silver material, no baroque generic gold jewelry.\n\n[K05_gold] image | OpenAI built-in image_gen (underlying model not returned)\nCreate one polished 16:9 cinematic art-film production keyframe, edge-to-edge, no text or panels, no people. Museum heritage reimagined as immense surreal architecture, sophisticated spectacular installation art, extreme dimensional depth and legible foreground/midground/background, tactile photoreal materials, precise 