pple in the sky. The antique silver rings are rigid sculptures with intact open circular centers and preserved dark carved patina. Strong macro-to-vast spatial reveal and layered parallax. Silver remains silver. End with the next ring filling most of the view. No people, no text.\n\n[G06] video | Runway web Gen-4.5 Unlimited\nContinuous majestic forward flight through the immense gold openwork world. The camera follows the winding luminous river and glides between gigantic thin planar crown-ornament sculptures toward the recognizable paired ornaments in the far center. Foreground gold cutout blades sweep dramatically past both edges, revealing many more layers behind them. Small hanging circular gold discs tremble delicately and catch traveling cascades of glints. Thousands of warm gold particles rise in broad coordinated streams, growing toward a dazzling controlled climax, while deep lapis-blue negative spaces stay clear between intricate gold shapes. Hammered metal detail, strong scale change and cinematic spatial parallax. Gold sheets remain coherent solid ornament silhouettes. No people, no text.\n\n[G07] video | Runway web Gen-4.5 Unlimited\nContinue seamlessly from this exact final frame. The two central gold crown-ornament silhouettes remain intact and clearly readable. The camera rises in a majestic sweeping crane move and tilts down gently, revealing an immense flowing field of many smaller gold openwork ornaments across the reflective floor. A brilliant wave of tiny golden lights spreads from the central pair through all the distant rows, drawing huge graceful flame-shaped curves. Thousands of fine gold filaments rise into the blue-black space overhead like a vast illuminated canopy. Hanging round gold discs shimmer and pass near the edges of the lens. The image grows from a clear pair into an overwhelming, richly layered golden universe, elegant controlled radiance and deep dark negative spaces. Strong vertical parallax and spectacular increasing scale. No people, no text.\n\n[G08] video | Runway web Gen-4.5 Unlimited\nOne continuous majestic aerial pullback from the recognizable ancient hillside fortress and river. The camera retreats smoothly and rises slightly, keeping the long winding stone wall and pavilion readable. Thousands of fine golden filigree light threads stream across the river and sweep upward in enormous calm arcs over the fortress. The broad aurora slowly folds into elegant crown-like curves across the sky, then the lines become fewer and settle into soft golden reflections on the water. Strong foreground water movement and layered luminous depth, a triumphant beautiful arrival home. The actual hill, pavilion and stone wall stay solid and unchanged. Deep lapis night, gold and teal, restrained highlights preserving all detail. No people, no text.\n\n[M01] music | Runway web Audio / Lyria 3 Pro\nCreate an ORIGINAL instrumental cinematic score, exactly 60 seconds long, for a spectacular Korean Baekje heritage art film titled Birth of Light. One continuous composed cue with a clear emotional arc and a memorable elegant five-note motif, not a repeating stock loop. No vocals, choir, humming, lyrics, speech, narration or sound effects. No imitation of any existing song, artist or recording.\n\n\n\nSound: beautifully recorded warm orchestral strings, expressive low strings, delicate Korean gayageum-like plucked strings, an airy bamboo flute, luminous celesta, noble mellow brass, deep rounded cinematic drums. Spacious sophisticated acoustic depth with subtle modern atmosphere. Majestic, mysterious and moving, never cheerful corporate music, EDM, a military march or harsh trailer noise. A graceful flowing pulse around 120 BPM, often felt in half time, with natural human phrasing and rich melodic development.\n\n\n\nTimed form for the complete 60-second cue:\n\n0-7s: enter immediately and softly with a single luminous plucked motif, airy flute and low string warmth, dawn and light on a river; a gentle rising