      "fullPrompt": "왕국의 두께 — 최종 영상·음악 생성 프롬프트 전문\n\n기준 이미지까지 포함한 전문 입력은 Google 폼이 응답 용량 초과로 거부했다. 아래에 최종 작품에 사용한 영상 12개와 음악 1개의 실제 프롬프트 본문을 생략 없이 기재한다. 기준 이미지 9개 전문 및 미채택 시험 요청, 각 입력 이미지·작업 식별자·설정까지 포함한 전체 전문은 첨부한 왕국의두께_최종_생성원본과제작기록.zip의 제작과권리/프롬프트_전체기록.txt에 보존했다. S10은 실제 전달된 잔여 문구도 수정 없이 포함한다.\n\n[C02 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nC02 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. Within this vast world of thin hammered gold openwork, a swift lateral camera move passes extremely close behind the curved gold leaf at the left of frame, giving powerful near-to-far parallax. As the camera emerges, all the tall delicate gold sheets begin to tilt together in a coordinated rolling wave, turning nearly edge-on to the lens so their broad surfaces become razor-thin golden lines and the huge dark gaps suddenly open. The camera decelerates into a suspended slow tracking moment between those thin lines. Round gold spangles swing independently from fine wires, with realistic weight. Then the thin sheets fan open again in a sharp, elegant wave and reveal a much larger illuminated space beyond, filling the wide frame with depth. Precise camera translation and real changes in sheet orientation, not a zoom. Warm worn gold, tiny hammer marks, fine cut edges, deep blue-black shadows, physical miniature cinematography. No melting, no tearing, no thick blocks, no fire, no people, no lettering. A bold rapid-slow-rapid rhythm, with a clear beautiful final open space.\n\n[E01 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\nEND V2 — single continuous 8-second shot. Begin with the exact two upright gold crown ornaments in the reference, filling the frame majestically. Their complete delicate cutout silhouettes and small hanging round spangles remain precisely intact. First 2 seconds: a narrow intense warm grazing light travels upward across the hammered gold, the tiny spangles settle, camera nearly still. Then BOTH paper-thin ornaments rotate decisively 90 degrees about their own vertical axes, together like two enormous doors turning away from the viewer; fast acceleration, strong physical momentum, clean dramatic specular streaks. Their faces narrow progressively until only two razor-thin vertical gold edges remain by second 6. Last 2 seconds: hold the two parallel edge-on gold lines against the deep blue-black void, faint floor reflection. Preserve their size and centered positions throughout. No zoom, no folding, no bending, no shattering, no extra ornaments, no newly invented motifs, no text. Photoreal material, cinematic high-contrast lighting, breathtaking precise mechanical choreography. The reference is the complete hero form, not a texture to morph.\n\n[M01 / Runway Lyria 3 Pro]\n\nM01 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. Create an original instrumental film score, approximately 60 seconds long, for a Korean heritage art film about the precision and imagination held inside a very thin ancient gold ornament. No vocals, choir, humming, speech or lyrics. Start immediately with one crisp resonant metal strike and a low cinematic drum pulse. A distinctive three-note plucked motif played with a dry gayageum-like timbre, airy bowed strings, deep organic percussion, and tiny metallic resonances. A clear 120 BPM pulse in 4/4, with accelerating subdivisions rather than constant loudness. At 0-8 seconds: sparse and intriguing, rapid bright details over dark spacious bass. At 8-24 seconds: rhythmic interlocking plucks and strings build momentum as microscopic gold becomes an enormous space. At 24-31 seconds: suddenly strip away the drums, leaving a suspended delicate metal resonance and one fine string. At 31-46 seconds: rebuild with faster subdivisions, strong syncopated low drums, rising harmonic tension, wide orchestral depth. At 46-54 seconds: the only full monumental climax, energetic and expansive, with a clear melodic statement. At 54-56 seconds: an abrupt inward pull, one precise final impact. At 56-60 seconds: a luminous resolved chord and natural shimmering decay to silence. This must have a complete ending, not a loop or a fade in the middle of a phrase. Tactile, dignified, mysterious, then immense; not a generic action trailer, no bomb sounds, no stock whooshes. Clean dynamic mix with room for separately edited material sound effects. Do not imitate any existing melody, recording, artist, or traditional ritual piece.\n\n[S01 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS01 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. A photorealistic live-action tracking shot of Gongbukru pavilion at Gongsanseong fortress in Gongju, exactly matching this reference. Start already moving briskly forward at eye level toward the central open ground-floor passage. The red timber pillars slide rapidly outward at different speeds with strong real parallax. The original two-storey open timber structure, five bays, long low gray tiled roof, stone wall and exact three-character plaque remain unchanged. The camera passes just beneath the central beam into the shadow of the passage and approaches the blue-and-gold Geum River visible beyond. A thin horizontal reflection on the river becomes the visual focus. Preserve this real low riverside terrain and the actual gate opening. Real aged red wood, rough irregular stone and ceramic roof tiles, natural blue-hour light, subtle moving river reflections. No people, vehicles or invented buildings. No architectural morphing, no explosion, no lens zoom, no added lettering, no timelapse. A decisive forward camera translation, not a slow sightseeing pan. Finish near the shaded passage looking toward the real river.\n\n[S03 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS03 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. A single continuous physical macro tracking shot. The camera shoots laterally to the right along the cut edge of this thin pierced gold sheet. A nearby curved rim sweeps rapidly across the lens, briefly covering most of the picture. As it passes, the view opens through the large dark cutout into two offset gold layers farther behind. Slow briefly inside that opening, revealing parallax between sharp foreground edges and distant warm gold. Then accelerate rightward behind the next curling gold rim, ending in natural foreground occlusion. The gold is rigid, paper-thin worked metal with fixed organic cut patterns, not liquid. Fine scratches and worn hammer marks remain coherent. Strong lateral translation and depth, not a zoom. Blue-black negative space, controlled warm specular light. No new flowers, no multiplying holes, no complete crown, no people, no words, no particles, no edits.\n\n[S04 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS04 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. One continuous tracking crane shot through this physically tangible installation of extremely thin pierced botanical gold. Begin with a brisk lateral truck to the left: a close round spangle passes across the lens while the foreground cut rim slides quickly right, with slower distant layers proving true parallax. Continue rising over the nearest curled sheet, looking slightly downward into a deep open blue-black channel between offset sheets. Over the final four seconds, the two large gold planes ahead slowly hinge apart as intact rigid sheets, revealing a broad open space farther below. Keep the original worn hammered-metal texture and fixed organic holes. Tiny circular spangles swing on their existing wires. Thin planes and open air, not thick golden rocks. Elegant strong speed contrast and changing depth, no optical zoom, no cuts, no whole artifact replicas, no particles, no text, no people.\n\n[S05 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS05 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. Photoreal live-action Gongju, South Korea. A brisk, short, low aerial lateral tracking shot over the Geum River beside the real Gongbukru pavilion of Gongsanseong. Preserve this exact geographic arrangement: broad calm river on the left, the low wooded hillside on the right, the old stone wall following the slope toward the two-storey open timber pavilion on the riverbank. The camera moves rightward and modestly forward, close enough that near wall stones pass faster than the water and distant shore, while keeping the entire pavilion and river relationship legible. Water ripples and faint leaves move naturally. Stable blue-hour exposure, worn real stone, red-brown timber, gray tile, natural photographic detail. Maintain building height and roof silhouette, no new structures, no mountainous fantasy citadel, no flags, no people, no artificial lighting beams, no text overlay. One continuous shot, no transformation.\n\n[S06 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS06 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. A continuous macro shot of this single thin pierced gold plane suspended in deep blue-black space. The existing sheet is rigid worked metal. During the first three seconds the whole sheet pivots ninety degrees around its long axis, so its broad surface becomes a razor-thin diagonal edge. The camera travels gently sideways at edge height, letting a small original curled lip cross the focus plane. For three seconds remain close to that slender rim, with the tiny hammer marks sharp and the distant sheet surface falling out of focus. At the end the camera passes beyond the rim into clean dark negative space. The same fixed openings and worn texture throughout, no added holes or changing outlines, no melting or elastic material, no new objects or spangles, no particles, no optical zoom, no people, no text, no internal cut. Emphasize how little physical thickness produces such a large surface.\n\n[S07 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS07 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. A continuous overhead camera journey through two offset sheets of very thin cut gold. First the camera slides diagonally across the upper filigree plane toward the large oval hole on the right, making the open blue-black channels between the cut shapes read graphically. Descend through that existing oval opening without changing its shape. The nearest gold rim briefly fills the foreground as the lower sheet, a long distance below, comes into focus. Then drift laterally under the upper plane, so its curved shadow travels across the lower plane through real parallax. The sheets are rigid and the original patterns remain fixed. Only the camera and a few curled sheet edges move; no spontaneous new shapes, no liquid morph, no complete crown replicas. Worn warm gold, thin edges, strong shadow depth, no haze, no particles, no words or people, no cut.\n\n[S08 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS08 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. One restrained physical macro take. The foremost round gold spangle is one solid circular disk with exactly its existing single suspension hole, hanging from its original fine wire. It slowly swivels from broad face toward a narrow edge and back only part way, keeping a perfectly stable disk outline and unchanged one-hole topology. Camera slides a small distance sideways, extremely close to the rim, and focus transfers once from the rough gold face to the wire loop and back. The other fixed disks remain soft in the background. Surface speckles are shallow patina marks, never holes. The cut-gold support at the left remains rigid and unchanged. Slow, tactile, weighty metal movement, visibly changing reflections but constant warm side lighting, deep blue-black negative space. No zoom, no extra disks, no growing or dissolving holes, no new cutouts, no text or people, no cuts.\n\n[S09 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS09 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. One powerful material-art shot through this immense open installation made from thin pierced gold. A synchronized turning motion travels across the suspended sheets from near left to far right. Each large intact sheet rotates like a rigid hinged plane, showing its incredibly thin edge, then opening its wide botanical cut face to the light. The wave is brisk at first, pauses for one breath as the nearest sheet stands almost edge-on, then continues into the distance. The camera trucks left at medium height and arcs upward modestly, giving strong foreground occlusion and a changing view through the existing negative spaces. Round spangles lag naturally behind the sheet motion on their fine wires. Keep every cut pattern stable and all material thin, worn gold rather than molten metal or fabric. No explosions, no debris or particles, no palaces, no whole crown replicas, no people or text. One continuous shot, no digital zoom.\n\n[S10 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\n원S10 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. The one monumental climax shot. From this low wide view, the enormous thin filigree gold sheets rise and rotate outward in an accelerating coordinated motion, as if one precise mechanical thought passes through the entire installation. The closest sheet sweeps upward across the top of the lens and reveals a dramatically deeper blue-black space beyond. The camera cranes upward and slightly backward only as the planes open, keeping large near gold rims at the sides to make the collective scale overwhelming. Over the last three seconds the sheet motion reaches its broadest fully spread configuration; the camera settles into a wide oblique vista while the small circular spangles continue one last weighty swing. Tangible paper-thin worked gold, fixed botanical holes and worn surfaces. Greatness through thin planes and vast negative space, not thickness or a gold mountain. No new objects, no explosions, no dust, no glowing particles, no buildings, no people, no letters, no internal cut.\n\nimmense open installation made from thin pierced gold. A synchronized turning motion travels across the suspended sheets from near left to far right. Each large intact sheet rotates like a rigid hinged plane, showing its incredibly thin edge, then opening its wide botanical cut face to the light. The wave is brisk at first, pauses for one breath as the nearest sheet stands almost edge-on, then continues into the distance. The camera trucks left at medium height and arcs upward modestly, giving strong foreground occlusion and a changing view through the existing negative spaces. Round spangles lag naturally behind the sheet motion on their fine wires. Keep every cut pattern stable and all material thin, worn gold rather than molten metal or fabric. No explosions, no debris or particles, no palaces, no whole crown replicas, no people or text. One continuous shot, no digital zoom.\n\n[S11 / Runway Gen-4.5 Unlimited]\n\nS11 KINGDOM THICKNESS 20260913. One continuous soaring oblique overhead reveal of an immense open installation of thin pierced botanical gold. The camera rises quickly above the nearest gold sheet and arcs to the right, looking down through the huge empty central channel. Strong parallax reveals that the many near and far sheets are separated by vast distances. During the rise the planes rotate together by a quarter turn, their openings remaining rigid and exactly shaped, so the warm cut faces and blue void alternately dominate the picture. End at a high wide angle that reveals the shared sweeping direction of the whole arrangement, with a clear blue-black central negative space and asymmetrical gold curves at the edges. The thin sheets do not multiply or become a forest. Reflections and small dangling disks respond physically. No extra towers or giant crown silhouettes, no fabric, no fluid morph, no particles, no text or people, no cuts or optical zoom.\n\n업스케일: Runway 웹 Topaz AI Unlimited. 기존 U02·U03(편집 확정 앞·뒤 30초)과 새 E01의 END_U01을 실제 4096×2304로 업스케일하고 3840×2160으로 출력했다. 새 엔딩 54–60초를 교체했다. END_U01은 수정 작업의 U01이며 기존 U01 시험과 별개다. 업스케일에는 텍스트 프롬프트가 없다.",
