      "fullPrompt": "② 영상 프롬프트 — Seedance 2.5\n[Attachments: @image_1 = first keyframe / @image_2 = review card overlay reference]\n\n=== CANON LOCK (FIXED) ===\nPhotorealistic live-action commercial, 16:9. The video starts exactly on @image_1 as the first frame: same framing, same woman, same living room, same lamp light, same delivery-tracking UI card at the top left. Tone is an ordinary everyday online-shopping commercial: relatable, lightly comedic, clean and warm. There is no historical, museum, gold, or cultural-heritage element anywhere in this clip.\n\nCONTINUITY LOCK: anamorphic 35mm lens look, natural soft window daylight from frame left mixed with a warm table-lamp key from behind the sofa, restrained teal-and-orange grade with gentle warm skin tones, subtle fine film grain, soft highlight roll-off, no lens flares. This exact look stays identical for the entire clip.\n\nCHARACTER LOCK — THE WOMAN: adult Korean woman, long dark brown wavy hair with a center part falling past her shoulders, natural light makeup, oversized cream chunky knit sweater with long sleeves covering part of her hands, light gray cotton shorts with thin white piping, cream chunky knit socks. She holds a silver smartphone with a triple rear camera; the back of the phone faces the camera and the phone screen is never visible to the viewer. She sits sideways on a beige fabric sofa with knees drawn up. Her hair, sweater, shorts, socks, and phone stay exactly the same in every shot. No other person appears at any time.\n\nSET LOCK: a modern apartment living room. Beige sofa with a mustard knit cushion and gray cushions, a wooden coffee table in the foreground with a white mug and two books, a green leafy plant at frame left edge, a large window with sheer curtains at left, a warm table lamp and a framed picture on the back wall, and a dark charcoal front door with a narrow frosted vertical panel and a digital door lock at frame right. The floor in front of the door is a matte light oak wood floor and it is completely EMPTY: no box, no package, no bag, no object at the door at any moment. The front door stays fully closed the whole clip. All surfaces are matte, with no visible reflections anywhere, including the floor, the picture frame, the window, and the mug.\n\nUI OVERLAY RULES: all on-screen graphics are flat 2D interface overlays locked to the screen. They never move with the camera or the woman, never warp, never blur, and never change their letters. Korean text must stay pixel-stable and spelled exactly as in the references. No other text, subtitles, logos, watermarks, or letters appear anywhere in the frame.\n\n=== SCENE BLOCK ===\nSHOT 1 — 00:00–00:06 — ONE CONTINUOUS TAKE, no cuts, no zoom. Wide shot, static locked-off camera on a tripod, eye level, exactly the @image_1 composition, moderate depth of field so both her face and the front door are readable.\n\n00:00–00:01 | WS | Static locked-off | eye level, frontal three-quarter | 35mm anamorphic. Opening hook: she presses her thumb onto the phone screen with a small firm tap, a pull-to-refresh motion. Her eyebrows pull together and her lower lip pushes out slightly. The tracking UI card at the top left stays exactly as in @image_1.\n\n00:01–00:02 | WS | Static locked-off | same framing | 35mm. She taps and drags her thumb down again, faster this time. Her chin lifts off her hand for a moment and she leans her face a little closer to the phone. The blue \"배송중\" dot on the tracking card gives one soft pulse; all card text stays unchanged.\n\n00:02–00:03 | WS | Static locked-off | same framing | 35mm. A third quick refresh tap. Nothing changes on the card. Her shoulders drop, she exhales through her nose, and her mouth presses into a flat line.\n\n00:03–00:04 | WS | Static locked-off | same framing | 35mm. She turns her head to frame right toward the front door, her hand sliding away from her cheek. Her eyes widen slightly with hope.\n\n00:04–00:05 | WS | Static locked-off | same framing | 35mm. The door stays closed and the matte floor in front of it is empty. She holds the look, blinks twice slowly, and her eyebrows sink back down.\n\n00:05–00:06 | WS | Static locked-off | same framing | 35mm. She turns her head back to the phone and rests her cheek on her hand again. From 00:05.6 to 00:06.0 the tracking UI card fades out smoothly and completely.\n\nHARD CUT at 00:06 (size change WS to MCU plus camera mode change static to stabilized dolly).\n\nSHOT 2 — 00:06–00:10 — Medium close-up, same woman, same sweater, same room, same lamp light, now framed from chest up, camera slightly to frame left of her so the closed front door sits softly out of focus behind her at frame right. Shallow depth of field, creamy background blur.\n\n00:06–00:07 | MCU | Stabilized slow dolly-in | eye level | 35mm anamorphic, shallow DOF. The camera begins a very slow smooth push toward her face. She stares at the phone, cheek on her hand, and says her line in a small tired voice with clear lip movement.\n\n00:07–00:08 | MCU | Stabilized dolly-in continuing, gentle | eye level | 35mm, shallow DOF. The line ends. Her head tilts heavier onto her hand, her eyelids lower halfway, and the corners of her mouth turn down. The push-in stops exactly at 00:08.\n\n00:08–00:10 | MCU | Static locked-off | eye level | 35mm, shallow DOF. The camera is completely still. At 00:08.0 the @image_2 review card rises gently about 3% from below while fading in over 0.3 seconds. Then it holds perfectly still until the end. Placement: bottom-center lower third, about 55% of frame width, 8% margin from the bottom edge, not covering her face. Reproduce @image_2 exactly as-is: white rounded card, gray profile icon at left, one filled yellow star followed by four empty gray stars, gray three-dot menu at right, and bold black Korean text exactly \"배송이 너무 늦어요.\" Behind the card she lets out a long silent sigh, her shoulders sink, and she lowers the phone slightly toward her lap. The clip ends on this still, relatable moment.\n\nPERFORMANCE NOTES: physical expression only, small and natural, commercial-realistic acting, no exaggerated mugging. Hands stay anatomically correct with five fingers, and the phone stays in her right hand the whole time. She never leaves the frame.\n\n=== AUDIO ===\nVOICE LOCK:\nNarrator: none in C01. No narration in this clip.\nWoman A: adult female, soft mid-range voice, slightly tired and sulky, relaxed slow conversational delivery, clear articulation, natural standard Korean. SAME VOICE ACROSS ALL CLIPS.\nRULES: one speaker only in this clip, no gender switch, Korean dialogue spoken exactly as written with no translation, no overlapping speech.\n\nDIALOGUE (Woman A, 00:06.3–00:07.5, spoken slowly, short pause after the first word):\n\"아… 언제 와?\"\n(pronunciation guide: \"a… eon-je wa?\")\n\nSOUND: quiet apartment room tone; three soft screen-tap sounds at 00:00.3, 00:01.3, 00:02.3; a faint sofa fabric rustle when she turns her head; a light, playful minimal pluck-guitar commercial music bed at low volume through the whole clip; a soft airy sigh at 00:08.5; a gentle UI pop sound at 00:08.0 when the review card appears. No other voices.\n\n=== NEGATIVE ===\nno delivery box, no package at the door, door never opens, no second person, no visible phone screen content, no reflections on any surface, no mirror, no subject leaving and re-entering frame, no extra text or subtitles, no warped or misspelled Korean letters, no moving or wobbling overlay cards, no morphing hands, no outfit change, no hair change, no zoom in shot 1, no camera shake.\n\nTotal: 10s / 2 shots / 16:9",
