      "fullPrompt": "1.픽셀 게임 화면 제작\n-시작 장면\nUse image 1 as the style reference and image 2 as the character reference.\nTurn Gongju City mascots \"Gomagom\" and \"Gongju\" into charming 16-bit pixel-art characters, keeping their original silhouettes, colors, costumes, expressions, and distinctive features. A side-scrolling 2D pixel-art platformer scene inside Gongsanseong Fortress (Gongju, Korea), Baekje era: stone fortress walls, wooden gates, tiled Korean roofs, hills, trees, and the Geumgang River in the distance. Subtly weave Baekje motifs into platforms, banners, stones, and architecture.\nFeels like a real playable game level, not a tourist poster. Small pixel HUD at top: hearts, inventory icon, mini-map indicator, and collectible Baekje-inspired heritage items. Layered parallax background.\n16-bit pixel art, crisp edges, limited palette, 2D game screenshot, side view, horizontal composition, nostalgic adventure atmosphere.\nNegative: photorealism, 3D, realistic textures, modern buildings, excessive text.\n\n-진묘수(석수) 제작\n16-bit pixel art, side-scrolling 2D platformer game screenshot, horizontal composition.\nTwo chibi heroes running side by side on a mossy stone fortress wall: a cheerful girl with short brown hair, yellow bunny-ear hair accessories and an orange dress, and a round brown bear wearing a yellow scarf, orange cape and red belt. A mossy stone beast statue with antlers on a stone pedestal stands ahead of them.\nSetting: Gongsanseong Fortress in Gongju, Baekje era. Layered parallax background with stone walls and stairs, a wooden pavilion with dark tiled roof, a stone arch bridge over a blue river, forested hills with a distant hilltop pavilion, mountains, white flowers, falling pink petals. Purple banners with golden crown emblems (Baekje motif). Dark leaf silhouettes in the foreground.HUD: parchment-style panels with character portraits, red hearts, a blue energy bar, gold coin counter (x025), pottery item counter (x03), and a parchment mini-map with dotted path and icons in the top right. Small \"GONGJU HERITAGE QUEST\" logo at bottom right. Bright sunny sky, vivid but limited palette, crisp pixel edges, detailed pixel clusters, charming nostalgic adventure mood.\n\n\n2.3D 캐릭터 제작\n- 캐릭터 & 진묘수\nSoft 3D-rendered fantasy scene, stylized toy-like CGI, cinematic wide shot (16:9).\nSeen from behind, two small chibi characters stand in a sea of fluffy clouds looking up: a child in a rounded brown hat/helmet with small golden horns and a round top knob, carrying a swirl-tipped staff and wearing a pale orange outfit, and a fuzzy brown teddy bear with a cream-yellow scarf.\nBefore them looms a giant mythical guardian beast statue made of translucent pale-green jade, with a smiling face, curled spiral scroll patterns on its body, and a dark ink-blue antler crest, partially veiled by billowing clouds.Layered puffy clouds in the foreground and midground, elegant swirling cloud ribbons (traditional Korean cloud-pattern feel), bright glowing white-blue sky, dreamy misty atmosphere, soft volumetric light, pastel palette of mint, white, and lavender-gray with warm brown accents.Sense of awe and wonder, smooth clay-like materials, subsurface scattering on the jade, shallow depth of field.\n- 고마곰, 공주\nThe camera performs a dramatic, continuous push-in toward the two characters. Starting from a wide shot where the characters are small in the middle of the frame with green hills and a blue-roofed temple behind them, the camera steadily moves straight forward and ends in a close-up where the girl and the bear fill most of the frame, showing their faces and upper bodies. The forward movement is large, clearly visible and never stops from the first second to the last. The camera moves straight forward only, with no vertical bobbing, no tilt, no shaking, no sideways pan.\nA cinematic 3D animated scene in a soft, dreamy, clay-like Pixar style. A girl with a brown bob hair, golden horn-like ornaments and a salute pose, and a brown teddy bear with a yellow scarf, stand side by side on a sea of soft white clouds. Green rolling hills and a traditional blue-roofed pavilion are in the distance under a bright blue sky. As the camera pushes in, the background hills and pavilion naturally grow larger and blur slightly with soft depth of field, keeping the two characters sharp and in the center of the frame. The characters stay in place. They may only blink softly or breathe very subtly. No walking, no turning, no large body movement. Their shape, color and design never change.\nSoft diffused sunlight, calm and cheerful atmosphere. Smooth, steady, cinematic pacing.\n\n- 무령왕릉 제작 \nSoft 3D-rendered stylized diorama, toy-like clay CGI, cinematic wide shot (16:9), high-angle aerial view. A large rounded green burial mound with a partially excavated ancient royal tomb entrance: gray stone brick walls forming a rectangular courtyard, a dark arched tomb doorway, stone steps, and sandy dirt ground around it. Two small gray guardian beast statues on stone pedestals flank the entrance. A few small mossy bushes scattered nearby.\nBackground: blurred rolling hills with more grassy mounds, winding paths, dense green trees, distant mountains and a faint river and town in soft haze (shallow depth of field).\nFluffy lavender-white clouds framing the corners of the frame. Large glowing 3D bubble-style cream-white text \"Who Is It?\" floating above the mound, with small gold sparkles.\nSoft bright daylight, pastel green, beige, and lavender palette, smooth clay-like materials, playful mysterious mood.\n\n3.영상 제작\n-픽셀 게임 진행\n(1)Retro 16-bit pixel game scene, camera completely locked and fixed for the entire video: no pan, zoom, tracking, rotation, shake, parallax, or change of viewpoint.\nThe princess and brown bear keep identical designs, proportions, costumes, colors, and faces throughout. Their only action is slowly walking forward together, with no other behavior.\nAnimate them like classic 2D pixel sprites: limited frames, stepped movement, discrete poses, low-frame-rate choppy walk cycle, slow and deliberate, never smooth or realistic.\nWhile they walk, only the background gradually transitions from the first reference image (Gongsanseong fortress, trees, mountains, pavilion, bridge, river, flowers) to the second reference image, keeping the same pixel-art style, colors, lighting, and pixel scale. No sudden cuts, no character changes. End on a scene closely matching the second reference image.\n\n(2)16-bit pixel art side-scrolling game scene. Camera fully locked: no zoom, pan, tilt, or shake. Background, game UI, and the girl and bear designs never change.Sequence, in strict order:\nThe girl and bear stand surprised beside a small stone guardian beast statue (seok-su) on its pedestal. A red exclamation-mark speech bubble floats above the girl. Golden sparkles twinkle around the statue. The bear raises one arm toward the statue, mouth wide open. The instant his hand reaches out, the statue starts glowing warm gold. The girl's exclamation bubble gently fades away.\nThe statue slowly and smoothly rises straight up, leaving the pedestal empty. Its shape, texture, and color stay identical. Golden light rays, sparkles, and a glowing ring appear around it.\nThe girl and bear look up at it. The girl clasps both hands near her chin, eyes wide and sparkling, mouth open. Once in this pose they hold perfectly still, no walking. Only after the statue has fully reached its floating position, with a clear pause first, glowing golden pixel text \"Quest: ?\" with a question-mark box and a small down arrow slowly fades in above it (0% to 100% opacity). The text must not appear before the rise finishes. Slow, smooth pacing, consistent 16-bit pixel style. Final frame matches the end image exactly.\n\n(3)The glowing stone guardian statue slowly dissolves into countless tiny luminous particles, magic dust, and glowing embers. Particles peel gently from its surface and drift outward in all directions like a galaxy of magical stardust, swirling softly with slow, graceful, ethereal motion.\nDense near the statue, the particles gradually thin out as they spread farther into the surrounding darkness. Warm golden light, subtle glowing trails, sparkling dust, soft radiant embers, mystical fantasy atmosphere.Gentle particle dissolution only: no shattering, no cracks, no shards, no large fragments, no explosion. Slow motion, elegant and cinematic. Preserve the original statue design and composition.\n\n- 3D영상 제작\n(1)Cinematic 3D animated scene, soft, dreamy, clay-like Pixar style. The camera continuously zooms in toward the jade statue, steadily closer from start to finish. Strong, clearly visible forward zoom only: no vertical bobbing, no shaking, no sideways pan. A pale green jade guardian beast statue with a small dark blue creature on its head stands in a sea of white clouds. In the foreground, seen from behind, a girl in a brown hat with golden horn-like ornaments and a brown teddy bear with a yellow scarf look up at it. As the camera zooms in, the thick clouds and swirling mist covering the statue slowly drift right and clear out of frame, gradually revealing the full statue. Cloud motion is slow, soft, and natural. The statue, girl, and bear stay completely frozen: no movement, head turns, breathing, or idle animation. Their shape, color, and design never change.\nSoft diffused white lighting, calm and serene mood. The zoom continues smoothly until the final frame, which matches the end image.\n\n(2)A very slow, smooth camera zoom-in toward the characters. The characters do not move from their positions. The girl only raises her arm slightly and slowly lowers it once. The bear stays still. No other actions. Keep the background and composition unchanged. Gradually transition from the wide shot to a closer medium shot of the two characters. Stable camera movement, no shake, no rotation, no panning, no dramatic motion. Preserve the original 3D character design, facial expressions, clothing, colors and proportions. \n\n(3)Continuous cinematic camera tracking shot. The camera starts behind the characters and smoothly moves forward in the exact direction indicated by the girl's pointing finger. Follow her pointing direction across the clouds and landscape, gradually leaving the characters behind and revealing the distant Korean traditional building as the visual destination. The movement is a steady forward push with a subtle upward perspective, as if the camera is following her gaze. The bear slowly looks left and right, curiously searching. The girl remains still with her arm extended and finger pointing. No cuts, no camera rotation, no shaking, no sudden movements. Preserve the original environment and 3D animation style. \n\n(4)Large clouds initially obscure the royal tomb. The clouds slowly drift away as if blown by a gentle breeze, gradually revealing the tomb. Simultaneously, the camera steadily pushes forward and zooms in toward the royal tomb. The camera continues moving closer throughout the shot. The \"Who Is It?\" text slowly fades in above the tomb at the same time, becoming gradually brighter and fully visible as the clouds clear. Smooth continuous camera movement, gentle wind, drifting clouds, soft atmospheric motion, cinematic 3D animation, no cuts, no camera shake, no sudden movements. \n\n(5)Cinematic 3D animation, soft golden glow, elegant magical transition.\nThe glowing Korean text \"무령왕\" slowly drifts from its position above the royal tomb to the exact center of the frame. The movement is smooth, elegant, and slightly floating, with no sudden acceleration. As the text moves, the entire background (royal tomb, characters, trees, sky, clouds, landscape) gradually fades into deep black through a smooth cinematic fade-out. The text stays visible and becomes the main focus. Tiny sparkling particles and golden light dust shimmer and float around the text, drifting outward and fading naturally. Subtle warm golden light rays radiate from the letters. Once the background is fully black, the text stays centered and glowing brightly, surrounded by a few twinkling particles and a soft golden halo.\nNo sudden movements, no camera movement or shake, no text distortion. Preserve the exact Korean text \"무령왕\".\n\n\n(6)Soft, dreamy 3D animation with warm glowing lighting and a cute cinematic atmosphere.\nThe glowing Korean text \"무령왕\" slowly breaks apart from its edges into countless tiny sparkling particles, scattering like magical glowing dust. Some sparkles keep floating in the air afterward.\nAs the text disappears, the girl and the bear enter from opposite sides, each riding a soft fluffy white cloud. They fly smoothly toward the center, happily waving at the camera to greet the viewer. Movements are cheerful, gentle, and natural. They stop near the center, floating on their clouds and still waving, the clouds swaying as if in a gentle breeze.\nToward the end, large fluffy clouds drift in from the left and right edges, gradually filling both sides of the frame into a soft cloud-frame around the characters, who stay visible in the center.\nSmooth magical transition, gentle wind, sparkling particle effects. No sudden cuts, no camera shake, no changes to character design or proportions.",
