      "fullPrompt": "[기획 및 구성]\n한국의 자연유산을 한국 전통미술의 물성과 결합하여 초현실적인 하나의 영상으로 표현한다. 두루미, 산양, 원앙, 보은 속리 정이품송, 무주 일원 반딧불이와 그 먹이 서식지를 주요 소재로 활용한다. 나전칠기의 빛, 수묵의 먹, 단청의 색, 한지의 섬유, 반딧불의 빛이 서로 해체되고 재구성되며 다음 자연유산으로 연결되는 구조로 구성한다. 전체적으로 현대적인 미디어아트와 시네마틱한 분위기를 유지한다.\n\n[두루미 × 나전칠기]\nBegin in absolute blackness. A single iridescent Korean mother-of-pearl fragment slowly appears and descends toward a glossy black lacquer surface. When it touches the surface, a subtle ripple spreads and dormant nacre patterns awaken. The mother-of-pearl pieces gradually assemble into a flat Korean najeonchilgi image of a realistic red-crowned crane. Individual nacre feathers begin to lift from the lacquer surface, releasing fine pearl dust. The transformation travels from the wingtip across the body, physically changing the flat 2D inlay into a dimensional living crane. The crane opens its eye, spreads its wings and powerfully launches into the landscape. Preserve realistic red-crowned crane anatomy. No phoenix anatomy, no extra wings, no text.\n\n[두루미 → 산양 × 수묵]\nA single iridescent mother-of-pearl fragment separates from the flying crane and falls toward a calm lake. Follow the fragment closely until it enters the clear water. Deep black Korean ink slowly blooms from around the submerged nacre fragment. Elegant translucent ink tendrils spread organically through the water. The flowing ink gradually suggests the silhouette of a Korean long-tailed goral, Naemorhedus caudatus, with realistic short backward-pointing horns. The abstract ink physically gathers and becomes a dimensional goral emerging into a restrained Korean sumukhwa landscape. Minimal, poetic Korean aesthetics, generous negative space, realistic ink diffusion and water physics.\n\n[산양 × 수묵 → 단청]\nA Korean long-tailed goral moves dynamically through a monochrome Korean sumukhwa landscape. The camera lowers and tracks its front hoof. As the hoof firmly touches a dark rocky surface, deep black ink spreads naturally through the cracks. From within the flowing ink, traditional Korean dancheong colors and patterns gradually awaken: deep teal, jade green, muted vermilion, warm ochre and subtle gold. Clearly show the organic physical transition from monochrome ink into colorful dancheong. Cinematic macro composition, tactile rock, realistic ink physics, sophisticated Korean aesthetics.\n\n[단청 → 원앙]\nThe camera follows the colorful dancheong patterns flowing across the ground. Individual flat dancheong fragments begin to lift naturally into the air. The fragments rotate, separate and physically transform into feather-like forms. These individual colored pieces progressively assemble into one realistic mandarin duck. Preserve recognizable mandarin duck anatomy and characteristic colors. The transformation must clearly show dancheong fragment → feather → living bird. No phoenix, no exaggerated wings, no fantasy tail, no text.\n\n[원앙 → 한지 → 소나무]\nFollow the flying mandarin duck. One dancheong feather fragment separates from the bird and floats through the air. Its pigments gradually peel away as fine particles, revealing pale Korean hanji fibers underneath. The fragment becomes a thin translucent sheet of handmade hanji. As it descends, the paper fibers spread like roots and begin twisting, folding and intertwining upward. Hundreds of hanji fibers physically construct the trunk, branches and needles of a monumental ancient Korean pine tree. The completed tree has a broad balanced crown inspired by Boeun Sokri Jeongipumsong. Cinematic Korean landscape, warm light, atmospheric mist, realistic handmade-paper texture.\n\n[한지 소나무 → 반딧불]\nStart from the monumental pine tree made from delicate Korean hanji. Several white hanji fragments physically detach from its branches and float through the wind. Follow one fragment closely. Its white handmade-paper fibers gradually catch warm golden light. Clearly show five separate physical states: white hanji paper → white hanji with golden fibers → pure golden fibers → microscopic golden particles → one realistic firefly. Do not skip any stage. Only after the paper has completely become golden particles may the particles assemble progressively into the elongated body, dark beetle-like wing covers, reddish thorax, small head, antennae and legs of a realistic Korean firefly. Finally, the bioluminescent organ at the end of the abdomen slowly illuminates yellow-green. No bee anatomy, no moth, no dragonfly, no fantasy insect.\n\n[반딧불 서식지 및 엔딩]\nFollow the single firefly dynamically through grasses and above a clean flowing stream. Gradually pull the camera backward and upward. One firefly becomes several lights, then dozens and hundreds naturally distributed throughout the riverside grasses, wetlands, forest and stream corridor. Their lights pulse independently and irregularly. Continue into a majestic aerial pullback revealing a vast Korean nighttime habitat with a winding stream, wet vegetation, mist and layered mountain ridges. From the enormous distance, the tiny lights create a subtle flowing luminous texture through the landscape, like a natural grain of light. Do not form literal writing or artificial symbols. End with one foreground firefly approaching extremely close to the lens until its yellow-green light becomes a large defocused glow filling the frame, then naturally dim into darkness.\n\n[음악 생성]\n60-second high-energy Korean media-art instrumental, 120–125 BPM. Modern, hypnotic, rhythmic, mysterious and sophisticated. Start immediately with a sharp gayageum motif, deep geomungo strikes and tight janggu pulses, creating forward motion from the first second. Layer fast plucked strings, buk hits, metallic jing textures and airy daegeum accents over a driving cinematic pulse. Keep the rhythm evolving constantly with short breaks, sudden accents, accelerating patterns and dynamic transitions, matching rapid visual transformations of material and nature. Build intensity continuously toward the final third with powerful Korean percussion, dense rhythmic gayageum and shimmering metallic textures. Contemporary digital-heritage exhibition sound, artistic and immersive, not traditional folk music. No slow ambient intro, no sentimental melody, no sadness, no epic orchestra, no vocals, no lyrics, no trot, no pop, no EDM drop.\n\n[영상 생성 공통 지시]\nCinematic photorealism, sophisticated Korean aesthetics, physically believable material transformations, dynamic camera movement, strong depth and parallax, realistic natural motion. No text or logos. No background music generated in the video clips. Use only natural environmental sounds such as wind, water, paper fibers, wing movement and ambient nature sounds.",
