oreground carefully carry the wooden platform together at the same pace.\nThe stone guardian beast remains firmly and safely placed on the platform.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nPreserve the guardian beast EXACTLY as shown in the starting image.\nDo not change its face, horn, body, proportions, size, stone color, or texture.\n\nThe guardian beast is a completely motionless stone sculpture.\nNo eye movement, no blinking, no head movement, no mouth movement, no body movement.\n\nThe royal coffin behind them is carried slowly and steadily by the attendants.\nThe mourners follow quietly with lowered heads.\n\nPreserve the main craftsman's face, hairstyle, clothing, and identity exactly as shown in the starting image.\n\nCAMERA:\nA slow cinematic backward tracking shot as the procession approaches the camera.\nKeep the guardian beast and royal coffin clearly visible throughout the scene.\nStable cinematic camera.\nNo sudden camera movement.\n\nMOVEMENT:\nSlow, solemn, respectful walking.\nNatural human body movement.\nSubtle realistic movement of clothing from walking and wind.\nNo running.\nNo exaggerated gestures.\n\nAUDIO:\nNatural slow footsteps on the ground.\nSoft wind.\nSubtle clothing movement.\nQuiet and solemn royal funeral ambience.\nNo dialogue.\nNo background music.\n\nSerious, restrained, emotional atmosphere.\nHigh-end Korean historical drama.\nPhotorealistic live-action.\n\nNo fantasy effects.\nNo transformation.\nNo modern objects.\nNo text, subtitles, or logos.\n\n\n[영상3]\n\n6-second realistic cinematic continuous shot.\nUse the provided first frame as the exact starting frame\nand the provided last frame as the exact ending frame.\nThe craftsman carries the heavy stone guardian beast alone with both arms\nand slowly walks toward its final position.\nThe stone guardian is extremely heavy.\n\nHe holds it low and tightly against his body with both arms.\nHis back is bent forward under the weight.\nHis shoulders and arms are visibly tense.\nHis knees are slightly bent.\nHe takes short, slow, heavy, difficult steps.\nHis entire body shows genuine physical strain.\nHe briefly adjusts his grip because of the weight,\nthen continues struggling forward.\n\nCAMERA:\n\nThe camera follows the craftsman as he moves.\nIt travels WITH him in the SAME direction he is walking,\nfrom a natural three-quarter side-rear angle.\nSmooth forward follow shot.\nMaintain a natural medium-wide distance. \n\nDo NOT zoom in.\nDo NOT make a close-up.\nDo NOT move backward in front of him.\nDo NOT orbit around him.\n\nNear the end,\nthe craftsman reaches the exact position shown in the provided last frame.\nStill struggling with the weight,\nhe bends his knees deeply and slowly lowers the stone guardian onto the floor.\nThe lowering must look physically difficult and heavy.\n\nFinish naturally in the exact composition and position of the provided last frame.\nPreserve the craftsman, stone guardian, tomb, scale, proportions,\nclothing, lighting and appearance from the provided frames.\n\nNo morphing.\nNo size change.\nNo extra people.\nNo extra objects.\nNo camera cuts.\nNo effortless carrying. \n\n\n[영상 4]\n\nCUT 6 — 10-second cinematic live-action scene.\n\nUse the provided image as the exact first frame.\nContinue naturally from this exact moment.\n\nThe craftsman looks down at the stone guardian and speaks quietly and seriously in Korean:\n\n“악한 것을 막고… 왕께서 가시는 길을 잘 지켜다오.”\n\nHe begins to turn away.\n\nAfter a brief pause, a quiet voice is heard:\n\nSTONE GUARDIAN VOICE:\n“저기요.”\n\nThe craftsman suddenly stops, surprised.\nHe slowly turns back toward the stone guardian and asks:\n\nCRAFTSMAN:\n“왜?”\n\nWithout moving at all, the stone guardian’s voice replies:\n\n“언제까지요?”\n\nThe craftsman freezes and stares at the stone guardian,\ncompletely caught off guard and unable to answer.\n\nEnd on his silent, confused reaction.\n\nCAMERA:\nOne continuous cinematic medium shot.\nKeep both the craftsman and the stone guardian visible.\nVery subtle natural camera movement.\nNo close-up and no dramatic camera movement.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nPreserve the exact appearance of the first frame.\nThe stone guardian remains completely motionless.\nIts mouth, eyes, head and body NEVER move.\nOnly its voice is heard.\n\nDo not change the stone guardian’s shape, size or proportions.\nDo not change the craftsman’s face, hair or clothing.\nDo not change the tomb, lighting or composition.\nNo king.\nNo additional people.\nNo morphing.\nNo fantasy effects.\nNo animated statue.\nNo subtitles or on-screen text.\n\n\n[영상 5]\n\nCUT 7 — 12-second cinematic live-action scene.\n\nUse the provided image as the exact first frame.\nContinue naturally from this exact moment.\n\nThe craftsman is crouching beside the stone guardian,\nstaring at it in surprise after hearing its question.\n\n[0–2 sec]\nThe craftsman remains frozen for a moment,\nlooking startled and confused.\nHe says nothing.\n\n[2–5 sec]\nStill confused, he slowly stands up naturally.\nHe gives the stone guardian one last uneasy look.\nHe does not answer.\n\n[5–8 sec]\nThe craftsman turns toward the FRONT OF THE FRAME,\ntoward the camera, and walks naturally toward the camera.\n\nHe exits completely through the unseen tomb entrance\nlocated OFF-SCREEN on the camera side.\n\nHe does NOT walk toward the rear wall.\n\n[8–9 sec]\nThe craftsman is completely out of frame.\n\nBrief silence.\n\nA heavy tomb door closes OFF-SCREEN near the camera.\n\nSOUND:\nOne single deep, heavy “BANG!”\n\nDo NOT show the door.\n\n[9–10 sec]\nComplete silence.\n\nHold on the stone guardian alone inside the tomb.\n\n[10–12 sec]\nThe stone guardian remains perfectly motionless.\n\nOnly its quiet voice is heard in Korean:\n\nSTONE GUARDIAN VOICE:\n“…대답은 해주고 가지.”\n\nEnd immediately after the line.\n\nCAMERA:\nOne continuous cinematic medium-wide shot.\nKeep the camera nearly locked.\nMaintain the exact composition and direction of the first frame.\nNo cuts and no new camera angle.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nPreserve the exact craftsman, stone guardian,\ntomb interior, lighting, scale and composition from the first frame.\n\nThe stone guardian is a solid stone artifact.\nIt NEVER physically moves.\nIts mouth NEVER moves.\nIts eyes NEVER move.\nIts head and body NEVER move.\nThe voice is heard ONLY as a voice.\n\nThe craftsman exits toward the CAMERA / FRONT OF FRAME.\n\nDo NOT create a doorway on the rear wall.\nDo NOT show or generate a visible door.\nThe tomb door closes completely OFF-SCREEN.\n\nNO smoke.\nNO dust.\nNO fog.\nNO mist.\nNO steam.\nNO particles.\nNO vibration effects.\nNO light effects.\nNothing comes out of the stone guardian.\n\nNo king.\nNo additional people.\nNo new objects.\nNo morphing.\nNo fantasy effects.\nNo subtitles.\nNo on-screen text.\n\n\n[영상 6]\n\n10-second cinematic passage-of-time scene.\n\nUse the provided image as the EXACT first frame.\n\nCRITICAL PRIORITY:\nThe stone guardian in the foreground must remain\n100% IDENTICAL to the reference image for the entire video.\n\nLOCK THE STONE GUARDIAN COMPLETELY.\n\nDo not change its color.\nDo not change its lighting.\nDo not change its brightness.\nDo not change its texture.\nDo not change its surface.\nDo not change its shape.\nDo not change its size.\nDo not change its position.\nDo not age it.\nDo not darken it.\nDo not desaturate it.\nDo not apply any time effect to it.\n\nThe stone guardian must look like a perfectly frozen element\nfrom the original image from beginning to end.\n\nONLY THE BACKGROUND BEHIND THE STONE GUARDIAN\nshows the passage of approximately 1,400 years.\n\n[0–2 seconds]\n\nThe stone guardian remains visually unchanged.\n\nIn the BACKGROUND ONLY,\nthe warm ancient tomb lighting begins to fade.\n\nLight and shadow slowly sweep across the rear walls and ceiling.\n\n[2–7 seconds]\n\nShow centuries passing cinematically\nONLY through the tomb background.\n\nThe background transitions rapidly through changing light,\ndarkness and historical cinematic tones.\n\nWarm ancient background →\ndesaturated background →\nmonochrome background →\ndeep darkness →\nfaded historical background →\ndeep darkness.\n\nCreate elegant waves of light and shadow\nmoving across the walls and ceiling,\nsuggesting centuries rushing past.\n\nThe rhythm gradually accelerates,\nlike 1,400 years passing in seconds.\n\nDO NOT apply these changes to the stone guardian.\n\nThe stone guardian remains exactly identical\nto the original first-frame image.\n\n[7–9 seconds]\n\nThe background time transitions gradually slow down.\n\nThe tomb background settles into deep darkness.\n\nThe stone guardian remains unchanged and clearly recognizable.\n\n[9–10 seconds]\n\nA faint natural light appears in the BACKGROUND\nfrom the unseen entrance on the camera side,\nsuggesting the tomb is about to be discovered.\n\nEnd before any person appears.\n\nCAMERA:\nCompletely locked.\nNo zoom.\nNo pan.\nNo camera movement.\nNo cuts.\n\nABSOLUTE RULE:\nBACKGROUND CHANGES ONLY.\n\nSTONE GUARDIAN = COMPLETELY FROZEN REFERENCE ELEMENT.\n\nNo visual effect may pass over,\ncover, recolor, distort or transform the stone guardian.\n\nNo movement.\nNo dialogue.\nNo mouth movement.\nNo eye movement.\nNo head movement.\nNo body movement.\n\nNO smoke.\nNO fog.\nNO dust.\nNO particles.\nNO magical effects.\nNO people.\nNO new objects.\nNO numbers.\nNO text.\nNO subtitles.\n\n\n[영상 7]\n\n8-second cinematic historical scene, Korea, 1971.\n\nUse the first reference image as the exact START FRAME.\nUse the second reference image as the exact END FRAME.\n\n0–3 sec:\nThe crouching worker carefully clears a small amount of soil\naround the partially exposed ancient brick structure.\n\nHis hand tool gently touches an unexpected brick.\nA subtle “툭” sound.\n\nHe immediately stops and looks closely at the brick.\nDo not break or damage it.\n\n3–5.5 sec:\nThe second worker notices his reaction\nand leans slightly closer.\n\nThe crouching worker looks at the exposed brickwork\nand naturally says in Korean:\n\n“잠깐만요… 여기 뭔가 있는데요?”\n\nBoth men stop working and stare at the unusual structure.\n\n5.5–6.5 sec:\nA brief quiet pause.\nThey remain still, realizing they have discovered something important.\n\n6.5–8 sec:\nHARD CINEMATIC CUT to the dark tomb interior.\n\nThe final shot must match the provided END FRAME exactly:\nthe stone guardian alone inside the tomb,\ncompletely motionless and unchanged.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT morph the excavation site into the tomb.\nUse a clean cinematic CUT between the two locations.\n\nDo NOT show the stone guardian outside.\nDo NOT open or destroy the tomb entrance.\nDo NOT break bricks.\nDo NOT add people.\nDo NOT alter the final stone guardian.\nNo movement of its eyes, mouth, head or body.\nNo smoke, fog, dust clouds or fantasy effects.\nNo subtitles or text.\n\nNatural Korean dialogue.\nSubtle realistic movement.\nHistorically grounded 1971 Korea.\nRealistic cinematic documentary style.\n\n\n[영상 8]\n\n12-second cinematic scene.\n\nUse the dark tomb image as the EXACT START FRAME.\nUse the modern museum image as the reference\nfor the final museum environment, mother and son.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThe stone guardian is the SAME artifact throughout the entire scene.\nIt must remain visually identical and completely motionless.\n\n0–3 sec:\nBegin inside the dark ancient tomb.\n\nFrom the FIRST FRAME,\na single strong handheld flashlight beam from OFF-SCREEN\nis already shining directly onto the stone guardian.\n\nThe flashlight beam stays FIXED on the stone guardian.\nIt does NOT sweep, search, shake or move around.\n\nThe surrounding tomb remains dark.\n\nThe fixed light slowly becomes brighter,\ngradually revealing the stone guardian more clearly.\n\nDo NOT show the flashlight or the person holding it.\n\n3–6 sec:\nThe light on the stone guardian continues to brighten.\n\nUse the bright illuminated stone guardian\nas the visual anchor for a slow, elegant cinematic transition.\n\nThe dark ancient tomb gradually OVERLAPS\nwith a modern museum exhibition hall.\n\nThe ancient brick walls slowly fade away\nwhile the modern museum environment gradually appears.\n\nThe flashlight illumination naturally transforms\ninto warm museum exhibition lighting.\n\nThis must feel like the passage of time,\nNOT like teleportation or magic.\n\nThroughout the transition,\nthe stone guardian remains visually fixed.\n\nDo NOT morph, rotate, resize or redesign it.\n\n6–8 sec:\nThe transition is now complete.\n\nWe are fully inside the modern museum.\n\nThe same stone guardian is displayed\nin the museum exactly as shown in the reference image.\n\nThe mother and her young son naturally walk\ninto the scene together from the side.\n\nThey walk slowly toward the stone guardian.\n\n8–9.5 sec:\nThe mother and son arrive in front of the exhibit.\n\nThey naturally slow down and stop.\n\nThe boy looks curiously at the stone guardian.\n\nThe mother stands beside him.\n\nBoth quietly observe it for a moment.\n\n9.5–12 sec:\nThe boy turns slightly toward his mother\nand naturally asks in Korean:\n\n“엄마, 얘는 여기 얼마나 있었어?”\n\nThe mother looks at the stone guardian\nand gently answers in Korean:\n\n“아주 오랫동안.”\n\nAfter answering,\nthey both quietly look at the stone guardian.\n\nHold this final moment naturally.\n\nEND.\n\nCRITICAL CONTINUITY:\n\nThe stone guardian must remain EXACTLY identical\nfrom the ancient tomb to the modern museum.\n\nSame face.\nSame horn.\nSame body.\nSame proportions.\nSame size.\nSame carvings.\nSame color.\nSame stone texture.\n\nThe stone guardian is an INANIMATE STONE ARTIFACT.\n\nNO eye movement.\nNO mouth movement.\nNO head movement.\nNO body movement.\n\nNO morphing.\nNO resizing.\nNO rotation.\nNO redesign.\n\nAt the beginning,\nthe flashlight beam is ALREADY shining directly\non the stone guardian.\n\nDO NOT sweep the flashlight around.\nDO NOT show the flashlight.\nDO NOT show the investigator.\n\nDuring the transition,\nONLY the surrounding environment changes.\n\nThe mother and son appear ONLY AFTER\nthe museum environment has formed.\n\nThey walk naturally,\nstop naturally,\nthen speak.\n\nNo extra people near them.\nNo smoke.\nNo fog.\nNo dust clouds.\nNo particles.\nNo magical effects.\nNo fantasy effects.\nNo subtitles.\nNo generated text.\n\nRealistic cinematic live-action.\nNatural Korean dialogue.\nSlow controlled pacing.\nSubtle realistic acting.\nQuiet emotional atmosphere.\n\n\n[영상 9]\n\n8-second cinematic final scene.\n\nUse the provided museum image as the EXACT START FRAME.\n\nSTRICT ACTION ORDER:\nDo NOT skip any action.\nThe mother and son MUST physically walk out of the frame\nBEFORE the camera moves into a close-up.\n\n0–2.5 sec — MOTHER AND SON LEAVE:\n\nBegin exactly from the provided image.\n\nThe mother is crouching beside her son,\nlooking at the stone guardian.\n\nFIRST, the mother naturally stands up.\n\nThe mother and son then turn away from the stone guardian\nand WALK TOGETHER toward the side of the frame.\n\nShow several clear, natural walking steps.\n\nThey continue walking until BOTH the mother and son\nCOMPLETELY EXIT THE FRAME.\n\nTheir departure must be clearly visible on screen.\n\nDO NOT cut away while they are walking.\nDO NOT zoom in yet.\nDO NOT move the camera yet.\n\nThe camera stays completely still\nand watches them leave.\n\n2.5–3 sec — EMPTY MOMENT:\n\nThe mother and son are now completely gone.\n\nFor a brief moment,\nthe stone guardian remains alone in the quiet museum.\n\n3–5 sec — CLOSE-UP AND MEMORY:\n\nONLY NOW,\nafter the mother and son have completely left,\nthe camera begins a slow cinematic push-in\ntoward the stone guardian's face.\n\nMove gradually into a clear close-up.\n\nAs the camera approaches the face,\nthe museum ambience becomes quieter.\n\nFaint voices from the distant past begin to return,\nlike an old memory echoing across 1,448 years.\n\nThe ancient craftsman's distant Korean voice:\n\n“악한 것을 막고…\n왕께서 가시는 길을 잘 지켜다오.”\n\nThen the stone guardian's distant voice\nfrom the ancient past:\n\n“언제까지요?”\n\nThese are ONLY distant memories.\n\nDO NOT show the past visually.\nDO NOT show the craftsman.\nDO NOT create flashbacks.\nDO NOT change the museum environment.\n\n5–6.5 sec — PRESENT:\n\nThe camera has now reached\na close-up of the stone guardian's face.\n\nBrief silence.\n\nThen the present-day stone guardian quietly says\nin Korean:\n\n“…이 정도면 됐나.”\n\nThe dialogue is VOICE ONLY.\n\nThe mouth must NOT move while speaking.\n\n6.5–8 sec — FINAL SMILE:\n\nONLY AFTER the final dialogue is completely finished,\nthe stone guardian forms a restrained,\nknowing and satisfied smile.\n\nThe eyes gently narrow into smiling eyes.\n\nAt the same time,\nthe corners of the carved mouth rise only slightly.\n\nThe mouth remains CLOSED.\n\nThis is a clear smile,\nbut subtle and controlled.\n\nIt should feel like the stone guardian\nhas finally completed its long duty.\n\nNo exaggerated smile.\nNo cartoon expression.\nNo teeth.\nNo open mouth.\nNo blinking.\nNo pupil movement.\nNo head movement.\nNo body movement.\n\nHold the quiet, satisfied smile.\n\nCUT TO BLACK.\n\n\nCRITICAL CONTINUITY:\n\nKeep the stone guardian EXACTLY identical\nto the provided start image.\n\nDo NOT change its face, horn, body,\nproportions, size, carvings, color or stone texture.\n\nSTRICT SEQUENCE:\n\n1. Mother stands up.\n2. Mother and son walk away together.\n3. BOTH completely leave the frame.\n4. Stone guardian is left alone.\n5. Camera slowly pushes into its face.\n6. Past voices are heard.\n7. “…이 정도면 됐나.”\n8. Eyes smile + mouth corners rise slightly.\n9. Cut to black.\n\nNEVER change this order.\n\nNo visual flashback.\nNo ghost images.\nNo ancient tomb appearing.\nNo craftsman appearing.\nNo transition to the past.\nNo extra people.\nNo magical effects.\nNo smoke.\nNo fog.\nNo particles.\nNo subtitles.\nNo generated text.\n\nRealistic cinematic live-action.\nNatural human walking motion.\nQuiet emotional ending.",
