      "postEditingDetails": "사용함 — CapCut(컷 편집, 전환, 음향 믹스, 타이틀 합성, 4K 업스케일 내보내기)",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "〈진묘수의 꿈〉 사용 프롬프트 (이미지 생성 — ChatGPT)\n※ 생성 과정 캡처 5장에 해당하는 이미지 프롬프트 원문입니다. 24컷 전체의 이미지·영상·음악 프롬프트 원문은 캡처 zip 안의 「진묘수의_꿈_프롬프트전문.pdf」에 수록했습니다.\n\n■ 최초 캐릭터 — 벽돌 진묘수\nA mythical guardian beast based on the stone Jinmyosu (tomb guardian) of King Muryeong's tomb, Baekje Kingdom, Korea. Keep the original silhouette exactly: a squat, stocky quadruped with a pig-like rounded snout, a single short iron horn on the forehead, small stubby wings on both flanks, thick short legs, body slightly crouched as if about to stand up. Height about that of a large dog.\n\nIts entire body is built from ancient Baekje tomb bricks: rectangular grey-brown fired clay bricks, each about the size of a hand, stamped with a lotus-flower relief pattern on the visible face (the lotus-pattern bricks of King Muryeong's tomb chamber). The bricks are stacked and interlocked in a curved herringbone pattern following the beast's body, exactly like the tomb walls, with dark mortar lines between them. Surface is weathered, slightly damp, moss in a few joints. The bricks are real archaeological brick, NOT cubes, NOT voxel, NOT Minecraft — irregular fired clay with chipped edges. A few bricks near the tail are floating slightly apart from the body, as if the beast is still assembling itself. Faint blue-white light leaks from the gaps between bricks.\n\nSetting: pitch-black void, a wet dark stone floor with faint reflection. Single hard light source from upper left, rim light on the back edge. No other objects.\n\nCamera: three-quarter front view, eye level, 85mm lens, shallow depth of field, the beast looks slightly past the camera. Photorealistic, cinematic, film still quality, ultra-detailed clay and mortar texture, 16:9.\n\n■ 컷 11 — 벽돌에서 꽃으로\nUse the first attached image as the exact reference for the beast's BEFORE state, the second attached image as the exact reference for its AFTER state, and the third attached image as the world reference. Same creature, same proportions throughout.\n\nDreamlike, painterly, mystical — NOT photorealistic. An endless sea of still black water under a dark sky with a pale full moon. Rising from the water, enormous lotus flowers the size of houses, petals white at the tips, blush pink in the middle, warm gold at the base, glowing from within like lanterns. Pink-gold mist drifts between them, countless loose petals float in the air. In the far distance, mountains drawn like soft ink-wash brushstrokes — no buildings, no temples, no pagodas on the mountains. The black water mirrors everything. Mid shot, three-quarter front view, at the edge of the black water with a giant glowing lotus behind. The Jinmyosu mid-transformation: a squat stocky quadruped, wide flat pig-like snout, branched rusted iron horn on top of the head, scroll wings on the shoulders, thick short legs, short stumpy tail. The rear half and hind legs are still weathered grey-brown lotus-relief bricks with dark mortar lines; the front half, head and front legs are already thousands of layered translucent lotus petals — white tips, blush pink middles, warm gold bases — glowing from within. Along the seam bricks crack and fall while petals push through. Fallen bricks in the shallow water, loose petals floating. Eyes two points of amber light. Luminous, soft, ethereal, painterly — like a dream painted with light and mist; rich color, cinematic composition, ultra-detailed, NOT photorealistic, 16:9.\n\n■ 컷 12 — 연꽃 진묘수\nUse the first attached image as the exact character reference — same creature, same head, same horn, same body, same proportions. Use the second attached image as the reference for the scene and composition: the black water, the small lotus flowers blooming on the water where the creature has stepped, the giant glowing lotus flowers, the ink-wash mountains, the moon, the colors and mood.\n\nDreamlike, painterly, mystical — NOT photorealistic.\n\nLow side shot at water level, pure side profile exactly like the first image. The creature is LARGE in the frame — its body fills about half the frame width, left of center — walking slowly toward the LEFT side of the frame, one front foot lifted mid-step. The head is exactly as in the first image and held LEVEL, not raised: a long, broad, flat box-shaped muzzle projecting straight forward, the mouth one long straight horizontal line along the side of the muzzle (NOT a short snout, NOT an upturned nose, NOT a smile); the eye a tiny point of amber light. On the crown, the horn exactly as in the first image: large, thick, dark rusted iron, with a broad flat branching lobe reaching forward, about as long as the head. Small flat spiral-scroll ornaments on the shoulders. Body entirely of small soft flat petals like fur, white tips, blush pink middles, warm gold bases, glowing from within. The body ends at the rump with a short tuft, exactly as in the first image; nothing trails behind it. No bricks anywhere.\n\nOn the black water behind it, spaced apart like footprints, small glowing lotus flowers have just bloomed where its feet stepped, each separate and not touching the creature; under its lifted front foot a new bud is just opening. Giant glowing lotus flowers and the moon behind.\n\nLuminous, soft, ethereal, painterly — like a dream painted with light and mist; rich color, cinematic composition, ultra-detailed, NOT photorealistic, 16:9.\n\n■ 컷 18 — 꽃잎에서 빛으로\nUse the first attached image as the exact character reference — same creature, same materials, same proportions — and the second attached image as the world reference: keep its environment, colors, scale and mood, repainted for this shot.\n\nDreamlike, painterly, mystical — NOT photorealistic. An endless sea of still black water under a dark sky with a pale full moon. Rising from the water, enormous lotus flowers the size of houses, petals white at the tips, blush pink in the middle, warm gold at the base, glowing from within like lanterns. Pink-gold mist drifts between them, countless loose petals float in the air. In the far distance, mountains drawn like soft ink-wash brushstrokes — no buildings, no temples, no pagodas on the mountains. The black water mirrors everything. Extreme macro shot on the SHOULDER of the Lotus Jinmyosu, filling the frame — only a patch of the shoulder is visible, with the scroll-shaped wing curl at one edge: a surface of thousands of layered translucent lotus petals, white at the tips, blush pink in the middle, warm gold at the base, glowing from within, lying smooth like fur. The tips of several petals are igniting into pure golden light — not fire, but thin lines of gold light tracing along the petal edges and veins, the petal turning transparent and luminous behind them, tiny gold particles lifting off. NO head, NO horn, NO eyes, NO legs in this frame — just the shoulder surface. Behind, soft-focus, the black water is beginning to glint gold. Luminous, soft, ethereal, painterly — like a dream painted with light and mist; rich color, cinematic composition, ultra-detailed, NOT photorealistic, 16:9.\n\n■ 컷 20 — 빛 진묘수, 공산성\nUse the first attached image as the exact character reference — same creature, same materials, same proportions — and the second attached image as the world reference: keep its environment, colors, scale and mood, repainted for this shot.\n\nDreamlike, painterly, mystical — NOT photorealistic. A sky of deep burnt reddish-brown lacquer — dark, matte, like an old lacquered Baekje headrest — with flakes and drifts of applied gold leaf across it; NO sun, NO sunset, NO orange glow. Beneath, mountains drawn like ink-wash brushstrokes float in white mist. Gongsanseong Fortress of Gongju, Korea: a weathered grey stone rampart of Baekje masonry running along the ridge and descending to the river; a wooden two-storey gate pavilion with a tiled roof by the water. The Geum River curves below as a river of liquid gold light, the lights of Gongju city scattered as gold dust along its far bank. Only two or three small yellow flags far along the wall. No other buildings, no temples, no pagodas.\n\nLow side tracking shot on the wall path, pure side profile like the first image. The Light Jinmyosu walks slowly along the top of the rampart toward the LEFT side of the frame, head on the left, one front foot lifted mid-step: squat stocky body, broad flat blunt muzzle, one short branched horn of dark rusted iron on the crown — solid, opaque, NOT glowing, NOT made of light, the only dark solid element on the luminous body, small flat spiral-scroll ornaments on the shoulders, thick short legs, the whole body woven from thin lines of golden light in a sparse curling flame-and-vine openwork pattern, semi-transparent, brighter at the edges, eyes two tiny white-gold points. Its body ends clearly at its rump with a very short stumpy tail; nothing trails behind it. Under each of its feet the old stones of the wall glow gold where it has stepped, the glow fading behind it like footprints of light. Beyond the wall below, the golden river and the gold-dust city lights; gold leaf drifts across the lacquer sky.\n\nLuminous, soft, ethereal, painterly — like a dream painted with light and mist; rich color, cinematic composition, ultra-detailed, NOT photorealistic, 16:9.",
