      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "제출 폼의 글자 수 제한으로 실제 사용한 원문 프롬프트에서 핵심 제작 지시사항을 중심으로 축약하여 기재하였습니다.\n\n[CLIP 1 — 10 SECONDS]\n\nCreate a cinematic opening inspired by the visual language of the Gold Diadem Ornaments of King Muryeong.\n\nBegin with an extreme macro view of ultra-fine handcrafted gold details in deep blue-black darkness:\npierced openwork,\nthin engraved curves,\ntiny gold-wire-like ornament,\nsmall bead-like details,\nfloral-vine motifs.\n\nGradually extend the gold linework into organic asymmetrical branching inspired by vines, flowers, and flame-like upward curves.\n\nReveal a richer field of layered gold craftsmanship at different depths.\n\nEnd by guiding the many gold lines and reflections into one elegant flowing diagonal direction that exits the frame and prepares Clip 2.\n\nKeep the materials photorealistic, refined, luxurious, and physically believable.\n\nAvoid:\nliteral crown reveal,\nsymmetry,\ncentered emblem,\nwearable jewelry presentation,\nthick gold ribbons,\npeople,\nneon,\nholograms,\nmagic,\ntext,\nlogos.\n\n16:9 horizontal.\n4K detail.\n24fps.\nPremium Korean heritage art-film cinematography.\n\n\n[CLIP 2 — 10 SECONDS]\n\nUse the final frame of Clip 1 as the continuity reference.\n\nContinue the final gold-line direction briefly, then use a natural foreground occlusion to create a clean cinematic match cut.\n\nAfter the transition, the ornamental gold line disappears completely and becomes real sunlight reflected on the Geumgang River in Gongju.\n\nThe river must look physically real:\ndark blue-gray water,\nsubtle ripples,\nsoft broken golden reflections,\nnatural movement.\n\nSlowly raise the camera and reveal the Geumgang River, riverbank, and Gongsanseong.\n\nShow Gongsanseong as a believable historic fortress landscape with fortress walls, wooded hillside contours, and the riverside setting.\n\nEnd on a calm wide shot of the Geumgang and Gongsanseong that naturally prepares Clip 3.\n\nAvoid:\ngold patterns floating on water,\nmetal river,\nliquid gold,\nmorphing,\nfantasy palace,\nfake Baekje architecture,\nmodern skyline,\npeople,\ntext,\nlogos.\n\n16:9 horizontal.\n4K detail.\n24fps.\nPhotorealistic cinematic environment.\n\n\n[CLIP 3 — 10 SECONDS]\n\nUse the final frame of Clip 2 as the EXACT opening frame.\n\nPreserve the Geumgang, Gongsanseong, terrain, and camera composition at the beginning.\n\nFine warm-gold filigree inspired by the Gold Diadem Ornaments of King Muryeong begins spreading through:\nthe river interior,\nriver boundary,\nsurrounding terrain,\nand visible Gongsanseong contours.\n\nUse:\nultra-fine branching filigree,\npierced-metal-like curves,\nasymmetrical vine rhythms,\nsmall floral branching,\nflame-like extensions,\ntiny bead-like ornaments,\nfine twisted-wire craftsmanship.\n\nDo not redesign Gongsanseong.\n\nUse one smooth dark transition.\n\nThen reveal a traditional Korean settlement from a VERY HIGH TRUE NADIR aerial view.\n\nCAMERA PITCH: EXACTLY -90 DEGREES.\nNO horizon.\nNO oblique angle.\n\nShow many tiled-roof houses, thatched-roof houses, courtyards, paths, low walls, and earthen areas.\n\nThe drone moves slowly forward while numerous fine gold streams move faster through the settlement.\n\nThe gold must travel through three-dimensional architectural height:\npath\n→ wall\n→ eave\n→ roof\n→ roof ridge.\n\nSmall ornamental floral details may briefly emerge from the moving lines, but the FLOWING GOLD LINE remains the main subject.\n\nKeep correct perspective, occlusion, metallic reflection, and physical realism.\n\nEnd with the gold still actively moving toward the edge of the frame, preparing Clip 4.\n\nCOMPLETELY SILENT VIDEO.\nNO AUDIO TRACK.\nNO MUSIC.\nNO SOUND EFFECTS.\n\n16:9 horizontal.\n4K detail.\n24fps.\nPhotorealistic.\n\n\n[CLIP 4 — 10 SECONDS]\n\nUse the FINAL FRAME of the EDITED Clip 3 as the exact opening continuity reference.\n\nProgress visually from:\n\nordinary settlement\n→ larger fortified historical space\n→ formal gate and courtyard\n→ prestigious tiled-roof architectural group.\n\nCreate a historically restrained and believable elite / royal precinct atmosphere.\n\nDo NOT invent a fantasy Baekje palace.\n\nContinue the slow forward drone movement.\n\nGradually reveal:\nstronger defensive boundaries,\na substantial formal gate,\nwider paths,\na broad courtyard,\nlarger tiled-roof buildings,\nand clearer architectural hierarchy.\n\nVery gradually shift the camera from the high aerial view toward an approximately 45-degree elevated perspective.\n\nGold filigree becomes more concentrated around the important architectural zone.\n\nMove fine gold streams across:\nfortress boundaries,\ngate edges,\nformal pathways,\ncourtyard borders,\neaves,\nlarge tiled roofs,\nroof ridges,\nwooden structural edges.\n\nKeep the gold inspired by the Gold Diadem Ornament:\nfine branching metalwork,\npierced-openwork curves,\nasymmetrical vine rhythms,\nsmall floral branching,\nflame-like extensions,\ntiny bead-like ornament,\ntwisted-wire detail.\n\nNear the end, one group of fine gold craftsmanship moves closer to the camera, revealing more microscopic detail and preparing Clip 5.\n\nCOMPLETELY SILENT VIDEO.\nNO AUDIO TRACK.\nNO MUSIC.\nNO SOUND EFFECTS.\n\n16:9 horizontal.\n4K detail.\n24fps.\nPhotorealistic.\n\n\n[CLIP 5 — 10 SECONDS]\n\nUse the FINAL FRAME of Clip 4 as the exact opening continuity reference.\n\nPreserve the same camera direction, lighting, moving gold lines, and visual rhythm.\n\nThe existing gold lines continue naturally out of the architectural space into a deep charcoal-black environment.\n\nKeep the composition strongly asymmetrical.\n\nThe moving gold lines cross and branch into an open network of extremely fine gold craftsmanship.\n\nCreate:\nultra-fine pierced-metal-like curves,\nirregular vine-like branching,\nsmall floral details,\ntiny bead-shaped accents,\nfine twisted-wire-like connections,\nlong flame-like curved extensions,\ndelicate openwork patterns.\n\nDo NOT assemble the gold into one solid object.\n\nDo NOT create a complete silhouette, mirrored sides, or a central peak.\n\nGradually increase the density and richness of the craftsmanship.\n\nUse foreground, midground, and background filigree to create strong depth.\n\nThe camera slowly approaches one intricate off-center region.\n\nFinish with a refined macro view of:\nfine openwork,\ntiny bead-shaped details,\nsmall floral branching,\ndelicate vine-like curves,\nlong flame-like lines.\n\nThe gold remains active until the final frame.\n\nCamera:\nslow forward glide,\nsubtle lateral movement,\nno orbit,\nno rotation,\nno circular movement,\nno zoom-out.\n\nCOMPLETELY SILENT VIDEO.\nNO AUDIO TRACK.\nNO MUSIC.\nNO SOUND EFFECTS.\n\n16:9 horizontal.\n4K detail.\n24fps.\nPhotorealistic.\nPremium Korean heritage art-film cinematography.",
