      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "[A] 배경 이미지 생성 프롬프트\nCreate a refined 16:9 Korean media-art style background on a clean white backdrop.\n\nThe composition should contain only three symbolic elements:\n1) Gongsanseong Fortress,\n2) a glowing swallow made of gold light and black ink-like brush trails,\n3) the royal tomb of King Muryeong.\n\nArrange them elegantly in one unified composition:\n- Gongsanseong Fortress on one side,\n- the luminous swallow near the upper middle area,\n- the royal tomb on the opposite side.\n\nNo road, no extra landscape, no unnecessary decorative objects.\nKeep the composition clean, minimal, and balanced.\n\nThe overall style should feel like elegant Korean digital media art:\nsoft white background, warm golden light, delicate black ink lines, subtle glowing particles, restrained and sophisticated atmosphere.\n\nThe fortress and tomb should look symbolic and beautiful rather than overly realistic.\nThe swallow should feel alive and radiant, formed with flowing gold light and ink-like motion.\n\nNo text, no logo, no frame.\nHigh detail, elegant, poetic, 16:9.\n\n[B] 여자 소리꾼 이미지 생성 프롬프트\nUse the fixed female pansori singer reference exactly.\n\nCreate a 16:9 cinematic upper-body image of a Korean female pansori singer performing in front of the provided media-art background.\n\nKeep her identity, face, hairstyle, hanbok colors, and proportions exactly consistent with the reference.\nShe wears an ivory jeogori and dark navy chima, with neat traditional styling.\n\nShe is singing pansori while holding an open folding fan in one hand.\nHer expression should be expressive and focused, with her mouth open naturally in the middle of singing.\nThe pose should feel elegant, restrained, and traditional.\n\nUse the provided background as the visual setting:\na clean white media-art composition with Gongsanseong Fortress, a glowing swallow made of gold light and ink-like trails, and the royal tomb of King Muryeong.\n\nKeep the singer as the main subject.\nFrame her in an upper-body composition so the face remains sharp and clear, even if parts of the background are partially obscured.\nNo face distortion, no blur, no extra people, no text.\n\nElegant Korean digital-art atmosphere, high detail, 16:9.\n\n[C] 남자 고수 이미지 생성 프롬프트\nUse the fixed male drummer reference exactly.\n\nCreate a 16:9 cinematic upper-body-to-medium shot of a young Korean male gosu playing a traditional Korean drum in front of the provided media-art background.\n\nKeep his identity, face, gat, ivory robe, dark navy details, and proportions exactly consistent with the reference.\nHe is seated with the drum in front of him and holding the drumstick naturally.\n\nUse the provided background as the visual setting:\na clean white media-art composition with Gongsanseong Fortress, a glowing swallow made of gold light and ink-like trails, and the royal tomb of King Muryeong.\n\nThe gosu should be the main subject.\nHis face must remain sharp and stable, not distorted or blurred.\nShow a calm, focused expression and a poised traditional performance mood.\n\nThe drum and upper body should be clearly visible.\nDo not make the drumming action too aggressive.\nNo extra people, no text, no logo.\n\nElegant Korean digital-art atmosphere, high detail, 16:9.\n\n[D] 여자 소리꾼 영상 프롬프트 (아~ 4초 / 커스텀 멀티샷용)\nCUSTOM MULTI-SHOT — 4 seconds total\n\nUse Image 1 as the exact start frame and Image 2 as the exact end frame.\n\nKeep the same female pansori singer throughout:\nidentical face, hairstyle, hanbok, body proportions, and the same white media-art background with Gongsanseong Fortress, the glowing swallow, and the royal tomb.\n\nThe motion must be very restrained and elegant.\nThis is a long sustained pansori note: “아~~~”\nThe voice lasts about 4 seconds.\n\nSHOT 1 — 0:00–0:02\nShe begins sustaining the sound “아~~~” softly and steadily.\nHer mouth opens naturally and remains stable for a long note.\nHer upper body stays mostly still with only subtle breath and a slight emotional lift in the chest and shoulders.\nHer fan hand rises very slightly and gracefully.\nHer eyes and expression remain focused and traditional.\nThe background media-art elements remain visually stable, with only a faint soft shimmer in the golden light and ink-like trails.\n\nSHOT 2 — 0:02–0:04\nContinue the same sustained note without interruption.\nHer expression deepens slightly with restrained pansori emotion.\nThe fan hand extends a little more naturally, and her free hand opens gently.\nNo sudden gestures.\nThe swallow and background do not fly around wildly; they only glow subtly as if responding to the voice.\nEnd exactly on Image 2.\n\nNo abrupt motion, no extra people, no text, no camera shake.\nVery smooth, elegant, restrained performance.\n16:9.\n\n[E] 여자 소리꾼 영상 프롬프트 (이미지1 → 이미지2)\nUse Image 1 as the exact start frame and Image 2 as the exact end frame.\n\nKeep the same female pansori singer throughout:\nidentical face, hairstyle, hanbok, body proportions, and the same white media-art background.\n\nThe singer begins in a calmer neutral singing posture and gradually transitions into the more expressive final pose.\nShe slowly raises the fan and opens her free hand in a graceful, restrained pansori gesture.\nHer lips move naturally as if singing a sustained phrase.\nHer expression becomes slightly more emotional and uplifted.\n\nThe transition must be smooth and continuous, with no sudden jump.\nThe background remains essentially the same, but the golden glow and ink-like lines can softly brighten and breathe as if reacting to her voice.\nThe swallow, fortress, and royal tomb remain part of the stable background composition and should not move aggressively.\n\nSlow cinematic motion, soft dolly-in, elegant traditional performance, 16:9.\nNo abrupt cut, no extra people, no text.\n\n[F] 남자 고수 북치는 영상 프롬프트\nUse Image 1 as the exact start frame and keep the same composition throughout.\n\nKeep the same male gosu:\nidentical face, hat, robe, drum, and background.\nMaintain stable facial detail and consistent proportions.\n\nHe performs a slow, controlled traditional drum action.\nThe drumming must not be fast or aggressive.\nHe gently lifts the drumstick, pauses briefly, and delivers one calm, deliberate beat.\nAfter the strike, the stick settles naturally.\n\nHis expression remains focused and composed.\nHis upper body moves only slightly.\nThe drum should not be hit repeatedly or rapidly.\n\nThe background media-art elements remain visually stable.\nOnly a subtle soft glow may pulse in response to the drumbeat.\nNo sudden flashes, no chaotic movement, no extra people, no text.\n\nSmooth slow cinematic motion, restrained Korean traditional performance, 16:9.",
