      "fullPrompt": "[영상 생성 프롬프트]\n\nPhotoreal high-end Korean cultural heritage motion graphic based on the actual Muryongwang Baekje gold ornament. Maintain a luxurious, elegant, antique and monumental visual tone with deep black space, aged worked gold, narrow amber highlights, fine tool marks, subtle age traces and physically realistic metallic reflections.\n\nThe artifact must remain a flat, tall and narrow perforated gold ornament panel based on the actual Muryongwang gold ornament reference. Do not transform it into a circular crown, head ring, cylindrical crown or fantasy royal crown.\n\nThe entire sequence must feel like one uninterrupted long take. Each generated clip starts exactly from the previous clip's END frame. No hard cut, fade, dissolve, scene reset, camera reset or transition effect. Camera movement, object velocity, lighting direction and sound continuity must carry naturally across every clip.\n\nThe visual progression is:\nsingle gold sheet → precise carving → perforated negative space → fragment separation → fragment movement → reassembly → complete artifact.\n\nDuring carving, the tool follows the existing ornament pattern continuously in one natural cycle. The cutting action must not stop and restart. As the carving continues, shallow incision lines become real open perforations. Small gold sections separate naturally without explosion or excessive sparks.\n\nFragment movement must remain limited and controlled. Use approximately five to seven meaningful fragments maximum. Only two or three fragments may retain recognizable curved portions of the original ornament pattern; the remaining pieces are simple thin cut-metal sections. No fragment swarm, random scattering, duplicated ornamental pieces or paper-like fluttering.\n\nDuring the assembly sequence, the remaining fragments are already moving from left to right through the middle section of the frame from the first moment. Flight and assembly happen simultaneously. Each fragment continues