      "postEditingDetails": "사용했습니다. 생성한 장면 클립을 순서대로 잇고, 작품명·소재·AI 제작 고지 자막 카드를 합성하고, 720p 생성본을 출품 규격 1920×1080으로 변환하는 데 로컬 편집 도구(FFmpeg)를 썼습니다. 장면 내용을 바꾸는 편집이나 프레임 조작은 하지 않았습니다.",
      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "「빛의 방향」 프롬프트 전문\n\n생성 도구: Topview Ultra — Seedance 2.5 (장면 영상) / ChatGPT Images — ChatGPT Pro (캐릭터 기준 이미지)\n아래는 요약이 아니라 실제로 입력한 원문입니다.\n\n■ 장면 영상 프롬프트 (채택)\n\n[장면 A — 오프닝 그림자 대비 · 2026-09-13]\nNight in a fictional royal tomb park viewing area, low walls and a dark walkway. A low guide lamp on a short post casts a huge horned shadow of the stone guardian beast in the attached reference image onto the dark wall. Under the beam the beast's real body is small. The body stays still; only its head turns away from the dazzling light. Camera: start close on the looming shadow, then pull back slowly to a low wide shot showing the small body and the light direction together. Cold night tone, single directional light source, realistic weathered stone texture, faint wind and stone friction ambience. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n[장면 B — 석수가 빛 앞에서 한 발 옆으로 · 2026-09-13]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. The stone guardian beast in the attached reference image steps sideways to stand between the guide lamp and its own spot. Its face enters shadow, but when it moves the beam catches it again; it takes one more small step sideways. Camera: fixed side view keeping the lamp, the beast and the wall in the same arrangement and light direction. Two soft footfalls, brief silence. Cold night tone, realistic weathered stone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n[장면 C — 관람객 발목 정지 · 2026-09-13]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. Reverse angle on the dark walkway entrance: because the small guide lamp points at the stone guardian instead of the path, an adult visitor's two shoes stop at the dark entrance. Only ankles, shoes and trouser hems are visible - no face, no hands, no child. Flat ground, no stairs, no fall. Footsteps stop, a brief cloth rustle. Cold night tone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n[장면 D — 램프 뒤 이동 · 2026-09-13]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. The small stone guardian beast in the attached reference image releases its light-blocking posture and looks in turn at the dark path, the rotating lamp head, and its own spot. Then it walks to behind the lamp fixture. Camera: short wide shot ending with the path and the lamp head in the same frame. Cold night tone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n[장면 E2 — 어깨로 램프 헤드 밀기 (장면 E 교체) · 2026-09-19]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. Fixed side view, camera locked. The small stone guardian beast in the attached reference image presses its shoulder firmly against the side of the low rotating guide lamp's head and pushes - the shoulder stays in clear contact with the metal head the whole time. Under the push the lamp head slowly rotates around its fixed vertical axis, and the beam swings in a smooth arc onto the dark walkway. The contact point on the lamp head, the rotation axis, and the light's destination on the path all stay visible in the same frame. The lamp post is never lifted, tilted or toppled. Stone-on-metal friction sound, a small mechanical catch at the end. Cold night tone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n[장면 F — 관람객 재보행 · 2026-09-15]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. Same camera angle as the earlier walkway-entrance shot: the guide lamp's beam now reaches the path, and the adult visitor's shoes - the same shoes, same walking direction, ankles only - resume walking safely on flat ground. At the bottom of the frame the small stone guardian is no longer lit head-on. Footsteps resume. Cold night tone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n[장면 G — 석수 원위치와 그림자 · 2026-09-15]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. Same wide angle as the opening shot: the small stone guardian beast in the attached reference image returns to its original spot, body facing outward. On the wall beside the lamp - now lighting the walkway - a shadow larger than its small body remains, an ordinary optical shadow. Footsteps stop, wind. Cold night tone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n■ 캐릭터 기준 이미지 프롬프트 (채택 · 2026-09-13 · ChatGPT Images)\n\nThe attached photos show the real stone guardian statue 'seoksu' from King Muryeong's tomb (Korean National Treasure). Create a single 16:9 landscape character reference image of this exact artifact as a stylized cinematic 3D render for an animated film. Keep the artifact's exact shape, proportions, surface texture and features — do not redesign it. Full body, front three-quarter view, centered, clean dark neutral studio background, soft cinematic lighting. No text, no watermark.\n\n■ 캐릭터 기준 이미지 1차 시안 프롬프트 (미채택 · Topview GPT Image 2)\n\nCreate one original full-body character reference of a small ancient Baekje stone guardian animal inspired by factual descriptions of the Stone Guardian from King Muryeong's Tomb. Show a clear front three-quarter view on a plain warm-neutral background, entire body and all four short legs visible. Preserve a blunt muzzle, large nose without nostrils, small carved eyes and ears, one branch-shaped iron horn on the head, carved flame motifs on the sides and legs, and a tail. Proportions: height 30.8 cm, length 49 cm, width 22 cm. Heavy weathered grey stone with subtle traces of red on the lips. Do not turn it into a lion, a haetae, a dog, a human-faced mascot, or a generic fantasy creature. No glowing eyes, no extra limbs or horns, no text, no watermark, no dramatic darkness. Soft even studio light makes every carved detail readable. This is a fictional production reference based on factual text, not a reproduction or transformation of any photograph.\n\n■ 미사용 프롬프트 (최종 영상에 쓰지 않음. 전체 이력 기록용)\n\n[장면 E — 어깨로 램프 헤드 밀기 · 2026-09-15 · 미사용]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. Fixed side view: the small stone guardian beast in the attached reference image slowly pushes the side of the low rotating guide lamp's head with its shoulder. The head rotates around its existing vertical axis and the beam swings onto the dark walkway. The contact point on the lamp head, the rotation axis, and the light's destination on the path are all visible in the same frame. The lamp post is never lifted, tilted or toppled. Stone-on-metal friction sound, a small mechanical catch at the end. Cold night tone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.\n\n[장면 D2 — 램프 뒤 이동 · 2026-09-19 · 미사용]\nNight, fictional royal tomb park viewing area. The small stone guardian beast in the attached reference image releases its light-blocking posture and looks in turn at the dark path, at the low cylindrical metal guide lamp on a short post beside it — a short cylinder head that can rotate around a fixed vertical axis — and at its own spot. Then it walks to behind that same cylindrical guide lamp. Camera: short wide shot ending with the path and the lamp head in the same frame. Cold night tone. No dialogue, no on-screen text.",
