      "fullPrompt": "최종 프롬포트:\n\nCUT 01 \nA quiet and dark exhibition hall inside the National Gongju Museum, displaying an ancient Baekje bronze mirror in a glass case.\n\nThe bronze mirror is clearly visible in the foreground and becomes the visual center of the composition. A visitor's point of view, wide cinematic shot, looking toward the display.\nThe present-day museum atmosphere is calm, dark, cool-neutral and slightly mysterious, with very soft exhibition lighting. The bronze mirror remains completely still and ordinary, with no supernatural effects yet.\nPhotorealistic cinematic historical documentary style, realistic museum architecture, subtle reflections on the glass, deep shadows, restrained contrast, quiet atmosphere, realistic materials and textures, cinematic composition, shallow atmospheric depth.\nNo glowing mirror, no magic, no fantasy effects, no dramatic movement, no ancient people, no historical reconstruction yet.\n--ar 16:9 --style raw\n\nCUT 02\n\nExtreme close-up of the same Baekje bronze mirror from the previous scene.\nPreserve the exact engraved patterns, shape, material, color and identity of the bronze mirror.\nA very faint golden-blue light begins to flow slowly along the engraved patterns of the mirror. Tiny dust particles around the mirror subtly react to the light.\n\nThe effect is extremely subtle and mysterious, as if the ancient object is quietly awakening after centuries of silence.Keep the museum environment dark and cool-neutral in the surrounding areas, while the faint light creates a restrained warm reflection on the bronze surface.Photorealistic bronze texture, detailed ancient engravings, cinematic macro photography, shallow depth of field, subtle atmospheric haze, realistic light interaction.\nNo people, no fantasy symbols, no excessive glowing, no explosion of light, no modern objects.\n--ar 16:9 --style raw\n\nCUT 03\n\nFront-facing cinematic close-up of the same Baekje bronze mirror.\nKeep the present-day museum clearly visible around the mirror, dark and cool-neutral.\nInside the reflective surface of the bronze mirror, a completely different world begins to appear: a warm Baekje environment with subtle silhouettes of ancient people and traditional architecture.\nThe museum remains outside the mirror, while the Baekje past exists only inside the reflection.\nCreate a clear visual contrast between the cool dark present outside the mirror and the warm golden historical world inside it.The transition should feel mysterious and emotional rather than magical or fantastical.\nPhotorealistic bronze reflection, realistic engraved patterns, warm golden sunlight inside the reflection, atmospheric haze, subtle dust particles, cinematic historical reconstruction, shallow depth of field.\nNo modern objects inside the reflection, no fantasy palace, no exaggerated supernatural effects.\n\n--ar 16:9 --style raw\n\nCUT 04\n\nBegin with the same dark museum environment and the same Baekje bronze mirror.\nThe golden light inside the bronze mirror suddenly becomes stronger and expands outward.\nThe museum environment gradually dissolves into fine particles of light, while the warm Baekje environment emerges through the expanding golden light.The transition moves from the cool dark present into a warm golden historical world.\nThe camera slowly pushes forward toward the mirror in a smooth cinematic movement, as if passing through the surface of the mirror and entering the past.End inside the warm Baekje environment.\nMaintain the same bronze mirror identity, engraved patterns, lighting logic and cinematic visual language established in the previous scenes.Smooth cinematic movement only. No camera shake, no jitter, no handheld movement, no sudden zoom, no rapid dolly, no pan, no tilt, no rotation.\nPhotorealistic historical reconstruction, warm golden sunlight, earthy brown tones, amber highlights, soft atmospheric haze, floating dust particles, realistic materials.\nNo modern objects, no fantasy portal, no futuristic effects, no exaggerated magical explosion.\n\nCUT 05\n\nContinue directly from the previous scene inside a warm Baekje historical environment.\nThe camera slowly reveals a space filled with authentic Baekje artifacts and everyday objects.\nA subtle golden light originating from the bronze mirror travels naturally across the scene and gently touches the objects.\nAs the light reaches each artifact, the objects respond with extremely subtle movements: a slight vibration, a small rotation, or a soft reflection of golden light.\nThe artifacts should feel as if they are awakening from memories that have been preserved for centuries.\nThe effect must remain restrained and realistic. The objects should not float dramatically or move unnaturally.\nMaintain warm natural sunlight, earthy architecture, deep brown shadows, amber highlights, subtle dust particles and atmospheric haze.Photorealistic historical reconstruction, cinematic historical drama, realistic Baekje artifacts and materials.\nThe camera moves extremely slowly and smoothly.\nNo camera shake, no jitter, no handheld movement, no rapid zoom, no sudden dolly, no pan, no tilt, no rotation. No modern objects, no fantasy armor, no exaggerated magical effects, no floating artifacts.\n\nCUT 06 \n\nA high-status Baekje royal woman using the same engraved bronze mirror in the past.\nA young East Asian royal woman wearing historically inspired Baekje clothing in rich warm red and earthy tones, with elegant gold hair ornaments and a refined traditional crown.\nShe carefully holds and studies the same ancient bronze mirror in her hands.\nAttendants stand beside her and gently adjust her crown and hair ornaments.\nThe bronze mirror must clearly maintain the same shape, engraved patterns and visual identity established in the previous scenes.\nWarm natural sunlight enters the room, creating soft golden rim light around the woman and attendants.\nDeep warm brown shadows, amber highlights, realistic warm skin tones, subtle dust particles, atmospheric haze, cinematic shallow depth of field.\nThe scene should feel intimate and historically grounded, as if witnessing an ordinary moment from the life of a high-status Baekje woman.\nPhotorealistic cinematic historical reconstruction, realistic Baekje clothing and architecture, cinematic historical drama.\nNo modern objects, no fantasy costume, no Chinese imperial palace aesthetic, no exaggerated jewelry, no artificial magical effects.\n\n--ar 16:9 --style raw\n\nCUT 07\n\nContinue directly from the provided starting image of an ordinary Baekje household.\nWoman A is naturally preparing food using traditional Baekje pottery.\nAs she finishes her action, the camera gently shifts attention within the same household space, revealing Woman B who is already naturally present.\nWoman B transfers water from a large earthenware storage jar into a smaller ceramic vessel.\nBoth women must remain clearly separate and must not morph into each other.\nThe transition should feel like a natural continuation of everyday life rather than a staged montage.\nThe same warm golden sunlight enters the room, creating soft golden rim light, deep warm brown shadows and amber highlights.\nTraditional pottery, baskets and wooden household objects are naturally placed throughout the space.\nSubtle dust particles float in the sunlight.\nThe camera moves extremely slowly and smoothly with a gentle lateral shift and slight pull-back.\nNo handheld movement, no camera shake, no jitter, no rapid zoom, no sudden dolly, no pan, no tilt, no rotation.\nRealistic water movement and pottery interaction.\nPhotorealistic cinematic historical reconstruction, warm earthy Baekje atmosphere, realistic ordinary clothing and architecture.\nNo palace, no royalty, no crowns, no elaborate jewelry, no fantasy, no modern objects, no Chinese imperial aesthetic.\nCUT 08 \nContinue directly from the previous scene, beginning with Woman B transferring water from the large earthenwa