      "fullPrompt": "## 1. C01 — 무령왕릉·진묘수 원본\n\nA restrained handcrafted sculptural animated film, 16:9. Dark plum negative space, dusty-pink lotus petals, muted engraved bronze and thin gold leaf, soft warm key light from upper-left, fixed exposure and white balance. Use the supplied character and artifact designs without redesign. Stylized virtual materials, not live-action museum photography. One continuous physically motivated camera move; no internal cuts, camera teleportation, digital zoom or orbit across the movement axis. Architecture remains rigid. No dialogue, narration, generated lettering, captions or logos. Generate synchronized quiet foley only, no music; one continuous score will be added later. Moving subjects must maintain velocity across the beginning and end; no freeze-to-reference pose. Do not introduce automatic speed ramps. Slow viewing comes from deliberate staging; optional time ramps are applied to the entire image in editing. Supplied stills define identity, not camera teleport destinations.\n\nIDENTITY / SPACE\nARCHITECTURE: compact barrel-vaulted burial chamber, central front entrance passage. Camera backs from chamber into lower passage. Guardian sleeps farther along RIGHT side of passage, initially occluded by doorway jamb, never on initially visible empty chamber floor. Preserve connected floor and distant chamber niche behind-left. No invented side chamber, palace, altar or secret room. Passage images are stylized blocking references, not a measured archaeological reconstruction.\nGUARDIAN IDENTITY: SLEEP/WAKE/B02 are one fictional character, broad rounded feline muzzle, round ears, single engraved bronze horn, same pink neck ruff, compact powerful torso, four thick paws, small shoulder wing, long tail. No replacement with realistic excavated stone beast. Choose one production scale fitting the small passage (proposed body shoulder height0.65m) and keep it through all shots; never enlarge character to fill screen. Only stone-to-fur material changes during awakening.\n\nONE CONTINUOUS TAKE\n0-4s empty brick burial chamber, rear niche facing camera; dolly backward toward central doorway following three petals. 4-6s pass threshold into lower passage, near RIGHT jamb covers foreground. 6-9s small lateral drift uncovers horn and paw then sleeping guardian on right passage floor, through parallax while the same jamb remains solid and visible. 9-12s in this SAME unbroken space, petals touch guardian and stone texture becomes dusty-pink fur, eyes open and chest breathes. 12-14s stand and follow camera toward the same central exit. 14-16s both clear the outer threshold; only now camera eases into side tracking. 16-19s guardian runs RIGHT at stable speed for at least two strides. No cut at first reveal or awakening. ARCHITECTURAL PERSISTENCE — CRITICAL: This entire 20-second shot is ONE continuous physical space, not a sequence of reconstructed rooms. Fix four world-space anchors: A rear niche, B central doorway, C the near right doorway jamb/pier, D continuous floor and threshold. The RIGHT JAMB is a solid architectural occluder and must keep its width, material, brick pattern, position and depth while the camera passes it. Reveal the guardian ONLY by lateral parallax around this occluder. Never delete, fade, dissolve, shrink, narrow, replace or move the jamb to reveal the animal. Once visible, the guardian has always occupied the same right-side passage floor. Keep the jamb visible in foreground during the partial reveal, then let it leave the frame only by continuous camera movement and perspective. It must not vanish between adjacent frames, even when the creature awakens. Preserve occlusion ordering: near jamb in front, guardian farther along passage, chamber niche through the doorway behind. Camera exits through the real central passage, not through a wall. No invisible cut, pillar disappearance, room morph, architecture rebuild, sudden lens change or background reset. SLEEP and WAKE images are CHARACTER/MATERIAL references; if their framing conflicts with this spatial continuity, preserve the established architecture and camera instead of matching their composition.\nTAIL HANDLE\nAt 19 seconds continue the same right-running stride and camera for one extra second. Total generated duration 20 seconds. No freeze at the end.\nIDENTITY\nUse exactly the same face, single bronze horn, ears, small shoulder wings, thick paws and tail in stone and pink-fur states. Only material changes.\nCONTINUITY\nPreserve fixed lens, exposure, body scale, floor and world-space architectural anchors. No subtitles or labels.\n```\n\n## 2. E8 — 진묘수 등장 교체\n\n```text\nOne continuous 10-second animated shot connecting the supplied starting and ending frames. SAME Baekje brick tomb, same one-horn pink guardian in the end frame. Change the middle camera trajectory to an OPEN unobstructed aisle. No pillar in the center of the image at any time. No pillar passes in front of the creature. Brick supports stay at extreme frame edges.\n\nThe camera begins on the empty tomb, then smoothly pulls backward into the adjoining open chamber. By 1.5 seconds the SAME sleeping guardian is naturally entering from the RIGHT edge of frame as the camera pulls back, already on the floor, initially gray stone. From 2 seconds onward the guardian's FULL head and body are visible continuously with NOTHING between camera and animal. The camera looks directly through the open aisle rather than sliding behind any pier. It gently arcs to frame the guardian on the right and settles. A few pink petals flutter on a breeze from the rear tomb toward the guardian, tipping and tumbling independently. At 5 seconds one petal grazes its shoulder; pink energy travels gently over its visible skin, changing stone to the same soft pink fur. At 8-10 seconds it slowly raises its head and sits in the exact END-frame pose and composition. End precisely on the provided final image. No cuts, no disappearance, no suddenly generated animal, no column wipes, no brightness flash hiding the animal. Architecture stays solid. Silent, no text.\n```\n\n## 3. E2 — 진묘수 달리기 연결 수정\n\n```text\nEdit the supplied 5-second video to repair its visible cut at second 2 into one continuous rightward tracking shot. It shows the same single pink-furred one-horn Baekje guardian running left to right. Preserve exactly its face, horn, proportions, fur color, direction and scale. Replace the motion discontinuity around seconds 1-3 with a continuous physically coherent four-legged galloping stride: the same footfall cycle continues, no reset, frozen paw, duplicate legs, teleport, abrupt speed change or camera jump. The tracking camera matches the same rightward speed; floor horizon, warm lighting and background parallax flow continuously. Match the opening and final three-quarter-second closely to the supplied video for seamless splicing. Preserve the existing progressive pink lotus-petal dissolution at the very end, carried forward by the running momentum. Do not introduce the mirror early or redesign the creature. No cutaway, no crossfade, no occluding flash, no additional text, no music.\n```\n\n## 4. C02 — 청동거울·신수 도약 원본\n\n```text\nA restrained handcrafted sculptural animated film, 16:9. Dark plum negative space, dusty-pink lotus petals, muted engraved bronze and thin gold leaf, soft warm key light from upper-left, fixed exposure and white balance. Use the supplied character and artifact designs without redesign. Stylized virtual materials, not live-action museum photography. One continuous physically motivated camera move; no internal cuts, camera teleportation, digital zoom or orbit across the movement axis. Architecture remains rigid. No dialogue, narration, generated lettering, captions or logos. Generate synchronized quiet foley only, no music; one continuous score will be added later. Moving subjects must maintain velocity across the beginning and end; no freeze-to-reference pose. Do not introduce automatic speed ra