 No dialogue, narration, generated lettering, captions or logos. Generate synchronized quiet foley only, no music; one continuous score will be added later. Moving subjects must maintain velocity across the beginning and end; no freeze-to-reference pose. Do not introduce automatic speed ramps. Slow viewing comes from deliberate staging; optional time ramps are applied to the entire image in editing. Supplied stills define identity, not camera teleport destinations.\n\nIDENTITY / SPACE\nSame modest fortress wall, gently ascending path and single-storey gate. Continuous screen-left to screen-right uphill movement. Gate already visible ahead. Camera stays outside the same wall, never swings behind or crosses the axis. Creature dissolves WHILE running uphill; petals take over along the same tangent. No palace, hairpin, turn-back or sudden new gate.\nLOTUS FAMILY: exact EAVE/LOTUS flower at the same tile seam. Base and stem stay attached, roof remains rigid. Open outer petals then inner petals. Only after complete bloom, TWO outer petals detach one after the other and form the TWO thin CROWN plates. Keep the remaining flower on roof. No single petal duplicating into a pair, no oval wipe.\n\nONE CONTINUOUS TAKE\n0-4s continue the same bronze creature running RIGHT and gently UP on one continuous inclined fortress path; modest gate already lies ahead upper-right. Camera tracks along the outside of the same wall. No U-turn, hairpin, camera axis crossing or orbit behind the animal. 4-6s dissolve tail then body into petals WHILE running uphill; petals inherit its right-and-up tangent. 6-9s only petals remain; follow them up the OUTSIDE of the same gate column, then around its outer eave corner, never through wood or roof. 9-12s settle beside a small lotus bud attached to the same tile seam, show outer petals then inner petals opening. 12-14s admire the full attached bloom. No giant flower or roof morph.\n\nTAIL HANDLE\nAt 14 seconds the described handoff is achieved. Continue