      "fullPrompt": "01.구름에서 전체동상이 신선으로 변하며 등장 하여 연주\nUse the first image as the exact starting frame and the second image as the exact ending frame. Keep the camera completely locked and preserve the exact five musicians, their left-to-right positions, instruments, mountain skyline, pine branch, and 16:9 composition.\nAt the very beginning, the five seated musicians are motionless gilt-bronze statues, partly concealed by luminous ivory-gold mountain mist. From the first musical beat, the mist flows smoothly outward to both sides and thins. At exactly the same time, warm golden energy passes naturally across all five figures: the rigid bronze surfaces soften into living skin, hair, and historically inspired Baekje-style robes while every instrument remains in the same position. The transformation is continuous, elegant, and simultaneous across the ensemble, with no cuts and no explosion. By the third second, all five are fully human and already performing together. Continue their restrained synchronized ensemble performance until the end, matching the ending frame exactly. Subtle fabric movement, natural hand motion, cinematic amber light, premium historical fantasy realism.\nNo camera movement, no zoom, no new people, no missing musician, no instrument changes, no face distortion, no extra limbs, no opaque smoke, no fire, no text, no logo, no scene change. \n01_01신선들의 연주\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. All five seated musicians perform subtle restrained movements on their existing instruments. Preserve their exact left-to-right order, seating and scale. Instruments remain stable and attached to their hands. Mist flows below the connected rock ledges. Slow gentle camera push-in. No character transformations.\n02.완함연주\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. The seated musician gently plucks the existing round lute, with small controlled finger motions and a slight breath. His other hand stays on the neck. The lute stays rigid and supported in his lap. Very slow push-in toward the hands.\n03.종적연주\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. The musician plays the existing vertical end-blown flute. Keep its mouth contact, vertical orientation and length unchanged. Tiny coordinated finger motions, subtle breathing, gently moving sleeve edges. Slow push-in, no sideways flute rotation.\n04.배소연주\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. The musician plays the existing panpipes with very small natural head and hand movements. Preserve the exact number, order and lengths of the visible pipes. Both hands support the instrument. Soft breathing and gentle fabric movement. Nearly locked camera.\n05.거문고연주\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. The seated musician makes restrained playing gestures on the existing board zither, preserving the reference hand positions and instrument supports. Small finger and wrist motions only. Keep the board rigid, horizontal and unchanged. Gentle sleeve movement, slow push-in toward the instrument.\n06.북연주\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. The drummer performs one clear measured strike using the existing raised short beater, then a gentle rebound. The other hand stabilizes the round drum. Keep the drum fixed in his lap. Natural wrist motion, tiny robe movement, locked camera. No duplicated sticks.\n07.산수공간\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. Very slow cinematic pullback revealing more atmosphere around the existing mountain landscape. Keep the small seated musician anchored on the lower-left rock. Thin clouds drift between distant mountains. Stable rock geometry, restrained movement, no new buildings or characters.\n08.다섯악사합주\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. All five seated musicians perform subtle restrained movements on their existing instruments. Preserve their exact left-to-right order, seating and scale. Instruments remain stable and attached to their hands. Mist flows below the connected rock ledges. Slow gentle camera push-in. No character transformations.\n09.봉황절정\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. The existing phoenix remains standing firmly on the summit and slowly opens its wings slightly wider, then settles. Elegant small feather movements in the wind, a soft warm rim light and drifting mist. Camera gently rises a little. Preserve its anatomy. No takeoff, no flight, no extra birds, no flame explosion.\n10_완함귀환\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. Locked camera. Begin with the living musician in the start reference. The playing movement gradually stops. Thin incense smoke curls inward around the hands, instrument, sleeves and face. Within that soft smoke veil, the visible surfaces gradually become aged gilt bronze, matching the end reference. The person stays seated in exactly the same pose and position. Preserve the instrument silhouette throughout. Finish with a motionless bronze figure, a small residual wisp of smoke drifting upward. No melting, shattering, skeletal imagery or movement toward the camera.\n11_종적귀환\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. Locked camera. Begin with the living musician in the start reference. The playing movement gradually stops. Thin incense smoke curls inward around the hands, instrument, sleeves and face. Within that soft smoke veil, the visible surfaces gradually become aged gilt bronze, matching the end reference. The person stays seated in exactly the same pose and position. Preserve the instrument silhouette throughout. Finish with a motionless bronze figure, a small residual wisp of smoke drifting upward. No melting, shattering, skeletal imagery or movement toward the camera.\n12_배소귀환\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. Locked camera. Begin with the living musician in the start reference. The playing movement gradually stops. Thin incense smoke curls inward around the hands, instrument, sleeves and face. Within that soft smoke veil, the visible surfaces gradually become aged gilt bronze, matching the end reference. The person stays seated in exactly the same pose and position. Preserve the instrument silhouette throughout. Finish with a motionless bronze figure, a small residual wisp of smoke drifting upward. No melting, shattering, skeletal imagery or movement toward the camera.\n13_거문고귀환\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. Locked camera. Begin with the living musician in the start reference. The playing movement gradually stops. Thin incense smoke curls inward around the hands, instrument, sleeves and face. Within that soft smoke veil, the visible surfaces gradually become aged gilt bronze, matching the end reference. The person stays seated in exactly the same pose and position. Preserve the instrument silhouette throughout. Finish with a motionless bronze figure, a small residual wisp of smoke drifting upward. No melting, shattering, skeletal imagery or movement toward the camera.\n14_북귀환\nCinematic 16:9. Preserve the reference composition, character identity, clothing, instrument geometry and warm gold / deep blue palette. Natural subtle movement. No extra people, extra limbs, floating instruments, text, logos, star-shaped sparkles or sudden cuts. Keep the camera steady or move only as specified. Locked camera. Begin with the living musician in the start reference. The playing movement gradually stops. Thin incense smoke curls inward around the hands, instrument, sleeves and face. Within that soft smoke veil, the visible surfaces gradually become aged gilt bronze, matching the end reference. The person stays seated in exactly the same pose and position. Preserve the instrument silhouette throughout. Finish with a motionless bronze figure, a small residual wisp of smoke drifting upward. No melting, shattering, skeletal imagery or movement toward the camera.\n15.금동악사 구름 가리기\nLocked camera. The bronze drummer remains completely motionless. Dense ivory incense smoke rises from the lower foreground and curls across the lens, gradually hiding the statue and mountains. End with the entire frame covered by smoke, matching the ending image. Warm gold light from the left, cool blue shadows on the right. The statue does not dissolve or move; only smoke conceals it. No fire, sparks or new objects.\n16.구름 걷히며 전체모습 등장\nBegin with the frame completely covered by incense smoke. The smoke slowly thins and drifts outward, revealing the five bronze musicians already seated exactly as shown in the ending image. All statues remain motionless. Reveal the existing scene without morphing or assembling the figures. Match the ending composition and lighting. No extra people, instruments, text or sparks.\n17.전체 동상이 유물과 이어짐\nBegin fully covered by the incense smoke in the starting reference. The smoke slowly thins and drifts aside, revealing the complete incense burner exactly as shown in the ending reference. The burner is already present behind the smoke; it does not form or transform from smoke. Preserve its shape and details. End with a clear, steady view of the full burner and a thin rising wisp of incense. No extra ornaments, text or camera rotation.",
