      "fullPrompt": "1. 영상 생성 — 진묘수 → 금제관식\n사용 도구: Seedance 2.5\n진묘수의 눈이 어둠 속에서 천천히 떠오르고, 눈동자에서 은은한 황금빛이 시작된다. 황금빛은 작은 입자들로 분해되어 주변으로 퍼지고, 다시 하나의 흐름으로 모이며 금제관식을 향해 이동한다.\n고대 백제 왕실의 신비롭고 장엄한 분위기. 어두운 공간 속에서 유물의 형태와 재질은 사실적으로 표현한다. 황금빛 입자는 과도한 판타지 효과가 아닌 섬세하고 자연스러운 빛과 먼지처럼 표현한다.\n카메라는 매우 부드럽게 움직이며 하나의 연속된 장면처럼 연결한다. 갑작스러운 컷, 화면 전환, 카메라 흔들림, 과도한 줌을 사용하지 않는다.\n16:9 landscape, 1920x1080 or higher.\nSFX only. No dialogue, no narration, no vocals, no background music.\n2. 영상 생성 — 금제관식 → 지석\nStart from the exact final frame of the previous gold crown ornament scene. The golden light separates from the ornament and begins traveling horizontally to the right. The camera smoothly follows the moving light while the crown ornament gradually moves toward the left side of the frame.\nAs the camera continues moving right, a weathered greenish stone stele gradually becomes visible from the darkness. The stele already exists in the scene and is revealed by the movement of the light; it must not appear through a magical materialization effect.\nWhen the golden light reaches the stele, the inscription areas softly illuminate with warm golden light. The actual characters must remain completely blurred and unreadable. Do not generate readable Chinese characters or invented inscriptions.\nThe light gathers toward the central circular hole of the stele. It concentrates inside the hole, passes through it, and transforms into a narrow, focused golden-white beam traveling toward the right side of the frame.\nThe beam must continue moving right at the end of the shot so that it naturally connects to the next gilt-bronze shoe scene.\nOne continuous smooth lateral camera movement. No hard cuts, no dissolve, no camera shake, no sudden zoom, no rotation.\n16:9 landscape, 1920x1080 or higher, exactly 7 seconds.\nSFX only. Ancient chamber ambience, subtle stone resonance and a soft focused energy whoosh. No background music, no vocals, no narration, no dialogue.\n3. 영상 생성 — 지석 → 금동신발\nBegin with the incoming concentrated golden-white beam from the previous stele scene.\nUse the provided corroded gilt-bronze shoe reference as the visual reference for the initial artifact.\nThe focused beam enters from the left and strikes the corroded gilt-bronze shoes. At the moment of impact, a powerful white-golden burst of light briefly fills the shoes.\nThe shoes are gradually revealed as a restored digital reconstruction of the original gilt-bronze shoes. Preserve the historical form and structure of Baekje gilt-bronze shoes. The material should clearly feel like gilt-bronze, with dark bronze surfaces and naturally aged golden plating, not solid pure gold.\nAfter the reconstruction is completed, the shoes remain illuminated on a ceremonial pedestal in the dark chamber. The golden energy gathers again and exits toward the right side of the frame, preparing the transition to the next artifacts.\nCinematic, realistic historical atmosphere. No futuristic holograms, no modern objects.\nOne continuous smooth camera movement. No hard cut, no camera shake, no excessive zoom.\n16:9 landscape, 1920x1080 or higher, exactly 7 seconds.\nSFX only. Soft impact, metallic resonance, subtle energy movement. No background music, no vocals, no narration, no dialogue.\n4. 영상 생성 — 금귀걸이 + 금목걸이\nFirst frame: a dark ceremonial chamber containing a single concentrated golden light mass.\nThe golden light suddenly divides from one central point into two streams of glowing particles, moving naturally like fireflies.\nThe two streams travel separately and illuminate two different artifacts: gold earrings above and a gold necklace below.\nAs the particles reach each artifact, the artifacts gradually become visible and illuminated. Preserve their historical form, delicate details and realistic gold material.\nThe light must not behave like a continuous glowing ribbon. It should behave as individual golden particles originating from one concentrated point and splitting into two separate flows.\nBy the end of the scene, both the earrings and necklace are clearly visible and glowing warmly in the dark chamber. Their light gently illuminates the surrounding environment.\nThe two artifact light sources remain separate until the final moment, preparing for the next scene where their energy converges.\nCinematic historical atmosphere, realistic artifact textures, subtle golden particles.\nNo futuristic holograms, no neon, no modern objects.\nOne continuous smooth camera movement. No hard cuts, no camera shake, no abrupt zoom.\n16:9 landscape, 1920x1080 or higher, exactly 7 seconds.\nSFX only. Subtle particle sounds, delicate metallic resonance and soft energy movement. No background music, no vocals, no narration, no dialogue.\n5. 영상 생성 — 금귀걸이·금목걸이 → 청동거울\nStart from the exact final frame showing the glowing gold earrings and gold necklace.\nThe golden particles surrounding both artifacts begin moving toward a single central point. The two separate streams of energy converge and become increasingly concentrated.\nThe gathered energy does not remain as a floating orb. It compresses into a narrow, sharp, arrow-like golden projectile.\nThe concentrated golden projectile is suddenly launched forward toward the bronze mirror.\nThe beam travels with strong direction and momentum, like a golden arrow of energy, while remaining elegant and cinematic rather than violent.\nThe projectile strikes the back surface of an ancient weathered bronze mirror.\nAt impact, the mirror vibrates subtly and the golden energy spreads across its surface.\nThe bronze mirror then slowly flips from its back side to its front side.\nAs the mirror turns, its front surface becomes brightly illuminated and reveals a golden reflection of King Muryeong’s Tomb landscape: green burial mounds, blue sky, white clouds and the tomb entrance.\nThe final frame should clearly show the front of the bronze mirror with the King Muryeong’s Tomb landscape reflected inside it.\nOne continuous cinematic movement. No hard cut, no white-out transition, no teleportation, no camera shake.\n16:9 landscape, 1920x1080 or higher, exactly 7 seconds.\nSFX only. Energy convergence, sharp projectile whoosh, bronze impact resonance, metallic mirror movement and a soft atmospheric resonance.\nNo background music, no vocals, no narration, no dialogue.\n6. Suno — 38초 전체 음악\n38-second cinematic instrumental music inspired by the ancient music of Baekje Korea.\nAncient Korean royal court atmosphere, mysterious and sacred. Use traditional Korean and ancient East Asian-inspired instruments as the main musical identity.\nPrimary instruments: daegeum-like bamboo flute, piri-like double-reed wind instrument, ajaeng-like bowed string, gayageum-like plucked strings, subtle janggu and buk percussion, ancient bronze bells and metallic resonances.\nBegin extremely quiet and mysterious, with a single breathy bamboo flute phrase and sparse plucked-string notes, as if entering an ancient Baekje royal tomb.\nGradually increase the emotional intensity as the golden light connects the artifacts.\nBuild toward a short ceremonial climax when the golden energy strikes the bronze mirror.\nImmediately release the tension at the final moment, returning to a soft bamboo flute tone and faint bronze resonance as the bronze mirror reveals King Muryeong's Tomb.\nNO vocals. NO lyrics. NO narration. NO modern pop. NO EDM. NO electronic synth melody. NO Hollywood orchestral soundtrack. NO heroic fantasy melody. NO excessive percussion. NO modern drum kit.\nAncient, restrained, ceremonial, mysterious, emotional and immersive.",
