      "fullPrompt": "영상 프롬프트 (연대귀문전)\n\nREFERENCE LOCK\n<<<image_1>>> = the start frame. It defines the look of every element: the guardian's face, hands, claws, crimson circuit lines and red silk ribbons, the evil smoke, the alley, the lanterns and the color grade. The video begins exactly from <<<image_1>>>, with the lanterns initially lit. The images define appearance; this text defines motion, material behavior and the timed change in lantern lighting. Preserve 1:1 the guardian's face, silhouette and hand shape throughout.\n\nMATERIAL PHYSICS (applies for the whole shot)\n- The guardian's body is not solid. It is a large volume of black ink smoke with no hard surface, no skin and no rubbery texture. Only its face, claws and ring belt are defined by the crimson lines; everything else is billowing smoke.\n- When the guardian moves, its smoke body lags behind the motion and streams backward in trails, like smoke dragged through air. Its edges constantly dissolve and reform.\n- Its arm is a column of smoke that stretches forward, not a solid limb; smoke pours off the arm as it reaches, and only the claws at its end are defined.\n- The existing red silk ribbons are thin, lightweight silk. They ripple in soft waves, lag behind every movement, twist and billow in the wind, never stiff, never flat like plastic.\n- The evil smoke is thick, heavy, restless smoke that constantly boils, surges and writhes; it is never still for a single frame.\n\nTONE\nRestrained and elegant, like a high-end fashion film or a prestige feature, never like a superhero film, an anime, a game or a monster movie. The lunge and the grab are fast and decisive; the smoke and silk move with natural physical softness.\n\nTEMPO\nMusic at 118 BPM, one beat = 0.51s. The grab lands exactly on the 4th beat at 1.53s.\n\nFORCE DIRECTION\nThe evil smoke surges down the alley toward the camera. The guardian lunges forward behind it, toward the camera. The grab happens just in front of the lens. The rest of the evil smoke scatters outward to the sides and back down the alley.\n\nLANTERN LIGHTING\nAt the first frame, the lanterns are lit exactly as in <<<image_1>>>.\nDuring 0.0–0.3s, as the evil smoke surges forward, every lantern rapidly goes out. Their warm spill on the walls, timber and smoke, and their warm reflections on the wet flagstones, disappear with them. The lantern fixtures remain in place, their paper panels dark.\nFrom 0.3s until the captured smoke has dissolved, all lanterns remain completely unlit.\nPreserve the existing cool moonlight and the guardian's glowing crimson circuit lines throughout. Do not darken the whole image through an exposure change.\nOnly after the captured smoke has vanished in the final interval do the lanterns gently relight with a subdued 2700K glow, restoring their local warm spill and reflections.\n\nRULES\nOne continuous shot, no cuts. The guardian's hands and claws keep exactly the shape they have in <<<image_1>>>, and its face stays exactly as in <<<image_1>>> as it grows larger in frame. The crimson circuit lines keep glowing as in <<<image_1>>>. No light ever comes out of its hands or claws, and no light passes into the smoke. The evil smoke never glows. The camera stays nearly locked. Total 5.0s = 1.4s + 0.3s + 1.3s + 2.0s.\n\n0.0–1.4s | LUNGE\nEVIL SMOKE: from the first frame, the whole mass surges forward along the flagstones toward the camera, boiling and rolling over itself, its tendrils whipping ahead of it.\nGUARDIAN: lunges forward behind it, its smoke body streaming backward in long trails, its face rushing closer, its smoke arm stretching out ahead of it.\nLIGHT: all lanterns rapidly extinguish within the first 0.3 seconds and remain dark. Their warm spill and reflections vanish with them.\nCAMERA: locked low on the flagstones.\n\n1.4–1.7s | GRAB (1.53s)\nGUARDIAN: at 1.53s its claws clamp around the front of the smoke mass just before the lens, fast and decisive. Its trailing smoke body keeps flowing forward for a moment after the arm stops, then settles.\nEVIL SMOKE: the seized part convulses violently; smoke squeezes out between the claws in wisps.\nCAMERA: one firm bump, pushed slightly backward.\n\n1.7–3.0s | CRUSH\nGUARDIAN: its face fills most of the frame, glaring into the lens; its smoke body churns around it; the red silk ribbons whip past in soft waves.\nEVIL SMOKE: the seized part thrashes, twists and tears thin in its grip. The rest of the mass recoils and breaks apart, rushing away to both sides and back down the alley.\nCAMERA: holds on the face.\n\n3.0–5.0s | AFTERMATH\nEVIL SMOKE: the seized smoke unravels into long thin wisps, like ink dispersing in water, and fades. The retreating smoke thins out down the alley.\nLIGHT: after the captured smoke has fully vanished, the extinguished lanterns gently relight at 2700K. Their warm illumination returns locally to the walls and wet stones, without a flash or an overall exposure change.\nGUARDIAN: keeps glaring into the lens, its smoke body still churning, its mane rippling, its red silk ribbons rippling and settling.\nCAMERA: holds, with a slight recovery drift.\n\nLENS / LIGHT\nARRI Alexa 35, 35mm at T2, 24fps with natural motion blur. Preserve the reference color grade, cool moonlight and crimson circuit illumination. Only the lantern emission and its associated warm spill and reflections change according to the lighting timeline above.\n\nSOUND\nA low sub-bass drone, the roar of rushing smoke, a heavy rush of air as the guardian lunges, a single deep hard thud at 1.53s, a rushing exhale as the smoke dissolves.\n\nNEGATIVES\nNo lanterns remaining lit after 0.3s, no residual warm lantern glow or warm reflections while the lanterns are off, no premature relighting before the captured smoke disappears, no global exposure fade, no blackout of the moonlight or crimson circuits.\nNo solid body, no rubber, no plastic, no smooth skin, no solid black limbs, no mannequin body, no stiff ribbon, no plastic ribbon, no static evil smoke, no evil smoke waiting still, no frozen smoke, no sudden disappearance of the smoke, no change to the guardian's face, no slow motion, no light coming from the hands or claws, no energy blasts, no glowing cracks, no shockwave, no flash, no superhero effects, no roaring monster voice, no freeze frame, no speed ramps, no anime-style impact, no game-style effects, no change to the guardian's hands or claws, no fingers, no human hands, no sparks, no debris, no mud, no explosion, no fire, no blood, no cuts, no orbiting camera, no whip pans, no camera dolly forward.\n\n이미지 프롬프트 (연대귀문전)\n\nSeedream Pro 5.0. <<<image_1>>> = a cutout photo of the carved beast figure on the Baekje patterned brick from Oe-ri, Buyeo.\n\nREFERENCE SCOPE\n<<<image_1>>> defines only the creature's face, glaring eyes, fangs, flame-shaped mane, body silhouette, ring belt, hanging strap, curled arms, claws and stance. Do not copy the flat relief, the stone or clay material, the pale beige color, the black background or the cropped edges from <<<image_1>>>. If <<<image_1>>> and this text disagree, the text wins.\n\nTransform the carved figure from <<<image_1>>> into a colossal guardian spirit made of dense black ink smoke, rising at the end of a narrow hanok alley at night, no people. It keeps the exact silhouette of <<<image_1>>>: an enormous wide face set directly on its chest with no neck, huge glaring round eyes, a blunt broad nose, a wide open square mouth with rows of teeth and long sharp fangs, a flame-shaped mane radiating out from both sides of the face, a belt studded with many rings, a long strap hanging down from the center of the belt, arms curving out to both sides and down ending in curled claws, legs bent in a wide stance. Its whole body is thick slowly swirling black smoke like ink dropped in water, darker than the night around it. Only the face, the flame mane, the fangs, the claws and the ring belt are defined, drawn in precise crimson red circuit lines floating inside the smoke, like the carved lines of the brick relief traced in circuitry. The lines are seen through a thin veil of smoke that softens and diffuses their glow, a deep muted crimson with a gentle soft bloom, dimmer than the moon, never neon, never harsh. The edges of its arms, legs and mane dissolve into drifting black smoke that curls away into the mist. Strips of sheer black gauze drift through the smoke, and one extremely long ribbon of crimson red silk, the goreum, come loose and streaming far behind in the wind. Its head is at the height of the roof eaves. A huge full moon behind it at 6500K lights the smoke edges silver, thick low mist on the ground merging with its legs, the warm hanji lanterns at 2700K along both walls dimming near it. Grey stone walls and grey unglazed roof tiles on both sides. Shot on ARRI Alexa 35, 35mm at T2, camera low near the ground looking up, symmetrical frontal composition. No neon, no oversaturated red, no harsh glow, no solid body, no fur, no clay, no stone, no cracks, no lava, no chubby belly, no cartoon, no ghost with a sheet, no grim reaper, no neck, no Japanese oni, no horns, no real fire, no red lanterns, no vermilion, no hologram glitch, no sparkles, no magic particles. muted elegant color grade where the most saturated colors are the glowing circuit lines and the goreum, subtle film grain, soft deep blacks, luxurious high end fashion film look, no horror mood\n\n음악 프롬프트\n\nPsychedelic rock with Korean traditional instruments; breathy female vocal floating far back in the mix, 96 BPM hypnotic swaying pulse, warm analog haze with tape saturation, phaser, long plate reverb and occasional reversed swells; hypnotic repeating gayageum riff, haegeum sustained wavering tones with heavy pitch bending, swelling fuzz guitar, continuous low drone, spacious buk and janggu groove, slowly thickening into a dense swirling wall, ‑EDM drop, ‑orchestral strings, ‑ballad, ‑cheerful major key, ‑long ambient intro",
