      "fullPrompt": "[Midjourney]\nAt the center, a tiny abstract form resembling a lily-of-the-valley bud, made of celadon mist and glazed porcelain fragments, floats delicately. Around it, a smooth backdrop stretches outward, textured only with soft ceramic grain and subtle ink-like ripples, quiet and neutral. Created Using: porcelain surface simulation, celadon glaze diffusion, micro-center focus mapping, RED Helium shallow lens emulation, ink ripple texture overlay, ambient fog lighting, traditional Korean motif dust pass, fine jade shimmer\nAn abstract three-dimensional space where traditional Korean celadon vessels spiral and collide in a vortex of debris and light. The objects float on multiple depth planes, overlapping and breaking apart mid-motion. Deep spatial layering creates an immersive tunnel of shattered pottery and ink waves. Created Using: RED Helium 8K simulation, volumetric space rendering, celadon shard modeling, multi-depth debris pass, kinetic energy shaders, ripple distortion field, ambient particle fog\nA massive vortex composed of overlapping celadon vessels, ornamental shards, and metal threads spinning with brutal centrifugal force. The center explodes with a thunderous shockwave, ink and glaze flying in every direction. The scene vibrates with tension and density. Created Using: macro fluid simulation, impact collision mapping, traditional pattern emboss overlay, volumetric energy lighting, rotating debris pass, ink discharge effect\nA flowing wave abstract structure made of porcelain segments and traditional Korean fan patterns, curving gracefully across the frame. The wave's spine is laced with metallic filigree and jade inlays. Behind it, ink bleeds softly in expanding motion. Pale blue and ivory tones dominate. Created Using: Canon tilt-shift lens emulation, Korean craft pattern mapping, ripple deformation modeling, depth-focused lighting pass, celadon shader layer, floating dust particles, ink diffusion simulation\nabstract ceramic art inspired by Korean traditional pottery, floating in space, central ink diffusion effect like watercolor bloom, celadon textures with subtle inlays, glowing jade and cobalt hues on high-key background, sharp focus, suspended patterns of metalcraft and jewelry, cinematic still, symmetry and softness combined\nAn abstract, immersive photograph of floating Korean craft elements--glazed pottery shards, etched metal filaments, and suspended patterns from norigae and traditional jewelry. Central ink bloom effect, soft expansion and contraction around the center. Colors: ivory white, powder blue, jade-like green. Deep focus on ornament textures. Created Using: RED Komodo 6K sensor, traditional Korean design motifs, celadon inlay textures, 3D ink dispersion simulation, fixed-frame cinematic staging, layered ornament repetition, ambient diffusion lighting\nA massive vortex composed of overlapping celadon vessels, ornamental shards, and metal threads spinning with brutal centrifugal force. The center explodes with a thunderous shockwave, ink and glaze flying in every direction. The scene vibrates with tension and density. Created Using: macro fluid simulation, impact collision mapping, traditional pattern emboss overlay, volumetric energy lighting, rotating debris pass, ink discharge effect\nA flowing wave abstract structure made of porcelain segments and traditional Korean fan patterns, curving gracefully across the frame. The wave's spine is laced with metallic filigree and jade inlays. Behind it, ink bleeds softly in expanding motion. Pale blue and ivory tones dominate. Created Using: Canon tilt-shift lens emulation, Korean craft pattern mapping, ripple deformation modeling, depth-focused lighting pass, celadon shader layer, floating dust particles, ink diffusion simulation\nabstract ceramic art inspired by Korean traditional pottery, floating in space, central ink diffusion effect like watercolor bloom, celadon textures with subtle inlays, glowing jade and cobalt hues on high-key background, sharp focus, suspended patterns of metalcraft and jewelry, cinematic still, symmetry and softness combined\n\n[Kling ai]\nThe camera plunges faster into the porcelain abyss, as massive ceramic streams twist violently around like braided storms. Explosive swirling motion fills the frame, with shimmering bubbles scattering in weightless suspension, amplifying cosmic depth and immense dynamic flow.\nThe camera moves closer as layered porcelain flowers unfold, merging into a vast field of complex organic shapes. Petals ripple outward in fluid motion, twisting and intertwining, creating an infinite expansion of abstract ceramic patterns and immense spatial depth.\nClockwise spinning tunnel pulls the viewer inward. As the motion accelerates, a sleek ceramic door opens in one smooth motion, revealing a fantastical mirrored room with glowing waveforms and digital lights.\nThe sculptural surface begins to lift with soft gusts, pieces floating upward and scattering. Gradually, the motion coalesces into a spiraling storm, rotating clockwise and pulling the viewer inward with forceful grace.\nThe camera drifts slowly inward as porcelain forms flutter gently like petals underwater. Organic shapes ripple and sway in fluid motion, filling the frame with a serene yet alive sensation, evoking a dreamlike descent into a soft, undulating abstract space.\nPorcelain-like organic folds pulse rhythmically, curling and unfurling as if breathing. The camera glides smoothly between the structures, rotating gently to highlight their layered depth. Subtle lighting enhances the glossy textures as patterns flow, evoking an intricate living sculpture.\nA porcelain-like deep blue fractal vortex, fine cracks spreading across its glossy surface, shards breaking away in slow motion, revealing an explosion of glass and digital particles in a black void, cinematic lighting\nThe ceramic tunnel begins to rotate clockwise as the camera moves steadily inward. As the spinning intensifies, a circular door opens smoothly, revealing a vast luminous hall with glowing patterns and mirrored reflections.\n하나의 중단 없는 시네마틱 원테이크 장면.첫 번째 이미지의 극단적인 클로즈업에서 시작하여 두 번째 이미지의 구도로 정확하게 이어진다. 향로 자체는 완전히 정지해 있으며 회전하거나 움직이지 않는다. 카메라만 동일한 높이와 각도를 유지한 채 매우 천천히 뒤로 이동한다.카메라는 투각 뚜껑의 세부 문양에서 시작해 일정한 속도로 뒤로 물러난다. 카메라가 멀어지면서 둥근 투각 뚜껑의 전체 곡면과 국화꽃 봉오리 형태의 몸체가 순차적으로 드러난다. 카메라는 뒤로 이동하면서 시계 방향으로 5~10도 정도만 아주 미세하게 움직인다. 큰 공전이나 360도 회전은 하지 않는다.향로의 형태와 세부 구조는 시작부터 끝까지 동일하게 유지한다. 투각 구멍의 모양과 위치, 꽃잎의 수와 배열, 몸체의 비례, 유약의 색과 표면을 절대 변형하지 않는다. 새로운 구멍이나 꽃잎이 생기지 않고 기존 장식이 녹거나 움직이지 않는다.왼쪽 위에서 들어오는 좁고 부드러운 빛은 그대로 유지한다. 카메라 이동에 따라 회청색 유약의 표면을 흐르는 반사광만 매우 미세하게 달라진다. 전체 노출과 배경 밝기는 갑자기 변하지 않는다.영상 중반부터 투각 구멍 사이로 아주 얇고 희미한 향 연기가 천천히 올라온다. 연기는 한두 줄만 나타나며 향로를 가리거나 크게 퍼지지 않는다. 배경은 끝까지 검은색으로 유지한다.카메라는 마지막 1초 동안 서서히 감속한 뒤 두 번째 이미지의 구도에서 거의 완전히 정지한다. 마지막에는 향로와 카메라가 모두 정지하고, 얇은 연기와 유약 위의 작은 반사광만 미세하게 움직인다.느리고 절제된 카메라 후퇴, 사실적인 고려청자 유약, 고요하고 엄숙한 미디어아트 엔딩, 16:9.향로 자체의 회전, 360도 회전, 형태 변형, 투각 문양 변화, 꽃잎 움직임, 새로운 장식, 급격한 줌, 카메라 흔들림, 강한 연기, 물결, 물보라, 제품 광고식 회전과 장면 전환은 없다.\nUse the provided image as the exact first frame. Create one continuous five-second macro shot with no cuts. For the first 0.7 seconds, preserve the original composition with only an extremely subtle forward drift. Then the camera slowly dollies forward, precisely following the existing dark inner opening located slightly below and to the right of the frame center. The movement gradually accelerates only a little, creating a calm and restrained inward pull.The glazed ceramic rim and surrounding body remain completely solid, rigid and unchanged. Blue-white reflections and existing speckled highlights gently slide along the curved glaze and converge naturally into the opening. The suction is expressed only through the camera movement and the inward flow of reflected light, never through deformation. As the lens passes across the rim, the dark opening gradually fills the entire frame. The blue reflected light fades into deep navy and then true black. Hold a completely black, motionless frame for the final 0.7 seconds. Smooth slow movement, calm atmosphere, realistic depth, one continuous take.\n\n[Suno ai]\nKorean Gayageum K-Drum Music Using Korean Traditional Instruments 120bpm\n\n[bbanana ai]\nA five-second close-miked organic ceramic texture: thin moist clay petals slowly unfolding and gently sliding across one another, soft glazed friction with delicate natural resonance. Very quiet and restrained. No cracking, breaking, scraping, music, rhythm or magical sparkle.\nA four-second sound effect: one clear water droplet falling into a deep glazed ceramic vessel, dark hollow resonance, long natural decay, silence after the single drop, no additional droplets\nA seven-second sound effect: one gentle low resonance from a thick celadon ceramic bowl, warm hollow tone, subtle uneven overtones, very long natural decay, no melody, no additional strikes\nAn eight-second sound effect: one low pure electronic sine resonance slowly fading in and out, soft granular edge, extremely quiet and restrained, no melody, no chord, no pulse\nA two-and-a-half-second soft reverse suction made from water shimmer and ceramic resonance, gently contracting inward into complete silence, subtle, calm, no impact or boom",
