      "fullPrompt": "씬1. Cinematic aerial drone shot of a traditional Korean Buddhist \ntemple surrounded by dense mountain forest in clear winter \nmorning light. The temple architecture remains completely \nunchanged and historically authentic, matching the reference\nimage precisely. The camera is mounted on a stabilized \nprofessional cinema drone, moving extremely slowly and \nsmoothly, with only a very subtle, gentle orbital movement \naround the \ntemple, almost imperceptible. The movement should feel like \na perfectly controlled cinematic rail shot, not handheld, not \nshaky, not FPV, and not an aggressive drone orbit. The \ncamera maintains a stable altitude, stable horizon, and \nconsistent distance from the temple throughout the shot.\nA gentle natural breeze moves through the surrounding trees. \nTree branches and leaves sway softly and naturally in the wind, \nwith subtle variations between different trees. The temple itself \nremains completely still and solid.\nClear, crisp winter atmosphere, cool transparent air, soft golden \nmorning sunlight falling naturally across the temple rooftops and \nsurrounding forest. Subtle atmospheric depth, realistic sunlight \nand shadows, delicate highlights on the roof tiles, natural \ncontrast,photorealistic textures.\nSlow cinematic pacing, restrained camera movement, realistic \ndrone physics, smooth parallax, natural depth, professional \ncinemato graphy, \nphotorealistic, extremely realistic live-action footage, high-end \nfeature \nfilm cinematography, 4K cinematic detail.\n\n씬2. A cinematic, photorealistic live-action shot of the same Korean female high school student from the reference image, walking naturally along the stone wall.\nShe walks at a calm, unhurried pace. She does not suddenly stop. Instead, as if something unseen and deeply familiar is quietly drawing her attention, her walking gradually slows down, her steps become smaller, and she comes to a gentle, almost unconscious stop. After stopping, she slowly turns her body toward the stone wall on the left side of the frame, then quietly looks at the wall in silence. Her movement feels instinctive and emotionally subtle, as though she has been drawn toward the wall without consciously deciding to go there.\nHer expression remains quiet and contemplative, with a faint, natural sense of wonder. No exaggerated acting. No sudden reaction. The turn is slow, restrained, and believable.\nThe camera continuously tracks the girl throughout the entire movement, smoothly following her walking path and maintaining the exact same framing, camera distance, and scale. The girl must occupy the same percentage of the frame from beginning to end. No zoom in, no zoom out, no change in focal length, no camera push-in, no reframing, and no change in subject size. The camera simply glides laterally/backward with her at the same pace, like a professional dolly or stabilized tracking shot.\nWhen she stops, the camera also smoothly settles into position without any sudden movement. The stone wall remains on the left side of the frame, and she turns toward it. Maintain natural spatial continuity and consistent perspective throughout.\nWarm cinematic natural light, realistic outdoor atmosphere.\n\n씬3. The same Korean female high school student stands beside the old stone wall, maintaining a careful, serious, contemplative expression and focused eyes. She remains almost completely still for a moment, quietly looking at the stone wall.\nThen, very slowly and deliberately, she raises her right hand toward the wall. Her movement is cautious and restrained, as if she is approaching something meaningful and unfamiliar. Her fingers extend naturally, and she gently places her right palm and fingertips against the rough stone surface, making soft, deliberate contact. The hand movement must be continuous, slow, subtle, and physically natural.\nHer eyes remain focused on the stone wall throughout the movement. No sudden gestures, no dramatic reaction, no exaggerated emotion. Her face and body language convey quiet curiosity, caution, and a sense of being drawn toward the wall.\nThe camera performs an extremely slow, almost imperceptible micro-orbit around her, moving only a few centimeters over the entire shot. The camera is virtually stationary, with only a subtle change in perspective and parallax. No noticeable camera movement. It should feel like a locked-off cinematic shot with an almost invisible orbital drift.\nThe girl remains sharply in focus. Natural shallow depth of field, realistic skin texture, authentic school uniform fabric, detailed weathered stone wall, subtle natural breeze moving a few loose strands of hair and nearby foliage.\nPhotorealistic live-action footage, cinematic cinematography, restrained performance, natural human motion, physically accurate hand movement, realistic lighting, subtle film grain, high-end cinema camera quality.\nNo handheld movement, no camera shake, no sudden orbit.\n\n씬4. The girl remains completely still, with her hand gently resting against the stone wall. Her hand, fingers, arm, body, and position must remain perfectly stationary throughout the entire shot.\n\nThe transformation happens only in the stone wall and the surrounding environment. The weathered, dirty, aged stones gradually transform as if **time itself is flowing backward**. Over a seamless cinematic time-lapse, years of accumulated dirt, moss, stains, discoloration, and weathering gradually disappear. The rough, dark, neglected stones slowly become cleaner, brighter, and more pristine, revealing fresh natural stone beneath the aged surface.\n\nThe transformation must feel like the passage of time reversing rather than the wall being digitally washed or instantly replaced. Dirt subtly fades, moss recedes, stains disappear, surface textures become cleaner, and the stones gradually return to a naturally clean, well-maintained appearance. The individual stones, their shapes, positions, cracks, and overall structure remain exactly the same throughout the transformation.\n\nThe girl remains completely motionless and sharply in focus while the stone wall undergoes the dramatic time-lapse transformation around her. Her hand never moves and never changes position, maintaining continuous physical contact with exactly the same stone.\n\nThe camera is almost completely locked off, with only an extremely subtle cinematic micro-orbit, barely perceptible. No zoom, no push-in, no pull-out, no reframing, and no change in composition.\n\n\n이하 스크린샷에 표기해놨습니다. 답변의 내용이 너무 크다고 프롬프트 전문이 추가되지 않아서 이 정도까지만 기재하겠습니다.",
