      "fullPrompt": "1. \nCommon Prompt – Style Cinematic live-action historical trailer, ultra-realistic Korean landscape and architecture, high production value, natural golden-hour lighting, realistic textures, grounded epic atmosphere. The camera behaves like an invisible floating observer, not a high drone. It glides smoothly through space, skims close to walls, passes near leaves and terrain, descends naturally, accelerates with believable inertia, and creates strong foreground parallax. The visual storytelling must feel seamless and immersive, with no captions, no subtitles, no narration, and no on-screen text. Use subtle cinematic VFX only to enhance speed and transition: natural motion blur, slight atmospheric shimmer, dust and pollen particles, foreground wipe transitions, and mild environmental morphing hidden behind occlusion. Maintain a realistic live-action film look in 16:9 widescreen. Negative Prompt No fantasy architecture, no Chinese palace architecture, no Joseon palace style in Baekje-period scenes, no modern clothing in historical scenes, no modern vehicles, no modern signs, no skyscrapers, no neon lights, no sci-fi portal, no magical glow, no obvious time-travel vortex, no video game HUD, no excessive lens flare, no overdone camera shake, no deformed anatomy, no duplicated people, no floating objects, no text, no subtitles, no logos, no watermark. Scene Prompt [0.0–2.0 seconds] Begin with a present-day view of Gongsanseong Fortress, closely based on the provided reference images. The camera starts from a low floating viewpoint outside the fortress, only slightly higher than human eye level, not from a high aerial drone perspective. Show the present-day stone fortress wall, the gate pavilion, the surrounding green hillside, and the distant Geumgang River. The atmosphere is calm and quiet, with warm late-afternoon golden sunlight. The camera glides smoothly forward toward the fortress gate at a calm, elegant speed. [2.0–4.5 seconds] The camera continues moving forward and slightly curves along the side of the stone wall rather than entering directly through the gate. It passes close to grass, shrubs, and the sloped terrain, creating strong foreground parallax. The present-day stone wall remains clearly visible. The mood stays peaceful and realistic. Subtle wind moves leaves and vegetation. No distracting people are necessary. [4.5–5.4 seconds] As the camera gets very close to the fortress wall, increase the movement speed slightly. Introduce only a faint atmospheric shimmer and tiny dust or pollen particles in the sunlight. Nearby leaves, branches, and the edge of the stone wall sweep quickly across the lens and cover most of the frame. Maintain forward momentum. This is the transition moment. While the frame is heavily occluded, transform the environment from present-day Gongsanseong into Baekje-period Ungjin Fortress in 475 CE. The transition must feel natural and cinematic, not magical. [5.4–7.8 seconds] As the foreground clears, reveal the same location in the past. The modern stone wall has now become a compacted earthen rampart. The terrain and overall layout remain recognizable as the same place, but the wall is made of dense brown earth, slightly weathered, with grass along the upper edge. The camera immediately accelerates and glides very close along the side of the earthen wall. Use a stronger sense of speed than in the first half. [7.8–10.0 seconds] The camera continues racing beside the earthen rampart and gradually descends toward the fortress entrance. Wooden poles, banners, branches, grass, and the earthen wall pass very close to the lens, creating intense foreground parallax. The air contains more dust and warmer earth-toned atmosphere than before. Do not use fantasy effects. [10.0–12.0 seconds] As the camera nears the entrance, reveal Baekje soldiers and displaced civilians moving urgently toward and through the gate. Use the provided Baekje costume references for soldiers and commoners. The fortress feels tense and newly occupied rather than fully prosperous. The camera keeps moving forward and slightly downward toward the gate, preparing naturally for the next shot. End close to the gate with the camera still moving.\n\n2.\n1. Common Prompt : Cinematic live-action historical trailer, ultra-realistic Baekje-period Korea, high production value, natural golden-hour lighting, realistic fabrics, architecture, skin, dust, and environmental textures. The camera behaves like an invisible floating observer moving freely through the historical environment. It is not a conventional drone and does not remain high above the scene. The camera can move at head height, skim past people, travel beside carts and soldiers, pass through narrow gaps in crowds, slightly rise or descend, and accelerate with physically believable momentum. Maintain continuous forward motion throughout the entire shot. Create strong foreground and midground parallax using people, carts, cloth banners, wooden structures, merchandise, and vegetation passing close to the lens. The sequence should feel fast, immersive, and cinematic, but the movement must remain smooth and physically believable. Use the provided Baekje soldier and commoner costume reference images consistently for all visible characters. 16:9 cinematic widescreen, realistic live-action film aesthetic, no captions, no subtitles, no narration, no on-screen text. 2. Negative Prompt : No Joseon-era hanbok, no Joseon palace architecture, no Chinese imperial architecture, no Japanese samurai clothing, no fantasy armor, no excessive gold armor on ordinary soldiers, no modern objects, no modern roads, no modern signs, no plastic, no modern carts, no modern hairstyles, no modern makeup, no neon colors, no fantasy portal, no supernatural energy, no video game HUD, no excessive slow motion, no static camera, no aerial drone-only perspective, no duplicated people, no cloned faces, no warped bodies, no deformed hands, no floating characters, no unnatural crowd movement, no text, no subtitles, no logos, no watermark. 3. Scene Prompt : [0.0–2.0 seconds] Begin exactly from the first frame image Baekje soldiers stand on both sides of the earthen gate while displaced civilians carrying bundles, baskets, sacks, and simple wooden carts move urgently toward the entrance. The camera immediately continues forward at moderate speed. Move just above shoulder height behind the civilians, close enough for people and carried belongings to pass near the lens and create strong foreground parallax. Do not stop or reset the camera. [2.0–4.3 seconds] Accelerate slightly and move deeper into the crowd. The camera smoothly slips between civilians, a wooden cart, and Baekje soldiers guarding the entrance. A soldier holding a spear briefly passes very close on one side of the lens while a civilian carrying a large cloth bundle passes close on the opposite side. Keep all movements natural and physically believable. Dust rises softly from footsteps and cart wheels. The crowd should feel tense and exhausted rather than chaotic or panicked. The camera approaches the gate opening directly. [4.3–6.0 seconds] Pass underneath the wooden fortress gate without cutting. As the camera enters the darker gate passage, briefly allow the wooden beams and shadowed interior to fill most of the frame. Increase the feeling of speed through stronger foreground motion blur and compressed parallax. For approximately half a second, the environment becomes darker as the camera travels through the gate tunnel. Then rapidly emerge into warm sunlight inside Ungjin Fortress. This transition marks the movement from the tense arrival outside the fortress into the newly forming capital inside. [6.0–8.0 seconds] Immediately reveal a much more active interior settlement. Continue moving forward at approximately human head height through a busy Baekje street. Ordinary men and women based on the provided commoner costume references walk in both directions. Cra