      "promptSummary": "",
      "fullPrompt": "사용한 프롬프트가 길고 많기 때문에, 전체 내용은 이미지 파일로 첨부하고 텍스트는 주요 장면 프롬프트 세가지를 작성하겠습니다.\n\n- 연꽃무늬 수막새 영상 연출 프롬프트: A high-end cinematic product film featuring a Baekje-era lotus-pattern roof-end tile (수막새), treated as a precious heritage object rather than an archaeological artifact.\n\nThe circular roof-end tile rests in a refined, minimal dark architectural space. Its aged ceramic surface, subtle mineral texture, hand-crafted irregularities, and deeply carved lotus petals are preserved with absolute material authenticity.\n\nA narrow, highly controlled beam of soft warm-white light slowly travels across the surface of the roof-end tile. The light reveals the relief progressively from darkness to illumination, emphasizing the dimensional carving, fine surface grain, softened edges, and restrained traces of age.\n\nThe camera performs an extremely slow, precise macro dolly-in combined with a subtle lateral orbital movement around the circular surface. Shallow depth of field gradually transitions across the lotus petals, creating the visual language of a luxury jewelry or premium material commercial.\n\nAs the light reaches the center of the lotus motif, delicate reflected highlights travel naturally along the carved contours. The illumination feels physically motivated by the surface geometry, never artificially glowing.\n\nAt the peak, the entire lotus pattern becomes clearly visible in a controlled sculptural composition. The camera continues moving closer until the carved lotus lines occupy the frame.\n\nThe final movement follows one elegant lotus-petal contour into extreme macro detail, allowing the carved line, shadow, and highlight to visually continue beyond the physical object and dissolve naturally into the next abstract graphic sequence.\n\nPremium Korean heritage art direction, contemporary luxury product cinematography, museum-grade material fidelity, sculptural lighting, restrained elegance, sophisticated negative space, tactile ceramic surface, precise optical rendering, subtle cinematic contrast, quiet visual tension.\n\nNO object morphing, NO deformation of the roof-end tile, NO changing lotus pattern, NO fantasy ornamentation, NO excessive glow, NO floating particles, NO sparks, NO neon light, NO gold glitter, NO artificial magical effects, NO camera shake, NO fisheye distortion, NO excessive depth of field, NO added objects, NO modern typography, NO text, NO people.\n\n- 그래픽 이팩트 추가 영상 프롬프트: Preserve the original video composition, camera movement, subjects, architecture, timing, and duration.\nApply a continuous Electro Biomorph effect directly onto the existing footage. Do not replace or regenerate the scene. The original drone movement remains completely unchanged. Add the effect onto the original footage while preserving the visual structure and motion.\n\nEFFECT BEHAVIOR & SUBJECT TRACKING:\nThe Electro Biomorph effect is one continuous living energy system running through the entire film. It dynamically traces and flows along the natural contours, structural lines, surface textures, architectural edges, and key subject details visible in each shot (such as roof ridges, decorative patterns, wood grain, stone surfaces, or primary silhouettes where present). The effect combines subtle electrical energy with biomorphic movement, looking as though the hidden cultural or innate energy stored within the subjects and environment has awakened and is traveling through the space.\n\nCOLOR PALETTE & VISUAL TEXTURE SPECIFICATION:\nPrimary Structure: Dual-layer organic bioluminescent energy.\nOuter Rims & Silhouette: Translucent Cyan, Mint, and Emerald bioluminescent glow, softly tracing the outer contours, structural silhouettes, and primary edges of visible subjects or architecture.\nInner Core & Lines: Glowing deep red, Warm Coral, and radiant Orange fluid energy lines flowing inside surface textures, interior details, intricate patterns, and structural cavities.\nVisual Materiality: Translucent bioluminescent structure with soft inner luminescence.\nDo NOT use standard high-voltage blue lightning or harsh synthetic neon graphics. The effect must look like living bioluminescent light structures and pulsating energy pathways, perfectly integrated with the physical environment and subjects.\n\nSHOT CONTINUITY & OVERALL MOTION LANGUAGE:\nWhen a shot changes, the same Electro Biomorph energy must continue from the previous shot into the next shot, maintaining the exact same direction and momentum. It may temporarily disappear behind subjects or architecture and re-emerge naturally in the next shot, but it must never restart as a new effect.\n- Continuous drone flight and spatial progression.\n- Continuous rotational momentum and visual energy.\nEvery cut must feel like the camera is still flying through the same physical world. Elegant, dynamic, immersive, cinematic film with photorealistic visuals, strong sense of spatial depth, parallax, momentum and discovery.\n\nNEGATIVE PROMPT:\n(static camera, camera reset, camera repositioning, stopped drone, sudden change of direction, reverse movement, teleportation, jump cut in camera position, abrupt altitude change, disconnected shots, slideshow feeling, floating camera, inconsistent motion, random camera movement, camera shake, chaotic movement, generic neon overlay, disconnected VFX, restarting energy effect, duplicated energy effect, effect appearing from nowhere, subject distortion, architecture distortion, warped structures, changing environment structure, high voltage blue lightning, harsh synthetic neon.)\n\n사운드: Create a sophisticated 30-second cinematic art-film score for a high-end Korean heritage media artwork.\n\nThe music should feel contemporary, refined, atmospheric, and timeless — not traditional Korean music, not commercial pop, and not epic trailer music.\n\nBegin with an almost silent, spacious atmosphere. A single delicate tonal texture slowly emerges, evoking the feeling of an ancient ceramic surface being revealed by light.\n\n0–7 seconds:\nVery sparse and restrained. Deep atmospheric drone, subtle resonant texture, one or two isolated bell-like overtones. Large sense of space and silence. No obvious rhythm.\n\n7–15 seconds:\nIntroduce a slow, organic pulse. Add delicate shimmering high-frequency textures that move gradually like light traveling across carved lotus petals and traditional patterns. The rhythm remains minimal and fluid, with no obvious drum beat.\n\n15–23 seconds:\nThe sound gradually becomes more active and dimensional. Layer several flowing tonal lines that gently separate, intersect, and expand. Use subtle granular and spectral textures to suggest organic light flow and the transformation of traditional patterns into contemporary digital forms.\n\n23–27 seconds:\nReach a controlled emotional peak. Add a wider harmonic layer and a restrained low-frequency pulse. The music should feel expansive and luminous rather than dramatic or heroic.\n\n27–30 seconds:\nAbruptly reduce the density. Let the final sustained tone and delicate high-frequency resonance remain in the air, creating a sense of continuation beyond the end of the film.\n\nSound palette:\ndeep warm ambient drone, soft ceramic resonance, delicate metallic overtones, subtle glass-like harmonics, organic granular textures, restrained electronic pulse, spacious reverb, fine high-frequency shimmer.\n\nMusical character:\nminimalist, elegant, contemplative, mysterious, tactile, architectural, cinematic, premium, contemporary Korean art direction.\n\nThe music should feel like light discovering the hidden grain of an ancient object and gradually transforming that grain into a living contemporary visual language.\n\nNO traditional Korean melody, NO obvious gugak instruments, NO traditional percussion, NO taiko, NO cinematic trailer drums, NO heroic orchestra, NO sentimental piano, NO pop melody, NO vocals, NO choir, NO excessive bass, NO EDM drop, NO dramatic climax.",
